Some of the firm's notable (past) employees include former Austrian chancellor [[Sebastian Kurz]], American politician and entrepreneur [[Blake Masters]], [[Kevin Harrington (national security advisor)|Kevin Harrington]] (Senior Director for Strategic Planning at the [[United States National Security Council]]) and [[Michael Kratsios]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Who's Who on Trump's National Security Council? |url=https://instituteforglobalaffairs.org/2025/05/mapping-the-trump-47-administration-nsc-key-figures-and-leaders/ |website=IGA |date=23 May 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Skelton |first1=Charlie |title=China haunts Bilderberg talks as usual suspects plot world domination |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jun/15/bilderberg-hroup |access-date=30 July 2025 |work=The Guardian |date=15 June 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Blake Masters' Views on Gay Marriage May Surprise His Political Master Peter Thiel |url=https://www.yahoo.com/news/blake-masters-views-gay-marriage-081805807.html |access-date=30 July 2025 |work=Yahoo News |date=27 June 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Peter Thiel - Der neue Chef von Sebastian Kurz |url=https://oe1.orf.at/artikel/690803/Peter-Thiel-Der-neue-Chef-von-Sebastian-Kurz |access-date=30 July 2025 |work=oe1.orf.at |date=21 February 2022 |language=de}}</ref>

====Quantum-Systems and Stark====
Thiel Capital's investment in the Gilching-based drone startup [[Quantum-Systems]] as well as Thiel's subsequent backing of the Berlin-based attack drone startup [[STARK|Stark]] are sometimes considered controversial, due to Thiel's politics.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Voss |first1=Markus |title=Rätselhafte Website: Das ist Deutschlands geheimstes Rüstungs-Startup mit Schatten-Investor Peter Thiel |url=https://www.focus.de/finanzen/news/schatten-investor-peter-thiel-das-ist-deutschlands-geheimstes-ruestungs-startup_6a6b0667-f910-4f3b-bd87-f1f998fa1bae.html |access-date=31 July 2025 |date=27 March 2025 |language=de-DE}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Pinster |first1=Jesse |title=U.S. gets sneak peek at Europe's military tech through CIA-backed fund |url=https://www.ftm.eu/articles/cia-invests-in-european-defence-startups |website=Follow the Money - Platform for investigative journalism |date=8 July 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Gurkov |first1=Andrey |title=Drones for Ukraine, made in Germany – DW – 02/01/2023 |url=https://www.dw.com/en/drones-for-ukraine-made-in-germany/a-64570826 |access-date=31 July 2025 |work=dw.com |date=2 January 2023 |language=en}}</ref> In May 2025, Quantum-Systems became Europe's first dual-use unicorn and third defense unicorn, after fellow Bavarian startup Helsing and the Portuguese Tekever (Thiel has a role in the success of Helsing too and the startup is considered a part of the "Thiel ecosystem", although he does not directly invest in it).<ref>{{cite news |title=German dual-use unicorn Quantum-Systems secures €160M Series C round |url=https://en.ain.ua/2025/05/06/quantum-systems-secures-eur160m-series-c/ |access-date=31 July 2025 |work=en.ain.ua |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=sifted Reports H1 2025 review A braver, bolder Europe emerges |url=https://www.datocms-assets.com/60124/1753103774-h1-2025-report.pdf |website=datocms-assets |publisher=sifted |access-date=31 July 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Amelin |first1=Anatoliy |title=Bilderberg Club 2025 and evolution of Ukrainian topic |url=https://global.espreso.tv/world-news-bilderberg-club-evolution-of-ukrainian-topic |access-date=31 July 2025 |work=global.espreso.tv |date=7 July 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Dromberg |first1=Jonas |title=Why Sweden has the necessary tools to lead new Nordic defense drive |url=https://www.arctictoday.com/why-sweden-has-the-necessary-tools-to-lead-nordic-new-defence-drive/ |access-date=31 July 2025 |work=ArcticToday |date=2 April 2025}}</ref> Thiel's mentee Moritz Döpfner brokered the deal with Quantum-Systems on Thiel's behalf and sits on its board. His venture fund Doepfner Capital also invests in Stark.<ref>{{cite news |title=Stark Valued at $500M after $62M in Fresh Funding Led by Sequoia Capital – UAS VISION |url=https://www.uasvision.com/2025/08/26/stark-valued-at-500m-after-62m-in-fresh-funding-led-by-sequoia-capital/ |access-date=5 September 2025 |date=26 August 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Holzki |first1=Larissa |title=Dubiose Geheimnistuerei um das Waffen-Start-up Stark |url=https://www.handelsblatt.com/technik/ki/waffen-und-munition-dubiose-geheimnistuerei-um-das-waffen-start-up-stark-03/100137508.html |work=handelsblatt.com |date=11 July 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Schlenk|first1=Caspar|last2=Rest|first2=Jonas|title=Kamikazedrohnen-Hersteller Stark: Peter Thiel steckt Millionen in deutsches Start-up |url=https://www.manager-magazin.de/unternehmen/tech/killer-drohnen-hersteller-stark-peter-thiel-steckt-millionen-in-deutsches-start-up-a-18517db7-c173-40ba-b6ff-50a654fe3593 |work=manager-magazin.de |date=3 April 2025 |language=de}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Rest |first1=Jonas |title=Peter Thiel: 50 Millionen Dollar für den Risikokapitalfonds von Mathias Döpfners Sohn |url=https://www.manager-magazin.de/unternehmen/tech/peter-thiel-50-millionen-dollar-fuer-den-risikokapitalfonds-von-mathias-doepfners-sohn-a-238af84f-d3bf-49e6-b99f-95568a215b95?ref=thenerdreich.com |work=manager-magazin.de |date=22 February 2025 |language=de}}</ref>

=== Mithril Capital ===
In June 2012, he launched [[Mithril Capital Management]], named after [[Mithril|the fictitious metal]] in ''[[The Lord of the Rings]]'', with [[Jim O'Neill (investor)|Jim O'Neill]] and Ajay Royan. Unlike Clarium Capital, Mithril Capital, a fund with $402 million at the time of launch, targets companies that are beyond the startup stage and ready to scale up.<ref name=latimes-mithril>{{cite news|url=https://www.latimes.com/business/money/la-fi-mo-peter-thiel-mithril-20120620,0,7460860.story|title=Facebook investor Peter Thiel opens Mithril venture capital fund|date=20 June 2012|newspaper=[[Los Angeles Times]]|first=Tiffany|last=Hsu|access-date=20 February 2020|archive-date=6 November 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131106235728/http://www.latimes.com/business/money/la-fi-mo-peter-thiel-mithril-20120620,0,7460860.story|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=techcrunch-mithril>{{cite news|url = https://techcrunch.com/2012/06/19/peter-thiel-mithril/|title = Peter Thiel Launches Mithril: A New $402 Million Late-Stage Fund|last = Cutler|first = Kim-Mai|work = [[TechCrunch]]|date = 19 June 2012|access-date = 14 December 2012|archive-date = 18 December 2012|archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20121218063343/http://techcrunch.com/2012/06/19/peter-thiel-mithril/|url-status = live}}</ref>

Thiel holds shares in the space-based intelligence company [[Spaceflight Industries#BlackSky|BlackSky]] through Mithril.<ref>{{cite news |title=Expanding the possibilities of space-based intelligence |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/creativegroup/blacksky/expanding-the-possibilities-of-space-based-intelligence/ |access-date=10 August 2025 |newspaper=Washington Post |date=11 April 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=United States Securities and Exchange Commission – Washington, D.C. 20549 – Schedule 14A |url=https://ir.blacksky.com/sec-filings/all-sec-filings/content/0001753539-24-000080/blacksky-preliminaryproxys.htm |website=ir.blacksky.com |access-date=10 August 2025}}</ref> It also invests in [[Helion Energy]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Nellis |first1=Stephen |title=Helion raises $425 million from SoftBank's venture arm, hits $5.4 billion valuation |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/helion-raises-425-mln-softbanks-venture-arm-hits-54-bln-valuation-2025-01-28/ |date=28 January 2025 |access-date=10 August 2025}}</ref>

=== 1517 Fund ===
The 1517 Fund was founded in 2015 by Danielle Strachman and Michael Gibson, who were both in the founding team of the Thiel Fellowship. The fund provides cash grants and investments, aiming at extending the support already granted by the Thiel Fellowship. It targets "dropouts, renegade students, and deep tech scientists". Peter Thiel backs the fund.<ref>{{cite news |title=Peter Thiel's 1517 Fund Is Out to Find the Next Mark Zuckerberg |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2016-12-01/thiel-s-1517-fund-is-stalking-the-next-zuckerberg |access-date=17 July 2025 |work=Bloomberg.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=1517 Fund - Backing Dropouts, Students & SciFi Science |url=https://www.1517fund.com/ |website=1517fund.com |access-date=17 July 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=1517 Fund {{!}} Medici Project - $1k Cash Grants |url=https://www.1517fund.com/medici-project |website=1517fund.com |access-date=17 July 2025}}</ref>

Its portfolio companies include [[Luminar Technologies]], [[Loom, Inc.]], [[Atom Computing]] and Durin Mining Technologies among others.<ref>{{cite web |title=1517 Fund investment portfolio {{!}} PitchBook |url=https://pitchbook.com/profiles/investor/123036-85#investments |website=pitchbook.com |access-date=17 July 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=An Entrepreneur's Perspective – Reinventing Early-Stage Venture Investing; Plus Register for Our Upcoming Conference! – Raging Capital |url=https://ragingcapitalventures.com/an-entrepreneurs-perspective-interview-with-michael-gibson/ |access-date=17 July 2025 |date=30 June 2022}}</ref>

=== America's Frontier Fund ===
Thiel is the co-founder of America's Frontier Fund, together with [[Eric Schmidt]]. ''[[The New York Times]]'' writes that, America's Frontier Fund is an organization committed to bring manufacturing back to the US, especially that of semiconductors, and the leaders are determined to carry out this mission whether the state helps them or not.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Livni |first1=Ephrat |title=The Billionaires Behind a Push to Reinvigorate U.S. Chip-Making (Published 2022) |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/09/business/americas-frontier-fund-chip-making.html |date=9 June 2022 |language=en}}</ref> ''[[InfluenceWatch]]'' notes the fund's bipartisan character, with the participation of [[Ashton B. Carter]] and [[H.R. McMaster]] and the fact that the two founders are left and right-of-center respectively. The chief executive is [[Gilman Louie]].<ref>{{cite web |title=America's Frontier Fund |url=https://www.influencewatch.org/non-profit/americas-frontier-fund/ |website=InfluenceWatch |access-date=5 June 2025}}</ref>

In December 2024, it got approval to get funding from the Small Business Investment Company Critical Technology Initiative (SBICCT), which is "a joint effort by the U.S. [[Small Business Administration]] and the [[United States Department of Defense|Department of Defense]]."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Doughty |first1=Nate |title=Arlington VC firm America's Frontier Fund lands up to $175M from feds to invest in defense-focused startups |url=https://www.bizjournals.com/washington/inno/stories/fundings/2024/12/18/americas-frontier-fund-sba-dod-jordan-blashek.html |access-date=8 August 2025 |work=Washington Business Journal}}</ref> In July 2025, it reportedly raised US$315&nbsp;million for its first fund.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Hornstein |first1=Julia |title=National security-focused VC firm America's Frontier Fund is raising $315 million for its debut fund |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/national-security-vc-firm-aims-for-315-million-debut-fundraise-2025-6 |access-date=8 August 2025 |work=Business Insider |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260225100107/https://www.businessinsider.com/national-security-vc-firm-aims-for-315-million-debut-fundraise-2025-6 |archive-date= 2026-02-25}}</ref>

It backs Venus Aerospace, a company develops hypersonic flight using rotating detonation rocket engine (since November 2024) and Foundation Alloy.<ref>{{cite web |title=America's Frontier Fund investment portfolio {{!}} PitchBook |url=https://pitchbook.com/profiles/investor/509242-24 |website=pitchbook.com |access-date=8 August 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Karmactive Team |title=MIT Startup Creates Metals 2x Stronger Without Melting: Foundation Alloy's Solid-State Revolution |url=https://www.karmactive.com/mit-startup-creates-metals-2x-stronger-without-melting-foundation-alloys-solid-state-revolution/ |access-date=8 August 2025 |work=Karmactive |date=5 July 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Hypersonic engine co. Venus Aerospace gets deep-tech investment - InnovationMap |url=https://houston.innovationmap.com/venus-aerospace-americas-frontier-fund-2671042746.html |access-date=8 August 2025 |work=houston.innovationmap.com |date=4 February 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Venus Aerospace's hypersonic flight tech just took a big step |url=https://aerospaceamerica.aiaa.org/venus-aerospaces-hypersonic-flight-tech-just-took-a-big-step/ |access-date=8 August 2025 |work=Aerospace America |date=15 May 2025}}</ref>

The fund is characterized by ''Intelligence Online'' as "China-sceptic".<ref>{{cite news |title=United States: Alexander El-Fakir lands at China-sceptic US tech fund backed by Eric Schmidt and Peter Thiel - 07/06/2023 |url=https://www.intelligenceonline.com/corporate-intelligence/2023/06/07/alexander-el-fakir-lands-at-china-sceptic-us-tech-fund-backed-by-eric-schmidt-and-peter-thiel,109991422-eve |access-date=10 August 2025 |work=Intelligence Online |date=7 June 2023 |language=en}}</ref>

=== Rivada Space Networks ===
Around the early 2020s, the Bavarian startup Kleo-Connect successfully developed a highly advanced satellite technology, which is considered much more suitable for governmental and military use than that of Starlink, which was originally conceived for civilian use only. It was feared the technology would fall into the hand of the PLA through its Chinese investors (who invested in the startup since 2018) though. Thus, the German government banned the sale of the company to China, but 144 lawsuits worldwide deterred investors from helping the company to expand the constellation. The founders decided to bring in the US's "highest conservative circles" (which led to the formation of [[Rivada Space Networks]], which drew its personnel mainly from Kleo-Connect, in 2022), among which [[Karl Rove]] participated as an investor and lobbyist, and former US secretary of state [[Mike Pompeo]] joined the board of the mother company in the US, alongside others like [[Richard Myers]], [[Jeb Bush]], [[James Loy]], [[Charles Guthrie, Baron Guthrie of Craigiebank|Lord Guthrie]] and the Democrat [[Martin O'Malley]]. [[Rivada Networks]]'s chairman [[Declan Ganley]] notes in particular the power of Thiel's name (whose investment in the firm remains undisclosed) in negotiation with investors.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Jahn |first1=Thomas |title=Peter Thiel macht mit deutscher Firma Elon Musk Konkurrenz |url=https://www.handelsblatt.com/technik/it-internet/rivada-space-wie-peter-thiel-elon-musk-konkurrenz-machen-will/100046186.html |access-date=5 June 2025 |work=handelsblatt.com |date=2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250605000000/https://www.handelsblatt.com/technik/it-internet/rivada-space-wie-peter-thiel-elon-musk-konkurrenz-machen-will/100046186.html |archive-date=5 June 2025}} [https://static1.squarespace.com/static/62b194511be03b40825b04e8/t/668d079472f9de363ccbec84/1720518548835/Peter+Thiel+competes+with+Elon+Musk+with+German+company.pdf Alt URL]</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Whyte |first1=Barry |title=Declan Ganley's Rivada reaches for the stars while teetering on a precipice |url=https://www.businesspost.ie/news/declan-ganleys-rivada-reaches-for-the-stars-while-teetering-on-a-precipice/ |access-date=5 June 2025 |date=2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230528054659/https://www.businesspost.ie/news/declan-ganleys-rivada-reaches-for-the-stars-while-teetering-on-a-precipice/#selection-887.2-887.32 |archive-date=2023-05-28 }}</ref> The [[United States Department of Defense]] is also an investor.<ref>{{cite news |title=Rivada Space Networks: 10 Milliarden US-Dollar für Starlink-Konkurrenten in München. |url=https://www.golem.de/sonstiges/zustimmung/auswahl.html?from=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.golem.de%2Fnews%2Frivada-space-networks-starlink-konkurrent-in-muenchen-hat-10-milliarden-2407-186643.html&referer=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2F |access-date=5 June 2025 |work=golem.de}}</ref> [[Newt Gingrich]] is noted to have lobbied for the firm too.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Gregg |first1=Aaron |title=Defense officials lukewarm on 5G spectrum-leasing plan pushed by the White House |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2020/11/25/rivada-pentagon-5g-leasing/ |access-date=5 June 2025 |newspaper=The Washington Post |date=25 November 2020}}</ref> By 2025, the "politically connected company" has already expanded to 33 countries and collected 16 billion dollars in investments, despite having not launched its satellites (deployment is set to begin in 2027 with initial tests set for 2026).<ref>{{cite news |title=Rivada Expands Outernet Access to 33 Countries, Secures $16 Billion+ in Global Business |url=https://www.morningstar.com/news/pr-newswire/20250428la74500/rivada-expands-outernet-access-to-33-countries-secures-16-billion-in-global-business |work=Morningstar, Inc. |date=28 April 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Harding McGill |first1=Margaret |title=Trump campaign downplays split with White House on 5G |url=https://www.politico.com/story/2019/03/03/trump-administration-5g-1232622 |access-date=5 June 2025 |work=Politico}}</ref> Thiel reportedly works to help the company's development, especially regarding its legal battles.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Titcomb |first1=James |title=Peter Thiel-backed satellite company plans to challenge Elon Musk in UK market |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/business/2023/10/25/peter-thiel-satellite-uk-licence-challenge-elon-musk/ |access-date=5 June 2025 |work=The Telegraph |date=25 October 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Starinvestor Peter Thiel startet mit Rivada Space Networks Angriff auf SpaceX |url=https://www.focus.de/finanzen/boerse/konkurrenz-fuer-elon-musk-starinvestor-peter-thiel-startet-mit-rivada-space-networks-angriff-auf-spacex_id_260101004.html |date=2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Atkinson |first1=Claire |title=Peter Thiel caught up in $7B lawsuit over Mexican wireless contract |url=https://nypost.com/2017/01/21/peter-thiel-caught-up-in-7b-lawsuit-over-mexican-wireless-contract/ |date=21 January 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Klein |first1=Charlotte |title=Trump Reportedly Pushing Through 5G Deal That Would Enrich His Friends |url=https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2020/10/trump-pentagon-5g-deal-karl-rove-peter-thiel |magazine=Vanity Fair |date=21 October 2020}}</ref>

=== SNÖ Ventures ===
Thiel is an investor and strategic partner of the Oslo-based SNÖ Ventures, having joined the firm in 2021, accompanied by a group of international strategic advisors.<ref>{{cite news |title=SNÖ Ventures launch new $100m Nordic venture fund backed by Peter Thiel - Nordic Startup News |url=https://nordicstartupnews.com/sno-ventures-launch-new-100m-nordic-venture-fund-backed-by-peter-thiel/ |access-date=24 June 2025 |date=25 June 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Oslo-based SNÖ Ventures launches Peter Thiel-backed $100 million fund, expands organisation into Sweden and Denmark |url=https://tech.eu/2021/06/15/oslo-based-sno-ventures-launches-peter-thiel-backed-100-million-fund-expands-organisation-into-sweden-and-denmark/ |work=Tech.eu |date=15 June 2021}}</ref> In 2024, the fund made its first investment in the defense tech sector, an early funding for the Swedish startup Nordic Air Defence, which developed counter-drone missile technology and is staffed with former employees from Palantir and Quantum Systems.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Escárzaga |first1=Antonio L. |title=Stockholm-based Nordic Air Defence secures €1.2 million to advance their drone defence solutions |url=https://www.eu-startups.com/2024/11/stockholm-based-nordic-air-defence-secures-e1-2-million-to-advance-their-drone-defence-solutions/ |access-date=24 June 2025 |work=EU-Startups |date=12 November 2024}}</ref> ''Arctic Today'' sees this as an evidence of Sweden's strong transatlantic bond which is "seeping into defence", which is also shown in [[Daniel Ek]]'s Prima Materia's investment in [[Helsing (company)|Helsing]] (which is a strategic partner of Palantir), which happened three months before Russia's 2022 invasion of Ukraine.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Dromberg |first1=Jonas |title=Why Sweden has the necessary tools to lead new Nordic defense drive |url=https://www.arctictoday.com/why-sweden-has-the-necessary-tools-to-lead-nordic-new-defence-drive/ |work=ArcticToday |date=2 April 2025}}</ref>

===Elevat3===
In 2020, Thiel became a strategic partner and anchor investor of Elevat3, which is set up by Christian Angermayer's Apeiron Investment Group to invest in startups in German-speaking countries. The fund focuses on "life sciences, deep tech, fintech (financial technology), property and insurance". The fund has a partnership with the Founder Fund.<ref name="HandelsblattHerz"/><ref>{{cite news |last1=Shead |first1=Sam |title=Peter Thiel's VC firm has become a strategic partner to a European tech fund |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2020/12/07/peter-thiels-founders-fund-partners-with-apeirons-elevat3-tech-fund.html |access-date=24 June 2025 |work=CNBC |date=7 December 2020 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Portfolio |url=https://www.elevat3.vc/our-portfolio |website=Elevat3 |language=en}}</ref> In 2020, Thiel invested into the [[Neunkirchen, Baden-Württemberg|Neunkirchen]]-based startup Neodigital through the fund.<ref name="HandelsblattHerz">{{cite news |last1=Herz |first1=Carsten |title=Star investor Peter Thiel invests indirectly in Maschmeyer start-up via funds |url=https://www.handelsblatt.com/finanzen/banken-versicherungen/versicherer/versicherer-star-investor-peter-thiel-steigt-ueber-fonds-indirekt-bei-maschmeyer-start-up-ein/26634418.html |access-date=7 August 2025 |work=www.handelsblatt.com |date=18 November 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Angermayer's Elevat3 Fund to Make First Investment in Neodigital |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2020-11-18/angermayer-s-elevat3-fund-to-make-first-investment-in-neodigital |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250216093616/https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2020-11-18/angermayer-s-elevat3-fund-to-make-first-investment-in-neodigital |archive-date=16 February 2025 |access-date=7 August 2025 |url-status=live }}</ref> The fund also backs other European startups such as the London-based aggregator startup Olsam.<ref>{{cite news |title=Thiel and Angermayer-backed Olsam hit by winding up petition – BeBeez International |url=https://bebeez.eu/2024/11/01/thiel-and-angermayer-backed-olsam-hit-by-winding-up-petition/ |access-date=7 August 2025 |archive-date=16 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250816063533/https://bebeez.eu/2024/11/01/thiel-and-angermayer-backed-olsam-hit-by-winding-up-petition/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> In 2022, through Elevat3 and in partnership with the Founders Fund, the Apeiron Group bought shares from the Chinese [[Fosun International]] and others to become a shareholder in the Hamburg-based [[NAGA Group]].<ref>{{cite news |title=The NAGA Group AG: Christian Angermayer's Apeiron Investment Group and Fosun Join Forces to Further Drive NAGA Growth |url=https://financialpost.com/pmn/press-releases-pmn/business-wire-news-releases-pmn/the-naga-group-ag-christian-angermayers-apeiron-investment-group-and-fosun-join-forces-to-further-drive-naga-growth |access-date=7 August 2025 |work=financialpost |language=en-CA}}</ref> Thiel also holds shares in {{ill|Heidelberger Beteiligungsholding|de|}} (which will be renamed as SQD.AI Strategies AG), the first dedicated German crypto holding treasury, through the firm.<ref>{{cite news |title=Christian Angermayer旗下Apeiron集团携手Piëch Family Office(保时捷与大众 汽车家族), 成立欧洲首家积累投资机构SQD.AI Strategies AG_腾讯新闻 |url=https://news.qq.com/rain/a/20250606A093AU00 |access-date=7 August 2025 |work=news.qq.com |date=6 June 2025 |language=zh-CN}}</ref>

===Octave companies===
Thiel is associated with a number of companies named Octave. Octave Japan or Octave Group, a [[Kantō region|Kantō]]- and Tokyo-based company controlled by Thiel, was founded in 2014.<ref>{{cite web |title=UNIFORM APPLICATION FOR INVESTMENT ADVISER REGISTRATION AND REPORT BY EXEMPT REPORTING ADVISERS Clarium Capital Management LLC |url=https://reports.adviserinfo.sec.gov/reports/ADV/138971/PDF/138971.pdf |access-date=19 July 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Mr James Rhee Aviation Outlook |url=https://www.terrapinn.com/exhibition/aviation-outlook-asia/speaker-james-RHEE.stm |website=Aviation Outlook Asia 2016 |access-date=19 July 2026 |language=en |date=26 January 2016}}</ref> Together with Rakuten, Noevir Holdings and Alpen, this company established [[AirAsia Japan]] as a joint venture in 2014, but the low-cost carrier shut down in 2020 due to the Covid pandemic.<ref>{{cite news |title=Two Of Asia's Richest Men Join Forces In Japan Venture |url=https://www.wealthbriefingasia.com/article.php/Two-Of-Asia's-Richest-Men-Join-Forces-In-Japan-Venture- |work=www.wealthbriefingasia.com |date=2 July 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Kumar |first1=P. Prem |last2=writer |first2=Nikkei staff |title=AirAsia approves shutting down Japan joint venture |url=https://asia.nikkei.com/business/transportation/airasia-approves-shutting-down-japan-joint-venture |work=Nikkei Asia |date=20 September 2020 |language=en}}</ref> Octave Ventures, a Thiel-backed, Nevada-based fund,<ref>{{cite web |title=Top Nevada Software VC investors |url=https://angelmatch.io/publication/nevada-vc-investors |website=angelmatch.io |access-date=19 July 2026 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=The top venture capital funding rounds for Austin tech startups in November 2020 |url=https://www.bizjournals.com/austin/inno/stories/roundups/2020/12/02/funding-for-austin-tech-startups-november-2020.html |work=Austin Business Journal |date=2 December 2020}}</ref> has supported companies such as Luminar, the fabless semiconductor company [[Wally Rhines|Cornami]] as well as [[John M. Martinis#Qolab|Qolab, a quantum company co-founded by Nobel laureate John M. Martinis]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Qolab Advances Superconducting Quantum Computing |url=https://quantumzeitgeist.com/qolab-quantum-computing/ |date=1 January 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Abdel-Kareem |first1=Mohamed |title=Qolab Closes $54.2 Million Series B to Accelerate Scalable Superconducting Quantum Processors |url=https://quantumcomputingreport.com/qolab-closes-54-2-million-series-b-to-accelerate-scalable-superconducting-quantum-processors/ |work=Quantum Computing Report |date=2 July 2026}}</ref> The manager of the fund is Michael S. Kim.<ref name="NikkeiOKWave">{{cite news |title=オウケイウェイヴ、米パランティアと業務提携契約を締結 |url=https://www.nikkei.com/article/DGXLRSP495780_V11C18A1000000/ |work=日本経済新聞 |date=15 November 2018 |language=ja}}</ref> It has two branches, Octave Life Sciences and Octave Tech Investment.<ref>{{cite web|title=OSARO Raises $30 Million Series C Round Led by Octave Ventures - 뉴스와이어 |url=https://www.newswire.co.kr/newsRead.php?no=928866 |website=www.newswire.co.kr |access-date=19 July 2026 |language=ko |date=18 August 2021}}</ref> The Mumbai-based biotech-focused Octave Life Sciences invests in companies such as {{ill|D&D Pharmatech|ko|D&D파마텍}}<ref>{{cite news |title=D&D Pharmatech raises KRW 20 billion Series A investment |url=https://www.biospectator.com/news/view/5260 |work=바이오스펙테이터 |date=2 April 2018}}</ref>  D&D and its branches such as [[Ted M. Dawson#Neuraly and Valted Seq|Neuraly and Valted Seq are associated with neurologist Ted M. Dawson]] (Valted Seq is also backed by Octave Ventures's affiliate OV Principal Investments).<ref>{{cite web |title=Valted Seq Raises $10.5 Million in Seed Funding Round |url=https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20211102005284/en/Valted-Seq-Raises-%2410.5-Million-in-Seed-Funding-Round |access-date=2 November 2021}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=UNIFORM APPLICATION FOR INVESTMENT ADVISER REGISTRATION AND REPORT BY EXEMPT REPORTING ADVISERS Octave Ventures LLC |url=https://reports.adviserinfo.sec.gov/reports/ADV/309878/PDF/309878.pdf |access-date=19 July 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Korea-based D&D under Johns Hopkins team in spotlight for novel dementia therapy - 매일경제 영문뉴스 펄스(Pulse) |url=https://pulse.mk.co.kr/news/english/10239550 |work=Pulse |date=3 March 2022 |language=ko}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Ray|first1=Forest  |title=Valted Seq Working to Discover Parkinson's Pathways, Biomarkers |url=https://parkinsonsnewstoday.com/news/newly-launched-valted-seq-working-to-discover-pathways-biomarkers-for-parkinsons-other-neurodegenerative-diseases/ |date=10 September 2020}}</ref> Octave Ventures plays a role in the partnership between Palantir and {{ill|OKWave|ja}} as well.<ref name="NikkeiOKWave"/><ref>{{cite news |title=（マーケットの話題）米大型上場、提携先にも関心 |url=https://www.nikkei.com/article/DGKKZO61292860Y0A700C2EN2000/ |work=日本経済新聞 |date=9 July 2020 |language=ja}}</ref>

===Crescendo Equity Partners===
Seoul-based Crescendo Equity is a [[private equity firm]] which focuses on developing SME companies into [[hidden champions]] and bringing them to the global scale.<ref>{{cite news |title=Crescendo Shifts to 'Stake-Splitting' Exit Amid HPSP Valuation Burden |url=https://www.globalnewstop.com/news/articleView.html?idxno=2164 |date=26 February 2026}}</ref><ref name="sungho">{{cite news |title=Sungho Electronics Buys INTIMAX, Peter Thiel's Crescendo Joins as Ally |url=https://www.globalnewstop.com/news/articleView.html?idxno=3244 |date=12 June 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Thiel-Backed Fund Looks for Korean Tech Firms to Take Global |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-04-26/thiel-backed-fund-looks-for-korean-tech-firms-to-take-global |access-date=24 June 2025 |agency=Bloomberg}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Crescendo Equity Partners Overview: Portfolio, Team and News |url=https://www.rootdata.com/Investors/detail/Crescendo%2BEquity%2BPartners?k=MTIyNTg%3D |website=RootData |language=en}}</ref>
According to the official website, "Crescendo was established in 2012 with the sponsorship of Peter Thiel".<ref name="LinkedIn profile">{{cite web | title=LinkedIn profile - Crescendo Equity Partners - Venture Capital and Private Equity Principals - Seoul | website=LinkedIn | url=https://www.linkedin.com/company/crescendo-equity-partners-limited/about/ | access-date=2025-06-27}}</ref> The fund is co-founded by Peter Thiel, Matt Danzeisen (who serves as a member of its investment committee and representative to selected portfolio companies),<ref name="Bridgetown"/> Andy Lee (company chairman), Matt Price (CEO) and Slava Zhakov (CTO). The president is Anand Chandrasekaran. [[General Catalyst]] is also heavily involved in its financing and organization.<ref name="Chosun"/><ref>{{cite web |title=Our Creation of Crescendo |url=https://www.generalcatalyst.com/stories/our-creation-of-crescendo |website=www.generalcatalyst.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Crescendo Closes $50 Million in Total Financing with Latest Round Led by General Catalyst {{!}} News |url=https://www.crescendo.ai/news/crescendo-closes-50-million-in-total-financing-with-latest-round-led-by-general-catalyst |access-date=1 August 2025 |work=www.crescendo.ai |language=en}}</ref> The fund invests in Line Next (a unit of the [[Line Corporation]]), a joint venture between [[Softbank]] and [[Naver Corporation|Naver]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Insights |first1=Ledger |title=Softbank offshoot LINE NEXT raises $140m for web3, NFTs |url=https://www.ledgerinsights.com/softbank-line-next-web3-nfts-raises-140m/ |access-date=24 June 2025 |work=Ledger Insights - blockchain for enterprise |date=18 December 2023}}</ref> The ''Business Korea'' credits Crescendo Equity Partners with transforming Korea's HPSP, which it invested in since 2017, into a global player in the semiconductor equipment sector.<ref name="Chosun">{{cite news |title=Crescendo expects record exit profit from HPSP amid competitive bidding |url=https://biz.chosun.com/en/en-finance/2025/02/19/B6BU5DVTRNDWXO4FS42OJQ2BAY/ |work=CHOSUNBIZ |date=19 February 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Eun-jin |first1=Kim |title=Crescendo Equity Partners Initiates Sale of 40.9% Stake in HPSP |url=https://www.businesskorea.co.kr/news/articleView.html?idxno=228689 |access-date=24 June 2025 |work=Businesskorea |date=6 November 2024 |language=ko}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=He-rim |first1=Jo |title=Why Carlyle, Blackstone, MBK are vying for stake in this little-known tech firm |url=http://koreaherald.com/article/10429368 |access-date=24 June 2025 |work=The Korea Herald |date=26 February 2025 |language=ko}}</ref> Crescendo also plays an important role in the Korean semiconductor industry through investments and support of other companies like {{ill|Hanmi Semiconductor|ko|한미반도체}}, {{ill|Samyang NCchem|ko|삼양엔씨켐}}.<ref>{{cite news |title=Samyang NCchem will receive general subscriptions for listing on KOSDAQ from the 16th to the 17th. S.. - MK |url=https://www.mk.co.kr/en/stock/11218527 |work=매일경제 |date=15 January 2025 |language=en}}</ref> and Movensys (originally known as Soft Servo Group or Soft Motions & Robotics; the name was changed to Movensys in 2021 after Crescendo's investment).<ref>{{cite news |title=Mitsubishi takes stake in motion software developer Movensys - Drives&Controls |url=https://drivesncontrols.com/mitsubishi-takes-stake-in-motion-software-developer-movensys/ |access-date=1 August 2025 |work=Drives&Controls - The global site of the UK's leading magazine for automation, motion engineering and power transmission |date=22 May 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=MOVENSYS LinkedIn |url=https://www.linkedin.com/company/movensys/ |website=www.linkedin.com |access-date=1 August 2025 |language=en |date=1 February 2014}}</ref> In 2026, Crescendo became a major shareholder of {{ill|Sungho Electronics|ko|성호전자}} after selling to them INTIMAX, a firm which provides semiconductor handlers to the "Big Three" memory manufacturers (SK Hynix, Samsung Electronics and Micron).<ref name="sungho"/>  In 2026, both HPSP and Hanmi were reported to prepare to work with [[Elon Musk]] on the [[Terafab]] project.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Wang |first1=Sherri|title=HPSP reportedly receives test equipment order for Musk's Terafab |url=https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20260612VL210/hpsp-testing-equipment-elon-musk-asml.html |work=DIGITIMES |date=12 June 2026 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Hanmi Semiconductor invests 50b won in SpaceX to join Terafab ecosystem |url=https://biz.chosun.com/en/en-it/2026/06/12/MFB632BMAVCYLFLFAGCUIXUZNM/ |work=CHOSUNBIZ |date=12 June 2026 |language=en}}</ref> The firm also invests in companies that make metal equipment, including Seojin System and Model Solution.<ref>{{cite news |title=Hanmi Semiconductor attracts another investment from PayPal co-founder Peter ThielView Details {{!}} Investment News {{!}} InvestKOREA(ENG) |url=https://www.investkorea.org/ik-en/bbs/i-465/detail.do?ntt_sn=465853 |access-date=1 August 2025 |work=www.investkorea.org |language=en}}</ref> Since 2019, Crescendo also owns [[Dong-Ah Geological Engineering]], which in 2024 succeeded in manufacturing a [[tunnel boring machine]] (TBM) using its own technology.<ref>{{Cite news |date=14 June 2024 |title=동아지질, 터널 굴착용 기계 제작…이달 중 현장 투입 |url=https://www.yna.co.kr/view/AKR20240614097600051 |work=[[Yonhap News]] |publisher=}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Crescendo PE revives Dong-Ah Geological sale as earnings rebound |url=https://biz.chosun.com/en/en-finance/2026/06/25/6MWEJOQDXFBZ3C4BCZAKMN2ABU/ |work=CHOSUNBIZ |date=25 June 2026 |language=en}}</ref>

===Pronomos Capital===
Thiel began to explore investing in charter cities on land after his interest in seasteading faded.<ref name= "BloombergProspera">{{cite news |last1=Farooq |first1=Umar |last2=BLAW |last3=McDonald |first3=Michael D |title=A Libertarian Island Dream in Honduras Is Now an $11 Billion Nightmare |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/features/2025-02-13/a-honduras-dream-city-now-faces-11-billion-political-dispute |access-date=March 12, 2026}}</ref> Thiel is the anchor backer of Pronomos Capital, a firm "set up like a venture capital fund" that seeks to establish experimental, semi-autonomous cities in vacant lands, with acceptance from the countries involved. The founder of the firm is [[Patri Friedman]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Chapman |first1=Lizette |title=The Hottest New Thing in Seasteading Is Land |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2019-12-20/silicon-valley-seasteaders-go-looking-for-low-tax-sites-on-land |access-date=13 August 2025 |work=Bloomberg.com |date=20 December 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251231213434/https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2019-12-20/silicon-valley-seasteaders-go-looking-for-low-tax-sites-on-land |archive-date= 2025-12-31|language=en}}</ref> Projects backed by the firm include [[Próspera]] in Honduras.<ref name= "NYTProspera">{{cite news |last1=Corbett |first1=Rachel |title=The For-Profit City That Might Come Crashing Down |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/08/28/magazine/prospera-honduras-crypto.html |access-date=13 August 2025 |date=28 August 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251219184428/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/08/28/magazine/prospera-honduras-crypto.html |archive-date= 2025-12-19}}</ref> The [[Próspera]] project attracted companies like [[Oklo Inc.]] (nuclear startup backed by Thiel's Mithril<ref>{{cite news |last1=Duffy |first1=Clare |title=AI bigwigs want to go all-in on nuclear. They also happen to be behind nuclear companies {{!}} CNN Business |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2024/12/24/tech/nuclear-energy-ai-leaders |access-date=13 August 2025 |work=CNN |date=24 December 2024 |language=en}}</ref> and Sam Altman) and biotech startups, but led to legal struggles when the new Honduran government changed the laws in 2022.<ref name= "BloombergProspera"/><ref name= "NYTProspera"/>

====Praxis and controversies in Denmark====
[[Praxis (proposed city)|Praxis]] is a company that seeks to establish a new city-state and has explored Greenland as a possible location.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Levy |first1=Rachael |last2=Ulmer |first2=Alexandra |title=Exclusive: Greenland 'Freedom City'? Rich donors push Trump for a tech hub up north |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/greenland-freedom-city-rich-donors-push-trump-tech-hub-up-north-2025-04-10/ |access-date=13 August 2025 |date=11 April 2025}}</ref> In 2025, when the Danish government was integrating Palantir into the country's military, police and intelligence services, a major argument put forth by opponents was that the Praxis project (backed by Thiel through Pronomos) was a threat to Greenland. Other arguments were concerned with Thiel's politics in the US and Palantir's association with American and other European intelligence services, as well as the security risk that might arise from handing citizens' data to Palantir. The [[Police of Denmark|Danish National Police]] answered with a reference to a 2021 response to the [[Folketing]], but otherwise, the Police, the [[Danish Security and Intelligence Service]] and Minister of Justice Peter Hummelgaard refused to comment on the matter.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Gjerding |first1=Sebastian |last2=Andersen |first2=Lasse Skou |title=Kontroversiel amerikansk virksomhed har adgang til fortrolige oplysninger hos dansk politi |url=https://www.information.dk/indland/2025/04/kontroversiel-amerikansk-virksomhed-adgang-fortrolige-oplysninger-dansk-politi?kupon=eyJpYXQiOjE3NDU3MzgxMDgsInN1YiI6IjI0MzMyOjgyOTM5NiJ9.Ixj7Qyo6zti7M6syRG9NEw |access-date=13 August 2025 |work=Information |date=25 April 2025 |language=da}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Seidelin |first1=Matias |title=OLFI - Kontroversielt amerikansk firma på vej ind i dansk våbenindustri |url=https://olfi.dk/2025/05/21/kontroversielt-amerikansk-firma-paa-vej-ind-i-dansk-vaabenindustri/ |date=21 May 2025 |language=da-DK}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Bech-Nielsen |first1=Peter Christian |title=Hummelgaard trods dybt kontroversielt PET-forslag om masseovervågning: Vil ikke tale om Palantir {{!}} Radar |url=https://radar.dk/artikel/hummelgaard-trods-dybt-kontroversielt-pet-forslag-om-masseovervaagning-vil-ikke-tale-om-palantir |access-date=13 August 2025 |work=radar.dk |date=5 May 2025 |language=da}}</ref>

=== Thiel Bio ===

The firm was found in 2023 by Jason Camm (Chief Medical Officer of Thiel Capital). The regulatory filing does not disclose the name of the single investor who provides US$100 million or Thiel's involvement beyond the use of his name.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Weiss |first1=Miles |title=Thiel's Chief Medical Officer Opens Biotech Venture Capital Fund |url=https://news.bloomberglaw.com/private-equity/thiels-chief-medical-officer-opens-biotech-venture-capital-fund |access-date=6 August 2025 |date=14 September 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250813160602/https://news.bloomberglaw.com/web/20250813160602/https://news.bloomberglaw.com/private-equity/thiels-chief-medical-officer-opens-biotech-venture-capital-fund |url-status=live |archive-date=August 13, 2025}}</ref> The fund has invested in Ataraxis AI and EnClear Therapies together with the Founders Fund.<ref>{{cite web |title=Bertelsmann Investments Invests In Ataraxis AI - Bertelsmann SE & Co. KGaA |url=https://www.bertelsmann.com/corporate-responsibility/engagement/project/bertelsmann-investments-invests-in-ataraxis-ai.jsp |website=www.bertelsmann.com |access-date=6 August 2025 |language=en|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250813160553/https://www.bertelsmann.com/corporate-responsibility/engagement/project/bertelsmann-investments-invests-in-ataraxis-ai.jsp|archive-date=August 13, 2025|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=EnClear Therapies, Inc. Secures Additional Funding to Advance Neuro-Oncology Innovations |url=https://braintumorinvestmentfund.org/news/enclear-therapies-inc-secures-additional-funding-to-advance-neuro-oncology-innovations/ |access-date=6 August 2025 |work=braintumorinvestmentfund.org}}</ref> Reports about investments in October 2025 (infection therapeutics company Peptilogics and cancer treatment startup HistoSonics) confirm that the firm is Thiel's. Hannes Holste from Thiel Capital is a partner.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Chapman |first1=Lizette |title=Thiel, Bezos Back Startup Treating Tumors With Sound Waves |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-10-15/thiel-bezos-back-startup-treating-tumors-with-sound-waves |date=15 October 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Jad |first1=Chloe |title=South Side biotech company raises $78 million for new drug to kill prosthetic joint infections |url=https://www.post-gazette.com/business/tech-news/2025/10/16/peptilogics-biotech-drug-raises-78-million/stories/202510160033 |work=Pittsburgh Post-Gazette |date=16 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251119021747/https://www.post-gazette.com/business/tech-news/2025/10/16/peptilogics-biotech-drug-raises-78-million/stories/202510160033 |archive-date=19 November 2025 |language=en}}</ref>

=== Rivendell companies ===
Thiel owns multiple entities named Rivendell, such as Rivendell One LLC, Rivendell 7 and Rivendell 25. Rivendell 7 and Rivendell 25 are personal investment vehicles, which are also used to hold Palantir shares.<ref>{{cite news |last1=del Castillo |first1=Michael |title=Peter Thiel has founded at least 5 'Lord of the Rings' -inspired companies |url=https://www.bizjournals.com/bizjournals/news/2015/04/16/peter-thiel-has-founded-at-least-five-lord-of-the.html |work=www.bizjournals.com |date=16 April 2015}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Lin |first1=Ed |title=Palantir Chairman Peter Thiel to Sell Up to $1 Billion of Stock |url=https://www.barrons.com/articles/palantir-stock-sell-peter-thiel-fb7bc3aa |work=barrons |date=10 September 2024|language=en-us}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Seiler |first1=Geoffrey |title=Palantir's Billionaire Chairman Just Filed to Sell $1 Billion in Stock. Should Investors Follow Suit? |url=https://www.fool.com/investing/2024/09/14/palantirs-billionaire-chairman-just-filed-to-sell/ |work=The Motley Fool |date=14 September 2024 |language=en}}</ref> [[ProPublica]] reports that Thiel's $1,700 PayPal investment and later investments In Palantir and Facebook through a [[Roth IRA]] had grown tax-free to over $5 billion by 2019. The Roth was held in Rivendell Trust since 2018.<ref>{{Cite web|last1=Bandler|first2=Justin |last2=Elliott |first3=Patricia |last3=Callahan |author3-link=Patricia Callahan |first1=James|title=Lord of the Roths: How Tech Mogul Peter Thiel Turned a Retirement Account for the Middle Class Into a $5 Billion Tax-Free Piggy Bank|url=https://www.propublica.org/article/lord-of-the-roths-how-tech-mogul-peter-thiel-turned-a-retirement-account-for-the-middle-class-into-a-5-billion-dollar-tax-free-piggy-bank?token=rM6_aIiraBTXQ_wSLfO1A-W9dsaUWVnP|access-date=14 November 2025|website=ProPublica|date=24 June 2021 |language=en|archive-date=14 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210714010029/https://www.propublica.org/article/lord-of-the-roths-how-tech-mogul-peter-thiel-turned-a-retirement-account-for-the-middle-class-into-a-5-billion-dollar-tax-free-piggy-bank?token=rM6_aIiraBTXQ_wSLfO1A-W9dsaUWVnP|url-status=live}}
</ref> Thiel bankrolled the satellite imaging startup HySpecIQ, known for serving government agencies but struggling financially, through Rivendell Fund.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Chapman |first1=Lizette |title=Peter Thiel Bankrolls Satellite Imaging Startup HySpecIQ |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-09-15/peter-thiel-bankrolls-satellite-imaging-startup-hyspeciq |work=Bloomberg.com |date=15 September 2021}}</ref> Rivendell entities are known to participate in his German or Korean investments.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Wirminghaus |first1=Niklas |title=In Deutschland setzt Peter Thiel fast nur noch auf Fintechs |url=https://financefwd.com/de/peter-thiel-deutschland-fintech/ |work=FinanceFWD |date=9 December 2019 |language=de}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=IQ |first1=S&P Capital |title=Rivendell Investment and an unknown buyer signed a contract to acquire 44.32% stake in Thinkfree NV from Hancom Inc. for KRW 29.1 billion. {{!}} MarketScreener |url=https://www.marketscreener.com/quote/stock/HANCOM-INC-6492369/news/Rivendell-Investment-and-an-unknown-buyer-signed-a-contract-to-acquire-44-32-stake-in-Thinkfree-NV-34563180/ |work=www.marketscreener.com |date=1 October 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Hager |first1=Sandy |title=Tracking the Fortunes of Corporate Psychedelia |url=https://yorkspace.library.yorku.ca/server/api/core/bitstreams/81763bdc-d70b-4016-9e3b-833220790b11/content |access-date=13 November 2025 |page=7}}</ref>

===Other business enterprises===

According to a 2020 article from ''Bloomberg'', Thiel was at the time an investor in funds managed by [[8VC]] and in the bank Disruptive Technology Advisers.<ref>{{cite news |title=Palantir's Peter Thiel keeps control while keeping invisible |url=https://www.latimes.com/business/technology/story/2020-09-29/palantirs-peter-thiel-keeps-control-while-keeping-invisible |access-date=31 July 2025 |work=Los Angeles Times |date=29 September 2020}}</ref> A 2017 ''Globe and mail'' article names Thiel as a limited partner at [[Social Capital]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Scott |first1=Alec |title=Chamath Palihapitiya wants to change the world |url=https://www.theglobeandmail.com/report-on-business/rob-magazine/how-canadian-facebook-billionaire-chamath-palihapitiya-plans-to-change-the-world/article34109864/ |date=23 February 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170518080213/https://www.theglobeandmail.com/report-on-business/rob-magazine/how-canadian-facebook-billionaire-chamath-palihapitiya-plans-to-change-the-world/article34109864/|archive-date=May 18, 2017}}</ref> He also sponsored Sam Altman's first venture fund, Hydrazine Capital as well as J.D.Vance's [[Narya Capital]].<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Hagey |first1=Keach |title=How Peter Thiel's Relationship With Eliezer Yudkowsky Launched the AI Revolution |url=https://www.wired.com/story/book-excerpt-the-optimist-open-ai-sam-altman/ |access-date=31 July 2025 |magazine=Wired |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260307071613/https://www.wired.com/story/book-excerpt-the-optimist-open-ai-sam-altman/|archive-date=March 7, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=How Thiel and Silicon Valley funded J.D. Vance's sudden rise |url=https://www.afr.com/world/north-america/how-peter-thiel-and-silicon-valley-funded-the-sudden-rise-of-jd-vance-20240718-p5jumu |access-date=31 July 2025 |work=Australian Financial Review |date=17 July 2024 |language=en}}</ref> He also backs Doepfner Capital, the venture fund of Moritz Döpfner, the son of [[Mathias Döpfner]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Politico's $50M Peter Thiel Problem |url=https://www.thenerdreich.com/politico-peter-thiel-problem-dopfner-jd-vance/ |access-date=31 July 2025 |work=The Nerd Reich |date=25 March 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=IAPD - Investment Adviser Public Disclosure - Homepage |url=https://adviserinfo.sec.gov/firm/summary/335225 |website=adviserinfo.sec.gov}}</ref> He funded 90% of [[Oren Zeev|Zeev Ventures's]] first fund and has backed it ever since.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Jin |first1=Berber |title=The Solo Venture Capitalist Who Doubles Down Like Andreessen |url=https://www.theinformation.com/articles/solo-venture-capitalist-oren-zeev-opens-his-books |url-status=live |access-date=13 March 2026 |work=The Information |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221206203142/https://www.theinformation.com/articles/solo-venture-capitalist-oren-zeev-opens-his-books |archive-date=December 6, 2022|language=en}}</ref> The Founders Fund was also a backer of the second fund of the Indonesia-focused Intudo. The involvement helped Intudo to validate its mission.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Freischlad |first1=Nadine |title=Intudo Ventures announces new $50m Indonesia-only fund with backing from Peter Thiel's Founders Fund |url=https://kr-asia.com/intudo-ventures-announces-new-50m-indonesia-only-fund-with-backing-from-pieter-thiels-founders-fund |access-date=31 July 2025 |work=KrASIA |date=14 February 2019 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Shu |first1=Catherine |title=Indonesia-focused Intudo Ventures closes $115M third fund |url=https://techcrunch.com/2021/09/07/indonesia-focused-intudo-ventures-closes-oversubscribed-115m-third-fund/ |access-date=31 July 2025 |work=TechCrunch |date=8 September 2021}}</ref> Founders Fund is also among the backers of the Israel-based Mensch Capital.<ref>{{cite news |title=Cyera acquires Israeli startup Shape AI |url=https://en.globes.co.il/en/article-cyera-acquires-israeli-startup-shape-ai-1001512508 |access-date=31 July 2025 |work=Globes |date=6 November 2025 |language=en}}</ref> Thiel also backs the Singaporean venture investment firm Syfe Group through Valar.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Thornhill |first1=James |date=4 June 2025 |title=Peter Thiel-backed Singapore venture pushes into financial advice |url=https://www.afr.com/companies/financial-services/singapore-s-syfe-plans-to-expand-selfwealth-into-financial-advice-20250603-p5m4nx |access-date=7 August 2025 |work=Australian Financial Review |language=en}}</ref> The Founders Fund also invested in the Seattle-based private equity fund Privateer Holdings in 2015, thereby becoming the first institutional investor in the cannabis industry.<ref>{{cite news |last1=McGee |first1=Suzanne |title=Paypal founder Peter Thiel becomes marijuana's first big investor |url=https://www.theguardian.com/business/2015/jan/08/cannabis-investor-peter-theil-paypal-founder |access-date=9 August 2025 |work=The Guardian |date=8 January 2015}}</ref>

His first investment in a hedge fund managed by an outside manager was made in 2011: the firm was Grandmaster Capital Management, founded by [[Patrick Wolff]], former Clarium and [[Thiel Macro]] executive.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Rose-Smith |first1=Imogen |title=Peter Thiel Reboots {{!}} Institutional Investor |url=https://www.institutionalinvestor.com/article/2bt017pmce8xr1woh6ku8/portfolio/peter-thiel-reboots |work=www.institutionalinvestor.com |date=28 February 2011 |language=en}}</ref> Also in 2011, he backed the second fund of [[Joshua Kushner]]'s [[Thrive Capital]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Shontell |first1=Alyson |title=26-Year-Old Investor Raises $40 Million More For His Fund, Thrive Capital |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/thrive-capital-raises-40-million-fund-2011-8 |work=Business Insider |date=22 August 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111028172316/https://www.businessinsider.com/thrive-capital-raises-40-million-fund-2011-8 |archive-date=2011-10-28 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Vardi |first1=Nathan |title=Joshua Kushner, Managing Partner, Thrive Capital, 26 - 2011-12-19 - 30 Under 30: Finance |url=https://www.forbes.com/pictures/mdg45gdhk/joshua-kushner-founder-and-managing-partner-thrive-capital-26/ |work=Forbes |date=19 December 2011 |language=en}}</ref>

In 2019, Thiel, together with [[Mark Cuban]] and [[Marc Andreessen]], backed the San Francisco-based crypto investment fund 1Confirmation.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Partz |first1=Helen |title=Peter Thiel-Backed Investment Fund 1Confirmation Raises $45M |url=https://cointelegraph.com/news/peter-thiel-backed-investment-fund-1confirmation-raises-45-million |work=Cointelegraph |date=25 September 2019 |language=en}}</ref>

Thiel gives backing to [[Vivek Ramaswamy]]'s financial firm Strive Asset Management, also described as an activist fund. The firm aims to free "corporate America" of what they deem to be "stakeholder capitalism" [[Environmental, social, and governance|ESG]] mandates created by the three companies [[BlackRock]], [[The Vanguard Group|Vanguard]] and [[State Street Corporation|State Street]] and accuse them of causing the energy crisis. The firm does not deny climate science.<ref>{{cite news |title=Strive |url=https://strive.com/article/revenge_of_the_based_thiel-backed_fund_to_take_on_woke_blackrock_activism |access-date=7 August 2025 |work=strive.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Peter Thiel-Backed ETF Takes Aim at ESG |url=https://www.etf.com/sections/news/peter-thiel-backed-etf-takes-aim-esg |access-date=7 August 2025 |work=etf.com}}</ref>

In 2021, Thiel backed the first fund of A-Star Partners, founded by [[Kevin Hartz]], former partner at Founders Fund.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Clark |first1=Kate |title=Fund Led by PayPal, Airbnb Backer Kevin Hartz Targets $250 Million |url=https://www.theinformation.com/articles/fund-led-by-paypal-airbnb-backer-kevin-hartz-targets-250-million |work=The Information |date=27 August 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210827174631/https://www.theinformation.com/articles/fund-led-by-paypal-airbnb-backer-kevin-hartz-targets-250-million |archive-date=27 August 2021 |language=en}}</ref> In 2022, he backed B2B-focused Wischoff Ventures founded by solo GP Nichole Wischoff.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Heim |first1=Anna |title=Solo GP Nichole Wischoff raises $20M fund backed by Peter Thiel to invest in 'unsexy businesses' |url=https://techcrunch.com/2022/12/16/solo-gp-nichole-wischoff-raises-20m-fund-backed-by-peter-thiel-to-invest-in-unsexy-businesses/ |work=TechCrunch |date=16 December 2022}}</ref>

Thiel is also a major backer of the venture debt firm Tacora, founded by Keri Findley.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Chapman |first1=Lizette |title=Peter Thiel-Backed Venture Debt Firm Tacora Raises $685 Million |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-07-29/peter-thiel-backed-venture-debt-firm-tacora-raises-685-million |access-date=31 July 2025}}</ref> Its inaugural fund in 2022 raised US$350 million in total, including US$250 million from Thiel. ''Bloomberg'' comments that, "It's an unusually large investment for Thiel, the size of which hasn't been previously reported." Findley was originally an associate of Danzeisen, whom she met because she and Thiel Capital both invested in [[SoFi]]. Thiel agreed to fund her after she discussed the idea with him at a casual dinner.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Chapman |first1=Lizette |title=Peter Thiel Bets $250 Million on Venture Debt Fund |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-12-08/peter-thiel-backs-tacora-capital-from-third-point-s-keri-findley |work=Bloomberg.com |date=8 September 2022|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Rafieyan |first1=Darius |title=The 10 power players you need to know to understand the booming world of venture debt |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/meet-the-10-power-players-dominating-the-venture-debt-boom-2023-2#keri-findley-ceo-tacora-capital-4 |work=Business Insider |date=6 March 2023}}</ref>

Alexandra Ulmer and Joseph Tanfani from ''[[Reuters]]'' remark that Thiel was an instrumental force behind the creation of [[1789 Capital]], which was co-founded in 2022 by [[Omeed Malik]] and [[Chris Buskirk]], a confidant of Thiel's. [[Blake Masters]] is also a board member. The fund is intended to create a "parallel economy", a network that combines "businesses, media outlets and political organizations" associated with the America First movement. In 2024, it recruited [[Donald Trump Jr.]] as a partner.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Betts |first1=Anna |title=Donald Trump Jr to join venture capital firm rather than father's administration |url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-jr-1789-capital |work=The Guardian |date=12 November 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Ulmer |first1=Alexandra |last2=Tanfani |first2=Joseph |title=Trump-linked venture fund 1789 Capital tops $1 billion in assets |url=https://www.reuters.com/investigations/trump-linked-venture-fund-1789-capital-tops-1-billion-assets-2025-09-08/ |date=8 September 2025 |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/FiX7c |archive-date=13 March 2026 }}</ref>

He personally invests in [[Quora]] (leading its Series B),<ref>{{cite news |last1=Tsotsis |first1=Alexia |title=Quora Raises $50M At $400M From Peter Thiel, D'Angelo Puts In $20M Of His Own Money |url=https://techcrunch.com/2012/05/14/quora-raises-50-at-400m-from-peter-thiel-dangelo-puts-20m-of-his-own-money/ |work=TechCrunch |date=14 May 2012}}</ref> [[Reddit]],<ref>{{cite news |last1=Cook |first1=James |title=Reddit Just Raised $50 Million From A Group Of A-List Investors Including Snoop Dogg |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/reddit-raised-50-million-2014-10 |work=Business Insider |date=1 October 2024}}</ref> and nuclear startup [[Saltfoss Energy|Seaborg Technologies (now Saltfoss Energy)]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Dalton |first1=David |title=Denmark's Seaborg Attracts Investment For Molten Salt Reactor Project |url=https://www.nucnet.org/news/denmark-s-seaborg-attracts-investment-for-molten-salt-reactor-project |work=The Independent Global Nuclear News Agency |date=26 March 2018}}</ref>

====AbCellera====
He served on [[AbCellera]]'s board from 2020 to 2024, when he resigned for personal reasons. Both sides stated that there was no disagreement, with Thiel saying that he was proud to have helped the company and AbCellera's founder Carl Hansen thanking him for his mentorship.<ref>{{cite news |title=AbCellera Announces Resignation of Tech Entrepreneur and Investor Peter Thiel from Company's Board of Directors |url=https://www.bctechnology.com/news/2024/2/26/AbCellera-Announces-Resignation-of-Tech-Entrepreneur-and-Investor-Peter-Thiel-from-Companys-Board-of-Directors.cfm |access-date=11 August 2025 |work=T-Net British Columbia}}</ref> He also retains his stake in the company, as of November 2024.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Krantz |first1=Matt |title=Peter Thiel Made A Fortune On Palantir — Here Are His 3 Other Bets |url=https://www.investors.com/etfs-and-funds/sectors/sp500-peter-thiel-made-a-fortune-on-palantir-here-are-his-3-other-bets/ |access-date=11 August 2025 |date=9 November 2024}}</ref>

==== Y Combinator ====
In March 2015, Thiel joined [[Y Combinator]] as one of 10 part-time partners.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://blog.ycombinator.com/welcome-peter|title=Welcome Peter|work=Y Combinator Posthaven|access-date=7 June 2015|archive-date=21 May 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150521115726/http://blog.ycombinator.com/welcome-peter|url-status=live}}</ref> In November 2017, it was reported that Y Combinator had severed its ties with Thiel.<ref>{{cite web|url =https://qz.com/1132892/peter-thiel-is-no-longer-affiliated-with-silicon-valleys-y-combinator-accelerator/|title =Peter Thiel is no longer affiliated with star accelerator Y Combinator|first =Michael J.|last =Coren|website =Quartz|date =17 November 2017|access-date =19 November 2017|archive-date =19 November 2017|archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20171119095514/https://qz.com/1132892/peter-thiel-is-no-longer-affiliated-with-silicon-valleys-y-combinator-accelerator/|url-status =live}}</ref>

====Enhanced Games====
[[File:Aron D'Souza 2025.jpg|thumb|Aron D'Souza in 2025]]
In 2024, Thiel became the lead funder of the [[Enhanced Games]], a multi-sport event that will allow athletes to use [[performance-enhancing substances]] without being subject to drug tests.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Ostlere |first1=Lawrence |title=Enhanced Games: Paypal billionaire Peter Thiel invests in controversial doped Olympics |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/olympics/enhanced-games-peter-thiel-olympics-b2488157.html |website=The Independent |date=1 February 2024 |access-date=4 February 2024 |archive-date=4 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240204114246/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/olympics/enhanced-games-peter-thiel-olympics-b2488157.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="swimswam">{{cite news |last1=Keith |first1=Braden |title=Enhanced Games Say They'll Fund Lawsuits for Clean Athletes Who Participate |url=https://swimswam.com/enhanced-games-founder-peter-thiel-says-hell-fund-lawsuits-for-clean-athletes-who-participate/ |work=SwimSwam |date=12 June 2025}}</ref> The founder is the Australian lawyer Aron D'Souza, who came to know and become Thiel's confidant in the process of leading the Gawker case for him. Angermayer, who was introduced to D'Souza by Thiel, also invested, even though, as per ''Wired'', Thiel and Angermayer were not normally interested in sports.<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Katwala |first1=Amit |title=The Definitive, Insane, Swimsuit-Bursting Story of the Steroid Olympics |url=https://www.wired.com/story/enhanced-games-freestyle-record-las-vegas-steroids/ |access-date=31 July 2025 |magazine=Wired}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Ryan |first1=Mac |title=This Man Helped Peter Thiel Demolish Gawker |url=https://www.buzzfeednews.com/article/ryanmac/this-is-the-man-who-helped-peter-thiel-demolish-gawker-mr-a |work=BuzzFeed News |date=24 February 2018 |language=en}}</ref> The startup agrees to cover legal expenses for any clean athletes who participate in the event and are banned from mainstream competitions as a result.<ref name="swimswam"/>

==== Objection ====
In 2026, Thiel invested in Objection.ai, a startup that evaluates claims made by journalists.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bellan |first=Rebecca |date=2026-04-15 |title=Exclusive: Can AI judge journalism? A Thiel-backed startup says yes, even if it risks chilling whistleblowers |url=https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/15/can-ai-judge-journalism-a-thiel-backed-startup-says-yes-even-if-it-risks-chilling-whistleblowers/ |access-date=2026-04-22 |website=TechCrunch |language=en-US}}</ref>

====Carbyne====
{{see also|List of people named in the Epstein files}}

In 2018, the Founders Fund invested in the [[Carbyne (company)|Israeli company Carbyne]] (emergency service).<ref name="Reason"/>

Leaked emails (released by the hacker group [[Handala (hacker group)|Handala]], which "likely operates out of Iran's Ministry of Intelligence", according to Reuters<ref>{{cite news |last1=A.J. |first1=Vicens |last2=Satter |first2=Raphael |title=Iran's hackers keep a low profile after Israeli and US strikes |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/irans-hackers-keep-low-profile-after-israeli-us-strikes-2025-06-27/ |date=27 June 2025}}</ref>) show that in 2014, [[Jeffrey Epstein]] leveraged his relationship with former Israeli Prime Minister [[Ehud Barak]] to get access to Thiel.<ref name="Reason">{{cite news |last1=Petti |first1=Matthew |title=Inside Jeffrey Epstein's spy industry connections |url=https://reason.com/2025/08/27/inside-jeffrey-epsteins-spy-industry-connections/ |url-status=live |work=Reason.com |date=27 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250827151130/https://reason.com/2025/08/27/inside-jeffrey-epsteins-spy-industry-connections/ |archive-date=27 August 2025}}</ref> Epstein arranged for Barak to meet Thiel in New York on June 9, 2014. In 2016, Epstein pitched Reporty (later Carbyne) to Valar, but the proposal got rejected on account of being premature (Epstein invested in total 40 million in Valar in 2015 and 2016).<ref>{{Cite news |last=Goldstein |first=Matthew |date=2025-06-04 |title=Jeffrey Epstein Invested With Peter Thiel, and His Estate Is Reaping Millions |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/04/business/jeffrey-epstein-peter-thiel-estate.html |access-date=2025-07-24 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>). Valar's McCormack said they would try to reengage when the startup was more developed. In 2018, the Founders Fund joined Carbyne's $15&nbsp;million Series B.<ref name="Reason"/>

Thiel said that the subsequent interactions with Epstein following their introduction in 2014 were due to the fact Epstein was a "crazed networker". One of the people introduced to Thiel by Epstein was the Russian diplomat [[Vitaly Churkin]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Benoit |first1=Khadeeja Safdar and David |title=From A to Z: The Famous Names in Jeffrey Epstein's Calendar |url=https://www.wsj.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein-calendar-names-ec88e7a0 |work=The Wall Street Journal |date=19 December 2023 |url-access=subscription}}</ref> ''[[Byline Times]]'' suggests that Epstein was one of contact points that Thiel used for his political network in the UK, including with on the [[Labour Party (UK)]], although there is no record of Thiel's social visits to Epstein's homes or flights on his jet.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Jukes |first1=Peter |title=From Epstein to Starmer: Mapping Peter Thiel's Web of Influence in the UK |url=https://bylinetimes.com/2025/09/12/peter-thiel-jeffrey-epstein-keir-starmer-peter-mandelson-global-counsel/ |work=Byline Times |date=12 September 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Jukes |first1=Nafeez Ahmed and Peter |title='Blue Labour' and the Thiel Effect: How MAGA Is Making In-Roads Into British Politics |url=https://bylinetimes.com/2025/09/25/blue-labour-and-the-thiel-effect-how-maga-is-making-in-roads-into-british-politics/#:~:text=On%20the%20business%20side%2C%20the,Valley%20blogger%20'Mencius%20Moldbug'. |work=Byline Times |date=25 September 2025}}</ref>

Documents reviewed by ''The Wall Street Journal'' in 2023 show that there were scheduled meetings (half a dozen between 2014 and 2016) between Thiel and Epstein, including with others such as [[Woody Allen]] and Obama's advisor [[Kathryn Ruemmler]]. [[Reid Hoffman]], Thiel's friend from the [[PayPal Mafia]] and a big Democratic donor was the one who directly introduced Thiel to Epstein (for years Epstein acquaintances had tried to invite Thiel to meet Epstein but were rejected) and also participated.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Benoit |first1=Khadeeja Safdar and David |title=How Jeffrey Epstein Tried to Tap Into Trump's Circle |url=https://www.wsj.com/politics/jeffrey-epstein-trump-associates-ab19d1f0 |work=The Wall Street Journal |date=30 August 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230830103809/https://www.wsj.com/politics/jeffrey-epstein-trump-associates-ab19d1f0 |url-status=live |archive-date=30 August 2023 }}</ref> Documents from the US House of Representatives showed Epstein invited Thiel to [[Little Saint James|his private island]] in 2018. A spokesperson for Thiel said he never visited the island.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Wendler |first1=Jacob |title=The 9 most shocking revelations in the Epstein docs |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2025/11/12/here-are-9-of-the-most-shocking-revelations-in-the-latest-batch-of-epstein-documents-00649853 |date=12 November 2025 |work=Politico}}</ref> In 2025, ''[[Snopes]]'' criticized a claim on the internet that Epstein offered girls to Thiel and others as misleading by omitting context.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Ibrahim |first1=Nur |title=Email doesn't show Epstein offering girls for sex to Peter Thiel, Gordon Brown among, others |url=https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/email-epstein-girls-peter-thiel-gordon-brown/ |work=Snopes |date=14 November 2025 |language=en}}</ref>

''[[Euronews]]'' writes that there is no known major financial connection between Thiel and Epstein, but Thiel seemed to treat Epstein as a contact point.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Hajdari |first1=Una |title=Epstein files cast long shadow over global business elite |url=https://www.euronews.com/business/2025/11/19/epstein-files-cast-long-shadow-over-global-business-elite |work=www.euronews.com |date=19 November 2025}}</ref> ''[[The San Francisco Standard]]'' comments that around the time, other Israeli officials (acting independently of Barak) tried to build contact with Thiel as well, often aiming at a "lucrative" job at Palantir.<ref>{{cite news |last1=MacColl |first1=Margaux |title=Inside the extended courtship linking Jeffrey Epstein, Peter Thiel, and Israeli officials |url=https://sfstandard.com/2025/11/23/extended-courtship-linking-jeffrey-epstein-peter-thiel-israeli-officials/ |work=sfstandard.com |date=23 November 2025 |language=en}}</ref>

''MintPress'' journalist<ref>{{cite news |title=How NeoCon Billionaire Paul Singer Is Driving The Outsourcing of U.S. Tech Jobs to Israel |url=https://www.wrmea.org/2019-august-september/how-neocon-billionaire-paul-singer-is-driving-the-outsourcing-of-u.s.-tech-jobs-to-israel.html |access-date=19 October 2025 |work=WRMEA |date=31 July 2019 |language=en-gb}}</ref> Whitney Webb has spread theories that link Thiel and Palantir to Epstein, Mossad, CIA. Webb has shared these theories via the Chinese website of ''[[MintPress News]]''{{unreliable source?|reason=WP:RSP lists MintPress News as "deprecated". Sources citing MintPress News for factual info have to be either carefully used or should be removed from this article.|sure=yes|date=June 2026}}{{snd}}known for being part of the "Russian web of disinformation"<ref>{{Cite web |date=February 8, 2019 |title=How a Little-Known Pro-Kremlin Analyst Became a Philippine Expert Overnight |url=https://www.codastory.com/disinformation/how-a-little-known-pro-kremlin-analyst-became-a-philippine-expert-overnight/ |access-date=April 4, 2022 |website=[[Coda Story]] |language=en-US |archive-date=June 25, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220625112749/https://www.codastory.com/disinformation/how-a-little-known-pro-kremlin-analyst-became-a-philippine-expert-overnight/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal |last=Ross |first=Alexander Reid |author-link=Alexander Reid Ross |date=November 8, 2019 |title=Fooling the Nation: Extremism and the Pro-Russia Disinformation Ecosystem |url=https://www.boundary2.org/2019/11/alexander-reid-ross-fooling-the-nation-extremism-and-the-pro-russia-disinformation-ecosystem/#_ftn81 |journal=[[Boundary 2]] |publisher=[[Duke University Press]] |access-date=April 10, 2022 |archive-date=July 19, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210719133650/https://www.boundary2.org/2019/11/alexander-reid-ross-fooling-the-nation-extremism-and-the-pro-russia-disinformation-ecosystem/#_ftn81 |url-status=live }}</ref>{{snd}}and Trineday, a publisher founded by conspiracy theorist<ref>{{cite news |last1=Robertson |first1=Campbell |title=In Donald Trump, Conspiracy Fans Find a Campaign to Believe In |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/18/us/in-donald-trump-conspiracy-fans-find-a-campaign-to-believe-in.html |access-date=19 October 2025 |date=17 October 2016}}</ref> Kris Millegan.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Sri Lanka Guardian |title=Fauci's Covert CIA Visit to Conceal COVID Truth and the Rise of a Privatized Surveillance State |url=https://slguardian.org/faucis-covert-cia-visit-to-conceal-covid-truth-and-the-rise-of-a-shadow-surveillance-state/ |work=Sri Lanka Guardian |date=16 October 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite book |last1=Webb |first1=Whitney Alyse |title=One Nation Under Blackmail – Vol. 2: The Sordid Union Between Intelligence and Organized Crime that Gave Rise to Jeffrey Epstein Vol. 2 |date=20 October 2022 |publisher=TrineDay |isbn=978-1-63424-357-5 |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=DsSVEAAAQBAJ&pg=PT286 |language=en}}</ref>

== Gawker lawsuit ==
{{Main|Bollea v. Gawker}}

In May 2016, Thiel confirmed in an interview with ''[[The New York Times]]'' that he had paid $10 million in legal expenses to finance several lawsuits brought by others, including a lawsuit by Terry Bollea ([[Hulk Hogan]]) against [[Gawker Media]] for invasion of privacy, intentional infliction of emotional distress, and infringement of personality rights after Gawker made sections of a [[sex tape]] involving Bollea public.<ref>{{cite web|last1=McBride|first1=Sarah|last2=Somerville|first2=Heather|date=25 May 2016|title=Tech billionaire Thiel helps Hulk Hogan|url=https://www.yahoo.com/tech/tech-billionaire-thiel-backing-wrestler-hogans-gawker-lawsuit-040625660.html|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160526152009/https://www.yahoo.com/tech/tech-billionaire-thiel-backing-wrestler-hogans-gawker-lawsuit-040625660.html|archive-date=26 May 2016|access-date=26 May 2016|website=[[Yahoo Tech]]}}</ref> The jury awarded Bollea $140 million, and Gawker announced it was permanently closing due to the lawsuit in August 2016.<ref>{{cite magazine|author=Davey Alba|author-link=Davey Alba|date=18 August 2016|title=Peter Thiel Just Got His Wish: Gawker Is Shutting Down|url=https://www.wired.com/2016/08/peter-thiel-just-got-wish-gawker-shutting/|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160818203822/http://www.wired.com/2016/08/peter-thiel-just-got-wish-gawker-shutting/|archive-date=18 August 2016|access-date=18 August 2016|magazine=Wired}}</ref> Thiel referred to his financial support of Bollea's case as one of the "greater philanthropic things that I've done."<ref name="Gawker">{{Cite news |last=Sorkin |first=Andrew Ross |date=2016-05-26 |title=Peter Thiel, Tech Billionaire, Reveals Secret War With Gawker |language=en-US |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/26/business/dealbook/peter-thiel-tech-billionaire-reveals-secret-war-with-gawker.html |access-date=2023-04-30 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170223185042/https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/26/business/dealbook/peter-thiel-tech-billionaire-reveals-secret-war-with-gawker.html |issn=0362-4331 |url-status=live |archive-date=23 February 2017 }}</ref>

Thiel said he was motivated to sue Gawker after they published a 2007 article publicly [[outing]] him, headlined "Peter Thiel is totally gay, people."<ref>{{cite web |url=https://gawker.com/335894/peter-thiel-is-totally-gay-people |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090521120121/https://gawker.com/335894/peter-thiel-is-totally-gay-people |url-status=dead |archive-date=2009-05-21 |title=Peter Thiel is totally gay, people |first=Owen |last=Thomas |date=December 19, 2007 |work=Gawker.com |access-date=12 March 2026 }}</ref> Thiel stated that Gawker articles about others, including his friends, had "ruined people's lives for no reason," and said, "It's less about revenge and more about specific deterrence."<ref name="Gawker" /> In response to criticism that his funding of lawsuits against Gawker could restrict the [[freedom of the press]], Thiel cited his donations to the {{not a typo|Committee}} to Protect Journalists and stated, "I refuse to believe that journalism means massive privacy violations. I think much more highly of journalists than that. It's precisely because I respect journalists that I do not believe they are endangered by fighting back against Gawker."<ref name="Gawker" /> Owen Thomas, the author of the Gawker article, stated that he did not think it was an outing in the conventional sense, as Thiel had been open about his homosexuality, but the "strangely conservative" Silicon Valley had refused to talk about it. Thiel said that the problem was less about the outing itself, but the troubles it caused with regard to his business in Saudi Arabia and his parents.{{sfn|Chafkin|2021|pp=127,128,134}}

On 15 August 2016, Thiel published an opinion piece in ''The New York Times'' in which he argued that his defense of online privacy went beyond Gawker.<ref name="nytimesopedonlineprivacyaugust15">{{cite news|last1=Thiel|first1=Peter|date=15 August 2016|title=Peter Thiel: The Online Privacy Debate Won't End With Gawker|work=The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/16/opinion/peter-thiel-the-online-privacy-debate-wont-end-with-gawker.html?_r=0|url-status=live|access-date=16 August 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160817232714/http://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/16/opinion/peter-thiel-the-online-privacy-debate-wont-end-with-gawker.html?_r=0|archive-date=17 August 2016}}</ref> He highlighted his support for the [[Intimate Privacy Protection Act]] and said that athletes and business executives have the right to stay in the closet as long as they want to.<ref name="nytimesopedonlineprivacyaugust15" />

In an open letter to Thiel after losing the case, Gawker's [[Nick Denton]] accused Thiel of making them "stripped naked", together with the warning "in the next phase, you too will be subject to a dose of transparency. However philanthropic your intention, and careful the planning, the details of your involvement will be gruesome."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Nakamura |first1=Reid |title=Nick Denton's Open Letter to Peter Thiel: 'This Is Twisted' |url=https://sg.news.yahoo.com/nick-denton-open-letter-peter-thiel-twisted-224622733.html |access-date=5 June 2025 |work=Yahoo News |date=26 May 2016 |language=en-SG}}</ref> Later though, in 2025, Denton said that Thiel was right and did him a favor in forcing the sale of Gawker Media.<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Peele |first1=Anna |title=Nick Denton on Betting Against Elon Musk, Aligning With Peter Thiel, and Selling That SoHo Loft |url=https://www.vanityfair.com/news/story/nick-denton-interview-thiel-musk |access-date=5 June 2025 |magazine=Vanity Fair |date=24 March 2025}}</ref>

== Views and political activities ==
[[File:Thiel vs. Graeber (15106550347).jpg|thumb|Peter Thiel and [[David Graeber]] discussing technology, democracy and the future in 2014<ref name="Schuessler">{{cite news |last1=Schuessler |first1=Jennifer |title=Still No Flying Cars? Debating Technology's Future |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/arts/peter-thiel-and-david-graeber-debate-technologys-future.html |date=21 September 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250701211841/https://www.nytimes.com/2014/09/22/arts/peter-thiel-and-david-graeber-debate-technologys-future.html |url-status=live |work=NYTimes.com |archive-date= 2025-07-01}}</ref>]]

===Philosophical views===
Thiel is described by different authors and media sources in different ways.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Scheu |first1=René |title=Peter Thiel: 'Donald Trump handelt für mich zu wenig disruptiv' |url=https://www.nzz.ch/feuilleton/peter-thiel-donald-trump-handelt-fuer-mich-zu-wenig-disruptiv-ld.1471818 |work=Neue Zürcher Zeitung |date=2 April 2019 |language=de-CH}}</ref><ref name="Hodgkinson">{{cite news |last1=Hodgkinson |first1=Tom |title=With friends like these ... |url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2008/jan/14/facebook |work=The Guardian |date=13 January 2008 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Mertes |first1=Klaus |title=Peter Thiel: Der Oligarch als Opfer |url-status=live |url=https://www.zeit.de/kultur/2025-03/peter-thiel-ideologie-macht-oligarchen-ambitionen/komplettansicht |work=Die Zeit |date=22 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250422093846/https://www.zeit.de/kultur/2025-03/peter-thiel-ideologie-macht-oligarchen-ambitionen#selection-1715.0-1733.12 |archive-date=22 April 2025 |language=de-DE}}</ref> He identifies as a [[libertarian]].<ref name=":3"/> He has been called an [[Ayn Rand]] libertarian,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Belfield |first1=Haydn |title=There's no libertarian approach to preventing the end of the world |url=https://www.vox.com/future-perfect/2023/3/7/23618766/peter-thiel-existential-risk-oxford-union-silicon-valley-technology-artficial-intelligence |work=Vox |date=7 March 2023}}</ref> [[Plutocracy|plutocratic]] reactionary,<ref name="Heer 06302025">{{Cite news|last=Heer|first=Jeet|date=June 30, 2025|title=The Billionaires Are Abandoning Humanity|work=[[The Nation (magazine)|The Nation]]|url=https://www.thenation.com/article/society/peter-thiel-billionaires-abandoning-humanity/#|url-access=subscription|access-date=September 7, 2025}}</ref> militarist techno-libertarian,{{sfn|Biddle|2024}} and [[libertarian authoritarian]].<ref>{{Cite web|last1=Nachtwey|first1=Oliver|last2=Amlinger|first2=Carolin|date=December 7, 2023|title=The new authoritarian personality|url=https://www.newstatesman.com/ideas/2023/12/new-authoritarian-personality|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241208221401/https://www.newstatesman.com/ideas/2023/12/new-authoritarian-personality|archive-date=8 December 2024|access-date=September 7, 2025|website=[[New Statesman]]|language=en-US}}</ref> His attitude towards democracy has been described as "skeptical",<ref name="lemonde1">{{cite news |last1=Bacqué |first1=Raphaëlle |last2=Leloup |first2=Damien |last3=Piquard |first3=Alexandre |title=Peter Thiel, the libertarian billionaire waging war on government |url=https://www.lemonde.fr/en/summer-reads/article/2025/07/22/peter-thiel-the-libertarian-billionaire-waging-war-on-government_6743617_183.html |website=[[Le Monde]] |date=22 July 2025 |language=en}}</ref> partly antidemocratic,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Mäurer |first1=Dietrich Karl |title=Sorge vor Missbrauch bei Software des US-Unternehmens Palantir |url=https://www.tagesschau.de/inland/gesellschaft/palantir-polizei-software-100.html |work=tagesschau.de |date=4 August 2025 |language=de}}</ref> or [[post-democracy|post-democratic]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Zarrelli |first1=Patrick |title=Peter Thiel Isn't Anti-Democracy, He's Post-Democracy |url=https://sfl.media/peter-thiel-isnt-anti-democracy-hes-post-democracy/ |work=South Florida Media |date=26 August 2025}}</ref> French economist [[Yann Algan]] links Peter Thiel and Elon Musk to the concept of "liquid democracy" and the rise of libertarian AI governance, which Algan defines as "a radically decentralized, algorithm-driven democracy", which "prioritizes efficiency and individual freedom over democratic safeguards".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Algan |first1=Yann |last2=Babinet |first2=Gillet |title=AI Must Be Governed Democratically to Preserve Our Future |url=https://www.hec.edu/en/knowledge/articles/ai-must-be-governed-democratically-preserve-our-future |website=HEC Paris |access-date=18 September 2025 |date=14 February 2025}}</ref>
Thiel's biographer Max Chafkin notes that his thinking is a mix of libertarianism and authoritarianism, but describes what Thiel truly believes and wants as a mystery.<ref>{{cite news |title=The Black Box of Peter Thiel's Beliefs |url=https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2021/09/20/peter-thiel-book-facebook-trump-jd-vance-blake-masters-josh-hawley-513121 |work=POLITICO |date=20 September 2021}}</ref>

Thiel describes himself as a political atheist.<ref name="Schuessler"/> He opines that trying to radically alter the current U.S. government is unrealistic. He also suggests that [[Curtis Yarvin]] methods will lead to Xi's China or Putin's Russia.<ref name="Gellman1"/> He does not deny the value of statesmanship though,<ref>{{cite web |last1=Thiel |first1=Peter |title=The Straussian Moment |url=https://gwern.net/doc/politics/2007-thiel.pdf |date=2007|access-date=22 October 2025}}</ref>{{refn|group=N|Peter Thiel: "But also there cannot be a decision to avoid all decisions and to retreat into studying the Bible in anticipation of the Second Coming, for then one will have ceased to be a statesman or stateswoman."{{sfn|Thiel|2007|p=214}}}} but opines that "people should spend less time trying to change the system than simply creating things outside it".<ref name="Schuessler"/>

Journalist Murad Ahmed from ''[[Financial Times]]'' calls Thiel "philosopher king at the very top of Silicon Valley" (with ''[[France 24]]'' using a similar description).<ref>{{cite news |title=Led by Musk, Silicon Valley inches to the right |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20240310-led-by-musk-silicon-valley-inches-to-the-right |work=France 24 |date=10 March 2024 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Ahmed |first1=Murad |last2=Tett |first2=Gillian |last3=Kinder |first3=Tabby |title=Transcript: Trump's tech bros — The enigma of Peter Thiel |url=https://www.ft.com/content/b9ec78ec-084b-44fb-9a91-c6f00d499617 |work=Financial Times |date=8 July 2025}}</ref> German philosopher [[Peter Sloterdijk]] also remarks: "Peter Thiel can be seen as more of a philosopher king. He acts very coolly and strategically{{snd}}a dazzling figure, far outside our left-liberal perception patterns",<ref>{{cite news |last1=Jakobs |first1=Hans-Jürgen |title='Ein herrschender Clown ist schöner als der Papst' |url=https://www.handelsblatt.com/politik/deutschland/peter-sloterdijk-ein-herrschender-clown-ist-schoener-als-der-papst/100089475.html |work=www.handelsblatt.com |date=23 November 2024 |quote=Eine Art Philosophenkönig ist vielmehr Peter Thiel. Er handelt sehr kühl und strategisch – eine schillernde Figur, weit außerhalb unserer linksliberalen Wahrnehmungsschemata.}}</ref> while [[Ross Douthat]] from ''New York Times'' describes him as "most influential right-wing intellectual of the last 20 years".{{sfn|Douthat|2025}} Commenting on Douthat's description, Luke Munn of the University of Queensland notes that, "Thiel's influence on politics is at once financial, technical and ideological [...] his potent cocktail of networks, money, strategy and support exerts a rightward force on the political landscape."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Munn |first1=Luke |title=Friday essay: libertarian tech titan Peter Thiel helped make JD Vance. The Republican kingmaker's influence is growing |url=https://theconversation.com/friday-essay-libertarian-tech-titan-peter-thiel-helped-make-jd-vance-the-republican-kingmakers-influence-is-growing-261856 |access-date=10 September 2025 |work=The Conversation |date=31 July 2025}}</ref>

In 2025, the author {{ill|Ijoma Mangold|de}} wrote an article for ''[[Die Zeit]]'', describing Thiel's theories as obscure and incoherent at first glance, argues he often displays an accurate "intuition", while noting that both the man and his ideas "simultaneously fascinates, repels, and outrages."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Mangold |first1=Ijoma |title=Peter Thiel: Eine Milliarde Ideen |url=https://www.zeit.de/kultur/2025-07/peter-thiel-paypal-palantir-unternehmen-tech-milliardaer |work=Die Zeit |date=27 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250727102006/https://www.zeit.de/kultur/2025-07/peter-thiel-paypal-palantir-unternehmen-tech-milliardaer |archive-date=27 July 2025 |url-status=live |language=de-DE}}</ref> Subsequently the author René Martens, writing for ''[[Mitteldeutscher Rundfunk]]'', criticized Mangold and ''Die Zeit'' for masking their admiration with pseudo-criticism and called Thiel a disciple of Nazi-supporter [[Carl Schmitt]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Martens |first1=René |title=Kolumne: Das Altpapier am 28. Juli 2025 – Wir sind nicht in Geiselhaft, wir sind die Geiselnehmer {{!}} MDR.DE |url=https://www.mdr.de/altpapier/das-altpapier-4262.html |work=www.mdr.de |date=28 July 2025 |language=de}}</ref>

In 2009, ''[[The Guardian]]'' stated that Thiel was a member of the web-based organization TheVanguard, a [[Neoconservatism|neoconservative]] pressure group founded in opposition to the progressive organization [[MoveOn]]. The outlet said Thiel believes the [[Age of Enlightenment|Enlightenment]] led humanity from nature's rule to a world where nature has been conquered, and also noted Thiel's philosophy disregarded art, beauty, love, pleasure, and truth.<ref name="Hodgkinson"/>

''The Guardian'' linked Thiel's investment in projects like the Singularity Institute to his belief in life-extension technologies as an escape from humanity's "nasty, brutish, and short" life. It criticized him for seeking to replace the natural world with a virtual one.<ref name="Hodgkinson"/>

Vadym Kovalenko notes that during the 90s and 2000s, Silicon Valley followed the spirit of [[Steve Jobs]], who saw technology as art. But later this has translated into Thielism, which emphasizes "truth, the ideal, ontology" and matters like flying to Mars, curing aging and creating a new world over the superficiality. Kovalenko sees Thiel as a humanitarian Über-artist.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Kovalenko |first1=Vadym |title=The Ideal World of Peter Thiel |url=https://resurgamhub.org/free-people-thoughts/vadym-kovalenko/the-ideal-world-of-peter-thiel |website=resurgamhub.org |language=en}}</ref>

On the question of exotericism versus esotericism, Paul Leslie writes that in "The Straussian moment", Thiel tries to "weave together Schmitt's political theology—with its emphasis on the friend/enemy distinction—and [[Leo Strauss|Strauss]]'s advocacy for esoteric wisdom and hidden hierarchies."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Leslie |first1=Paul |title=From Philosophy To Power |url=https://salmagundi.skidmore.edu/articles/1176-from-philosophy-to-power |website=Salmagundi Magazine |access-date=12 September 2025 |language=en}}</ref> In the article "Exotericism and the Untroubled Race for the Future", Thiel discerns between ancient esotericism, in which "thrice-great Hermes revealed his magical recipes only to a few" and "modern esotericism of grantwriting". He remarks, though, that exotericism takes time, and [[Johann Wolfgang von Goethe|Goethe]] was "perhaps [...] the last human being to command the sum total of human knowledge."<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Thiel |first1=Peter |title=Exotericism and the Untroubled Race for the Future |journal=Perspectives on Political Science |date=2 October 2015 |volume=44 |issue=4 |pages=221–222 |doi=10.1080/10457097.2015.1080088 |url=https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/10457097.2015.1080088 |issn=1045-7097|url-access=subscription }}</ref>

Writing for the ''[[Quarterly Journal of Speech]]'' in 2024, James Rushing Daniel wrote that:<ref name="Daniel 2025">{{Cite journal|last1=Daniel|first1=James Rushing|date=2025|title=Rewriting the plan of the world: Peter Thiel's messianic rhetoric and the end of progressive neoliberalism|url=https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00335630.2024.2340046#abstract|journal=Quarterly Journal of Speech|volume=111|issue=2|access-date=September 10, 2025|pages=272–295|issn=0033-5630|doi=10.1080/00335630.2024.2340046|url-access=subscription}}</ref>

{{blockquote|(...) "a rhetor ambitiously capitalizing on the material crises and political disillusionment of the day, defending a "cultural revolution" to put an end not just to the progressivism of the long 1990s but the values of collectivism and social justice and the remnants of social democracy and the Keynesian welfare state, replacing them with Randian individualism and the absolute dominance of the capitalist project."<ref name="Daniel 2025"/>}}

According to Daniel, Thiel has financially supported the intellectual wing of "the reactionary, traditionalist turn of conservative politics" termed by some as "the [[New Right]]".<ref name="Daniel 2025"/> ''[[The Nation]]'' notes that he advocates "for a dramatic, right-wing political turn to address technological stagnation".<ref name="Heer 06302025"/>

[[Nick Land]] attributed Thiel's 2009 essay "The Education of a Libertarian" and statement that "I no longer believe that freedom and democracy are compatible" as a watershed moment in the development of the [[Dark Enlightenment]] movement.<ref name="Daniel 2025"/> Patrick Zarrelli argues the quote is misread as anti-democratic, when Thiel's real concern is that mass democracy could erode the freedoms essential for innovation, but notes that Thiel underestimates the limits of technocracy like lack of democratic accountability. Zarelli remarks that Thiel has partially realized his philosophy: "By aligning technology with national priorities like defense modernization, pandemic response, and intelligence fusion. He has built parallel governance inside the state itself.", and notes that critics call Thiel a "shadow [[Business oligarch|oligarch]]". Zarelli opines that a solution might be a hybrid form between technocracy and democracy.{{sfn|Zarrelli|2025}}

Italian professor [[Giuliano da Empoli]] opines that Thiel represents the alliance between the post-modern Silicon Valley and the archaic Trump, that threatens democracy. The author recognizes that the Silicon Valley actors are gifted and have the means to govern more efficiently than democratic institutions in some respects. He argues that humanity must not respond to post-modern tech leaders like the Aztecs did to the conquistadors, but must instead make deliberate choices about which areas should still prioritize democratic decision-making, even at the risk of less efficient outcomes. In his book ''L'Empire de l'ombre'', Da Empoli echoes the sentiment of Thiel's quote, "Darker questions still emerge in these dusky final weeks of our interregnum," interpreting the "apocalypse" not as the end of the world, but as a sudden unveiling of forces that had long been taking shape beneath the surface.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Hesse |first1=Michael |title=Giuliano da Empoli – "Unser Verständnis der Realität zerbricht" |url=https://www.fr.de/kultur/gesellschaft/giuliano-da-empoli-unser-verstaendnis-der-realitaet-zerbricht-93956879.html |work=www.fr.de |date=26 September 2025 |language=de}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Malik |first1=Matheo |title=L'apocalypse de Donald Trump selon Peter Thiel |url=https://legrandcontinent.eu/fr/2025/01/10/lapocalypse-de-donald-trump-selon-peter-thiel/ |work=Le Grand Continent |date=10 January 2025 |language=fr-FR}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Malik |first1=Matheo |title=Face à l'Empire de l'ombre, une conversation avec Giuliano da Empoli |url=https://legrandcontinent.eu/fr/2025/04/17/lempire-de-lombre-giuliano-da-empoli/ |work=Le Grand Continent |date=17 April 2025 |language=fr-FR}}</ref>

[[Blue Labour]] founder [[Maurice Glasman]] (who first met Thiel at Oxford, where Glasman rebuked Thiel's description of the [[British Empire]] as the Antichrist) denounces Thiel's view on democracy but defends leftist politicians' interaction with Thiel, saying that parties which have no place in the AI conversation will be out of the game very fast.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Rodgers |first1=Sienna |title=Maurice Glasman On Nigel Farage, Peter Thiel and Shabana Mahmood |url=https://www.politicshome.com/news/article/lord-glasman-i-want-see-muslims-outside-synagogues-protecting-jews |work=Politics Home |date=17 October 2025 |language=en}}</ref> Danish politician {{ill|Christopher Arzrouni|da}} dismisses ''[[Dagbladet Information]]'''s description of Thiel as a Prussian warhorse (''preussisk kamphest'') or a bigot tech prince who would bring the end of democracy or the world, calling him "a smart European who finds better opportunities in the U.S.", and criticizes European intellectuals' fear of new technology.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Folketingskandidat |first1=Skrevet af: Christopher Arzrouni |last2=Alliance |first2=Liberal |title=Peter Thiel er ikke den skurk, som Information vil gøre ham til |url=https://www.information.dk/debat/2025/10/peter-thiel-skurk-information-goere |work=Information |date=29 October 2025 |language=da}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Dressler-Bredsdorff |first1=Skrevet af: Matthias |title=Den mest indflydelsesrige intellektuelle på USA's højrefløj er hovedrig og frygter Antikrists genkomst |url=https://www.information.dk/moti/2025/09/mest-indflydelsesrige-intellektuelle-paa-usas-hoejrefloej-hovedrig-frygter-antikrists-genkomst |work=Information |date=26 September 2025 |language=da}}</ref>

Jacob Silverman noted that Thiel's actual political work drifted away from libertarianism, but it remained his intellectual guiding star.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Silverman |first1=Jacob |title=Gilded Rage: Elon Musk and the Radicalization of Silicon Valley |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=AAiIEQAAQBAJ&pg=PA105 |publisher=Bloomsbury Publishing |date=9 October 2025 |isbn=978-1-3994-1999-4 |language=en}}</ref> Jack Nicastro of ''[[Reason (magazine)|Reason]]'' notes that Thiel's solution for "the dangers of government overreach and a one-world state" is "surprisingly libertarian".<ref>{{cite news |last1=Nicastro |first1=Jack |title=I listened to over 7 hours of Peter Thiel's leaked Antichrist lectures. They're surprisingly libertarian. |url=https://reason.com/2025/10/14/i-listened-to-over-7-hours-of-peter-thiels-leaked-antichrist-lectures-theyre-surprisingly-libertarian/ |work=Reason.com |date=14 October 2025}}</ref>

George A. Dunn believes that Thiel is the pathbreaker in connecting the thoughts of [[René Girard|Girard]] and [[Leo Strauss|Strauss]] to debates on the origins of [[Modern philosophy|modernity]].<ref>{{cite encyclopedia |last= Dunn|first=George A.|editor-last1=Dunn |editor-first1=George A. |editor-last2=Telli |editor-first2=Mango |contribution=The Collapsing Ladder of Degree: René Girard and Leo Strauss on the Origins of Modernity|title=A New Politics for Philosophy: Perspectives on Plato, Nietzsche, and Strauss |date=16 November 2022 |publisher=Bloomsbury Publishing PLC |isbn=978-1-4985-7733-5 |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=i3ufEAAAQBAJ&pg=PA276 |language=en}}</ref>

=== Political views ===
{{Libertarianism US|intellectuals}}
Thiel is a self-described [[conservative libertarian]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.politicslaw.org/peter-thiel-technology-globalization-economy/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130506063307/http://www.politicslaw.org/peter-thiel-technology-globalization-economy/|url-status=dead|archive-date=6 May 2013|title=Peter Thiel on the Role of Technology and Globalization in Our Economy|work=Politics Law & Economics Blog|first=Aaron|last=Street|date=2 March 2013|access-date=25 December 2013}}</ref> Since the late 2010s, he has espoused support for [[national conservatism]],<ref name="natcon">{{cite news|work=[[Reason (magazine)|Reason]]|title=Peter Thiel Explains the New 'National Conservatism'|date=17 July 2019|url=https://reason.com/2019/07/17/peter-thiel-explains-the-new-national-conservatism/|access-date=3 January 2020|archive-date=22 September 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190922034954/https://reason.com/2019/07/17/peter-thiel-explains-the-new-national-conservatism/|url-status=live}}</ref> and criticized [[economically liberal]] attitudes towards [[free trade]]<ref>{{cite magazine|magazine=[[The New Yorker]]|title=Peter Thiel's Oddly Conventional Defense of Trump|date=1 November 2016|url=https://www.newyorker.com/business/currency/peter-thiels-oddly-conventional-defense-of-trump|access-date=3 January 2020|archive-date=16 April 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200416091120/https://www.newyorker.com/business/currency/peter-thiels-oddly-conventional-defense-of-trump|url-status=live}}</ref> and [[Big Tech]].<ref name="natcon" />
Thiel advocates that companies should avoid competition and attention, and try to develop into monopolies by creating something new, dominate a niche market before expanding into slightly broader markets. He notes that years or even decades of profits can come from such specific markets.<ref>{{cite news |title=Tech in Asia - Connecting Asia's startup ecosystem |url=https://www.techinasia.com/3-steps-building-monopoly-peter-thiel |access-date=5 June 2025 |work=www.techinasia.com}}</ref>

In ''The Straussian Moment'', Thiel notes that, "Since 1920, the vast increase in welfare beneficiaries and the extension of the franchise to women{{snd}}two constituencies that are notoriously tough for libertarians{{snd}}have rendered the notion of 'capitalist democracy' into an oxymoron." After the statement caused controversies, he replied that, he had made a "commonplace statistical observation about voting patterns that is often called the gender gap", and that women's right to vote was not under siege nor would taking it away solve any problem, but people should focus on projects outside of voting and politics.<ref name=":3">{{Cite news |date=2009-04-13 |title=The Education of a Libertarian |url=https://www.cato-unbound.org/2009/04/13/peter-thiel/education-libertarian |access-date=2023-05-01 |website=Cato Unbound |language=en |archive-date=29 April 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130429131334/http://www.cato-unbound.org/2009/04/13/peter-thiel/the-education-of-a-libertarian/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Adam Rogers contends that this essay has prefigured the [[Department of Government Efficiency]] project.<ref>{{Cite web| last = Rogers| first = Adam| title = From DEI to DOGE: how Peter Thiel foresaw the future| work = Business Insider| access-date = 2025-03-31| url = https://www.businessinsider.com/godfather-of-doge-peter-thiel-elon-musk-government-funding-cuts-2025-2}}</ref>

In a 2015 conversation with [[Tyler Cowen]], Thiel claimed that innovative breakthroughs were happening in [[computing]]/[[Information Technology|IT]] and not the physical world. He lamented the lack of progress in space travel, high-speed transit, and medical devices. As a cause for the discrepancy, he said: "I would say that we lived in a world in which bits were unregulated and atoms were regulated."<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/peter-thiel-tech-innovation-is-outpacing-everything-else-for-a-simple-reason-2015-4 |title=Peter Thiel says tech innovation is outpacing everything else for one simple reason |work=[[Business Insider]] |date=8 April 2015 |access-date=27 September 2019 |first=Drake |last=Baer |archive-date=16 April 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200416093805/https://www.businessinsider.com/peter-thiel-tech-innovation-is-outpacing-everything-else-for-a-simple-reason-2015-4?r=US&IR=T |url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2021, Thiel wrote an article for ''[[Die Welt]]'', claiming that the extreme political experiments of fascism and communism in the 20th century had led Germany to fear extremism in both politics and technology. However, as "the decisive arena for the future of the West", being the land of poets and thinkers would not be enough for Germany in the new era. He criticized "green quietism" and opined that new ideas could be dangerous but would be the source of growth.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Thiel |first1=Peter |title=Poesie reicht nicht, die Welt braucht deutsche Ideen |url-status=live |url=https://www.welt.de/kultur/plus234258474/Investor-Peter-Thiel-Poesie-reicht-nicht-die-Welt-braucht-deutsche-Ideen.html |access-date=20 August 2025 |work=Die Welt |date=11 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211012130839/https://www.welt.de/kultur/plus234258474/Investor-Peter-Thiel-Poesie-reicht-nicht-die-Welt-braucht-deutsche-Ideen.html |archive-date=12 October 2021 |language=de}}</ref>

In the 2025 Douthat interview, Thiel stated that, "Reagan was consumer capitalism, which is oxymoronic. You don't save money as a capitalist; you borrow money. And Obama was low-tax socialism{{snd}}just as oxymoronic as the consumerist capitalism of Reagan."{{sfn|Douthat|2025}}

Thiel prefers a small state, for which he cites Singapore as a good example, which is between the model of France (big state) and Somalia (no state).<ref>{{cite news |title=Peter Thiel, Pierre Manent. Et si la vérité était scandaleuse ? {{!}} Philosophie magazine |url=https://www.philomag.com/articles/peter-thiel-pierre-manent-et-si-la-verite-etait-scandaleuse |work=www.philomag.com |date=25 September 2014 |language=fr}}</ref>
<ref>{{cite news |title=Quote of the day by Peter Thiel: I no longer believe that freedom and democracy are compatible |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/technology/tech-news/quote-of-the-day-by-peter-thiel-i-no-longer-believe-that-freedom-and-democracy-are-compatible/articleshow/132536901.cms |work=The Times of India |date=21 July 2026}}</ref> He criticizes California's wokeism and Saudi Arabia's wahhabism.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Hetzner |first1=Christiaan |title=Peter Thiel tells Joe Rogan his next move is either to Nashville or Miami to avoid California taxes |url=https://fortune.com/2024/08/19/peter-thiel-joe-rogan-california-taxes/ |work=Fortune |date=19 August 2024 |language=en}}</ref>

[[Klaus Schwab]], the [[World Economic Forum|WEF]]'s founder and originator of the theory of [[Inclusive capitalism|stakeholder capitalism]],<ref>{{cite book |last1=Congress |first1=International Federation of Commercial, Clerical, Professional, and Technical Employees World |title=Report on the ... World Congress |date=1995 |publisher=The Federation |page=50 |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=nVJZAAAAYAAJ |access-date=25 June 2026 |language=en}}</ref> calls what Thiel represents "tech-elite capitalism". According to Schwab, contrary to stakeholder capitalism, tech-elite capitalism emphasizes speed and innovation, creating a "quiet revolution" with explosive innovation that challenges democratic legal framework. Noting the reality that capital follows innovation and not vice versa, thus giving power to those who control innovation, Schwab opines that the tech elites need to be recognized but also given guidance and integration into the democratic order.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Schwab |first1=Klaus |title=Die Tech-Eliten und die stille Revolution der Macht: Der Unternehmer Peter Thiel steht für einen neuen, dramatisch vorwärtsdrängenden Kapitalismus. Überlebt die Demokratie die explosive Dynamik des technologischen Fortschritts? |url=https://weltwoche.ch/story/die-tech-eliten-und-die-stille-revolution-der-macht/ |work=Die Weltwoche |date=30 April 2026 |language=de}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Schwab |first1=Klaus |title=Commentary: The Tech Elites and the Quiet Revolution of Power - Caixin Global |url=https://www.caixinglobal.com/2026-05-20/commentary-the-tech-elites-and-the-quiet-revolution-of-power-102445828.html |work=www.caixinglobal.com |date=20 May 2026 |language=en}}</ref> Vatican advisor [[Paolo Benanti]] writes that Thiel's career is "a challenge to the very foundations of civil coexistence",  noting that innovation only becomes development if it serves everyone, and democracy is eroded when "one player controls the entire stack," from hardware to software. Benanti calls for the student and academic community to develop alternatives to parts of this stack.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Laborde |first1=Antonia |title=“La máquina nunca es tuya”: el asesor de IA del Vaticano que critica a Peter Thiel visita Chile |url=https://elpais.com/chile/2026-06-23/la-maquina-nunca-es-tuya-el-asesor-de-ia-del-vaticano-que-critica-a-peter-thiel-visita-chile.html |work=El País Chile |date=23 June 2026 |language=es-CL}}</ref> Italian scholar Andrea Venanzoni notes that Thiel is organically linked to almost all current tech companies, even those whose vision contrasts against his, like [[Anthropic]]. Venanzoni writes that technological innovation transforms geopolitical and diplomatic structures, pointing to Thiel's work in Argentina, which represents "parallel diplomacy" on behalf of the US but also accelerates innovation in the host country. Venanzoni urges the Italian government to approach Thiel without bias, in order to build up Italian innovation policy, without bowing to Washington.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Venanzoni |first1=Andrea |title=Lo scontro Meloni-Trump e le incomprensioni col mondo parallelo di Thiel e Musk |url=https://www.ilfoglio.it/esteri/2026/06/20/news/lo-scontro-meloni-trump-e-le-incomprensioni-col-mondo-parallelo-di-thiel-e-musk--400890 |work=www.ilfoglio.it |date=20 July 2026 |language=it}}</ref>

====On international relations====
The Founders Fund and Khosla Ventures are backers of the Hill & Valley Forum, a group that is described by the ''[[Wall Street Journal]]'' as an anti-China alliance between Silicon Valley and Capitol Hill.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Wells |first1=Georgia |title=Silicon Valley and Capitol Hill Build an Anti-China Alliance |url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/silicon-valley-and-capitol-hill-build-an-anti-china-alliance-e508c75e |url-status=live |access-date=6 August 2025 |work=Wall Street Journal |date=17 March 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230317131541/https://www.wsj.com/articles/silicon-valley-and-capitol-hill-build-an-anti-china-alliance-e508c75e |archive-date=17 March 2023 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Chapman |first1=Lizette |last2=Edgerton |first2=Anna |last3=Barinka |first3=Alex |title=China Hawks Dine on Seared Branzino And Lament Threat to US |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2023-03-23/china-hawks-dine-on-seared-branzino-and-lament-threat-to-us |access-date=6 August 2025}}</ref> In an article named ''Silicon soldiers of fortune'', the ''China Daily'', the channel of the Central Propaganda Department of the Chinese Communist Party,<ref>{{cite news |title=Chinese state media mocks Biden over "hysterical" reaction to spy balloon |url=https://www.newsweek.com/chinese-state-media-mocks-biden-reaction-spy-balloon-1780565 |access-date=7 August 2025 |work=Newsweek |date=11 February 2023 |language=en}}</ref> identifies Thiel, [[Palmer Luckey]] and [[Jacob Helberg]] as tech hawks who are increasingly shaping the US policy towards China.<ref>{{cite news |title=Silicon soldiers of fortune |url=https://epaper.chinadaily.com.cn/a/202503/26/WS67e347a6a310358b44fde34c.html |access-date=6 August 2025 |work=epaper.chinadaily.com.cn}}</ref> The ''[[Xinhua News Agency]]'', China's official state news agency,<ref>{{cite news |title=Trade war is about more than just trade, China's official news agency argues |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2025/05/11/xinhua-china-trade-position-00340489 |access-date=7 August 2025 |work=Politico |date=11 May 2025}}</ref> states that Palantir and its leaders like Thiel and Vice President Wendy R. Anderson as well as other companies like Anduril and Saronic Technologies, as representatives of "the new military industrial complex", are an unpredictable danger to the US and the international community.<ref>{{cite news |title=美国"新军工"企业玩转军政商"旋转门"-新华网 |url=http://www.news.cn/milpro/20250407/29cc02e8702e49878b44fcf87afd96ef/c.html |access-date=6 August 2025 |work=www.news.cn}}</ref> The tech-focused outlet ''[[36Kr]]'' though praises his long-term vision and methods in breaking down the traditional barriers in the US military-industrial complex and government sector, and his contribution to leading startups like Palantir, Anduril and SpaceX.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Jin Duan |title=The Media-Portrayed Palantir: Not the Real Deal |url=https://eu.36kr.com/en/p/3423362767870088 |work=eu.36kr.com |date=15 August 2025}}</ref> The Brazilian newspaper ''[[Brasil de Fato]]'' (described by ''[[The New York Times]]'' as part of a "global web of Chinese propaganda"<ref>{{cite news |last1=Hvistendahl |first1=Mara |last2=Fahrenthold |first2=David A. |last3=Chutel |first3=Lynsey |last4=Jhaveri |first4=Ishaan |title=A Global Web of Chinese Propaganda Leads to a U.S. Tech Mogul |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/05/world/europe/neville-roy-singham-china-propaganda.html |url-status=live |date=5 August 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260111052424/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/05/world/europe/neville-roy-singham-china-propaganda.html |archive-date= 2026-01-11}}</ref>) portrays Thiel as "the brightest anti-communist in the US", part of the anti-China brigade, "the leader of the tech-based section of the military-industrial complex" as well as "the most geo-politically strategic tech billionaire" and "the most dangerous non-state figure in the world today". According to ''Brasil de Fato'', among all the capitalists, Thiel has the strongest grip on the [[United States National Security Council|National Security Council]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Estanislau |first1=Lucas |title=Understanding Trump's Nationalist Conservative White Christian Agenda |url=https://www.brasildefato.com.br/2025/03/07/understanding-trumps-nationalist-conservative-white-christian-agenda/ |work=Brasil de Fato |date=7 March 2025}}</ref>

In 2019, Thiel called [[Google]] "seemingly treasonous" and urged a government investigation, citing Google's work with China and asking whether DeepMind or Google's senior management had been "infiltrated" by foreign intelligence agencies.<ref>{{Cite web |date=15 July 2019 |title=Peter Thiel Urges U.S. Probe of Google's 'Seemingly Treasonous' Acts |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2019-07-15/thiel-urges-u-s-probe-of-google-s-seemingly-treasonous-acts |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191031054144/https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2019-07-15/thiel-urges-u-s-probe-of-google-s-seemingly-treasonous-acts |archive-date=31 October 2019 |access-date=17 January 2020 |website=[[Bloomberg News]]}}</ref>

In 2025, Thiel called for a drastic reset in economic relations with China, stressing that economic relations should be viewed from a geopolitical standpoint as well.<ref>{{cite episode |title=Tariffs, DOGE & Fixing America: Peter Thiel's Skeptic Solutions |series=Joe Lonsdale: American Optimist |last=Lonsdale |first=Joe |date=17 April 2024 |publisher=Self-published}} Minute 26 – 28: "We really need a drastic reset with China [...] But it is the geopolitical rivalry in the background that the economists are never able to factor in properly with China."</ref> In a discussion with Peter Robinson, he opined that the US should not let itself be stuck between two extreme views about China (that China itself encourages to promote an attitude of political inaction towards them): "It's China is super weak, and China is super strong. And I've been in meetings in China where in some sense you got both messages within 20 minutes of one another, and it's like logically inconsistent but psychologically it doubles up."<ref>{{cite news |title=The World According to Thiel |url=https://www.hoover.org/research/peter-thiel-transcript |access-date=6 August 2025 |work=Hoover Institution |language=en}}</ref>

In 2024, Palantir became a strategic partner of Israel in military technology in an occasion both Thiel and Karp visited the country.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Newman |first1=Marissa |title=Thiel's Palantir, Israel Agree Strategic Partnership for Battle Tech |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-01-12/palantir-israel-agree-to-strategic-partnership-for-battle-tech |access-date=6 August 2025 |date=12 January 2024}}</ref> In a 2024 interview with [[Bari Weiss]], Thiel advocated cooperation with Israel to deter Iran from getting nuclear weapons:
{{blockquote|One of the lessons I take of the mid-20th century was every time a country got a nuclear weapon, we got a regional war. The Soviet Union gets the bomb in 1949. The Korean War starts in 1950 because when the Soviet Union backs North Korea, we can't bomb Russia. Then they can back North Korea with impunity, and we get a massive, massive regional war. That's, in a way, the price for being asleep at the switch and letting the Soviets get the bomb. 1964, Communist China gets the bomb. Vietnam War explodes in 1965. And again, China can back North Vietnam with impunity. We can't reciprocate. And the way I understand why would an Iranian nuclear bomb be a catastrophe? Because the degree to which Iran can support this plethora of bad actors, the Houthis, the Hamas people, and Hezbollah, and on and on throughout the Middle East, you could not retaliate against Iran [...] And so we don't have to go to the crazy theocracy that said they'd use the bomb and would use it.<ref name= "Weiss">{{cite news |last1=Weiss |first1=Bari |title=Peter Thiel and the Triumph of the Counter-Elites |url=https://www.thefp.com/p/peter-thiel-honestly-trump-jd-vance |access-date=6 August 2025 |work=[[The Free Press (Bari Weiss media)|The Free Press]] |date=2024-11-15 |language=en}}</ref>}}

Regarding the Russia-Ukraine war, he opined that "the relentless NATO expansion might not have been a good idea", but the US could not simply retreat from Ukraine, because it would become a rout.<ref name= "Weiss"/>

In 2025, writing for the Singapore-based think tank ThinkChina, Artyom Lukin, a leading Russian expert on Asia-Pacific geopolitical issues,<ref>{{cite web |title=Professor Artyom Lukin |url=https://www.internationalaffairs.org.au/aiia-authors/associate-professor-artyom-lukin/ |website=Australian Institute of International Affairs |access-date=20 August 2025}}</ref> wrote that Thiel, whom Lukin described as "the [[éminence grise]] of Trump's own deep state" and "the most anti-China figure in the US top elite", together with his allies, were pushing the American geostrategy towards focusing on China (a country Thiel saw as "a half fascist, half communist gerontocracy" with "a socialism of a nationalistic sort, and [...] extremely racist.") as the paramount threat. Lukin noted that Thiel had little sympathy for Russia, but viewed it as a lesser threat and did not want to push Moscow towards Beijing's arms.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Lukin |first1=Artyom |title=Was the Trump-Putin Alaska meeting about Ukraine — or China? |url=https://www.thinkchina.sg/politics/was-trump-putin-alaska-meeting-about-ukraine-or-china |website=ThinkChina - Big Reads, Opinions & Columns on China |access-date=20 August 2025 |language=en}}</ref>

According to ''[[The Intercept]]'', Thiel is the source of the warrior culture in Silicon Valley, one focused on an arms race with China, although the anti-China sentiment is found on both sides of the political spectrum.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Biddle |first1=Sam |title=Trump's Election Is Also a Win for Tech's Right-Wing 'Warrior Class' |url=https://theintercept.com/2024/11/17/tech-industry-trump-military-contracts/ |work=The Intercept |date=17 November 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241119022659/https://theintercept.com/2024/11/17/tech-industry-trump-military-contracts/ |url-status=live |archive-date=19 November 2024}}</ref> [[Alex Karp]] notes that Palantir has a warrior culture, which values excellence over money.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Burleigh |first1=Emma |title=Palantir CEO credits the company's $3.9 billion revenue projections to its 'warrior culture' |url=https://fortune.com/2025/05/06/palantir-ceo-alex-karp-warrior-culture-trump-administration-business-growth/ |work=Fortune |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251203212509/https://fortune.com/2025/05/06/palantir-ceo-alex-karp-warrior-culture-trump-administration-business-growth/ |archive-date= 2025-12-03|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Sun |first1=Jasmine |title=Stanford students used to chase jobs at Meta and Google. Now they want to work on defense |url=https://sfstandard.com/2025/03/12/stanford-students-want-in-on-the-military-tech-gold-rush/ |work=[[The San Francisco Standard]] |date=12 March 2025 |language=en}}</ref>

In 2026, Thiel said that by focusing on restricting just one side of the AI race between the US and China, [[Pope Leo XIV]] inadvertently acts as a Chinese agent.<ref>{{cite news |title=Peter Thiel: The pope is ‘working for the Chinese Communists’ by criticizing AI {{!}} CNN |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2026/07/02/us/peter-thiel-aspen-pope-china-ai-cec |work=CNN |date=2 July 2026 |language=en}}</ref> Swiss author {{ill|Giuseppe Gracia|de}} writes that Thiel "expects every American and European to side with the West in the race against China. Anything less would be treason", commenting that in the current atmostphere, this logic of objective necessity is limiting critical thinking.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Gracia |first1=Giuseppe |title=Das Diktat des Unvermeidlichen: wie mit Sachzwängen in der Politik Druck gemacht wird |url=https://www.nzz.ch/feuilleton/zeitgeschehen/das-diktat-des-unvermeidlichen-wie-mit-sachzwaengen-abweichende-stimmen-diffamiert-werden-ld.10015370 |work=Neue Zürcher Zeitung |date=15 July 2026 |language=de}}</ref>

=== Religious views ===
Thiel is a self-described [[Christianity|Christian]] and a promoter of [[René Girard]]'s [[fundamental anthropology|Christian anthropology]].<ref>{{cite web|first=Sean|last=Salai|url=http://americamagazine.org/content/all-things/faith-technology-qa-peter-thiel|title=Faith & Technology: Q&A with Peter Thiel|website=[[America (Jesuit magazine)|America]]|date=1 October 2014|access-date=16 August 2016|archive-date=3 September 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160903203712/http://americamagazine.org/content/all-things/faith-technology-qa-peter-thiel|url-status=live}}</ref> Girard, a [[Catholic Church|Catholic]], explained the role of sacrifice and the [[scapegoat mechanism]] in resolving social conflict, which appealed to Thiel as it offered a basis for his Christian faith without the [[Christian fundamentalism|fundamentalism]] of his parents.<ref>{{Cite news|last=Paul|first=Elie|title=America's Problem: Mimetic Desire|url=http://everythingthatrises.com/post/67695583821/americas-problem-mimetic-desire|newspaper=Everything That Rises|access-date=25 December 2013|archive-date=7 July 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180707231141/http://everythingthatrises.com/post/67695583821/americas-problem-mimetic-desire|url-status=live}}</ref> Thiel grew up in an [[Evangelicalism|evangelical]] household but, as of 2011, described his religious beliefs as "somewhat heterodox", stating: "I believe Christianity is true but I don't sort of feel a compelling need to convince other people of that."<ref name=newyorker/> According to Thiel, "Christianity for me is the anti-identity. Your identity is in Christ [...] and it's in that context we can figure out things about the world and truth [...] [Truth] is not a social construct."<ref name="vatortv"/> Thiel has participated in [[Veritas Forum]] events with the theologian [[N. T. Wright]] discussing religion, politics, and technology.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.veritas.org/reshaping-our-view-of-god/|title=Reshaping Our View of God|date=5 February 2016|website=The Veritas Forum|access-date=14 June 2019|archive-date=16 April 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200416093146/http://www.veritas.org/reshaping-our-view-of-god/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Anderson |first=Max |title=Peter Thiel, N.T. Wright On Technology, Hope, And The End Of Death |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/valleyvoices/2015/06/24/peter-thiel-n-t-wright-on-technology-hope-and-the-end-of-death/ |access-date=2023-05-01 |website=Forbes |language=en |archive-date=1 May 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230501015030/https://www.forbes.com/sites/valleyvoices/2015/06/24/peter-thiel-n-t-wright-on-technology-hope-and-the-end-of-death/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

Thiel believes that "[[wokeism]]" or "wokeness" is a type of secular religion, which he sees as both "anti-Christian" and "ultra-Christian", stating: "There’s no forgiveness, and you still have original sin, and you have all these bad things that happen in the past, the past is terrible, and you can never overcome it. But there surely is a religious interpretation of this. What happened is, let’s say, the church lost a certain amount of authority, but people didn’t become rationalist, atheist people; they went into this sort of Woke religion, which I would interpret as a certain, extreme form of Christianity."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Arnold |first1=Joshua |title=Is 'Woke Religion' an 'Extreme Form of Christianity'? |url=https://washingtonstand.com/commentary/is-woke-religion-an-extreme-form-of-christianity |work=washingtonstand.com |date=7 August 2024}}</ref><ref name="Minakov">{{cite journal |last1=Minakov |first1=Mykhailo |title=Freedom and Progress at the Dawn of the Age of Will |journal=Ideology and Politics Journal |date=5 July 2025 |volume=27 |issue=1 |pages=97–144 |doi=10.36169/2227-6068.2025.01.00005 |url=https://www.ideopol.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2.1.-Minakov.pdf}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=TOI World Desk |title=JD Vance's mentor Peter Thiel claims 'wokeness' is just hyper-Christianity: A billionaire's radical take on power and faith |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/jd-vances-mentor-peter-thiel-claims-wokeness-is-just-hyper-christianity-a-billionaires-radical-take-on-power-and-faith/articleshow/118560462.cms |work=The Times of India |date=25 February 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Weiss |first1=Bari |title=Weekend Listening: Peter Thiel Says We Have Bigger Problems Than Wokeness |url=https://www.thefp.com/p/peter-thiel-donald-trump-desantis-ai-tiktok-woke?hide_intro_popup=true |work=www.thefp.com |language=en}}</ref> He claims that this strand of thinking, which attacks Christians for not doing enough for victims or the poor, is a continuation of communism and the social gospel, which also inherit some Christian characteristics while being anti-Christian at the same time.<ref name="vatortv">{{cite news |last1=Loeb |first1=Steven |title=Peter Thiel talks democracy, religion, freedom, and woke culture with Bambi Francisco |url=https://vator.tv/2021-11-02-peter-thiel-talks-democracy-religion-freedom-and-woke-culture-with-bambi-francisco/ |work=vator.tv |date=2 November 2021}}</ref> [[Mikhail Minakov]] writes that "Thiel's conception of will integrates Christian eschatology, Girardian mimetic theory, and Straussian elitism to critique the impotence of liberal democracy while proposing the efficiency of a techno-feudal alternative."<ref name="Minakov"/> Elke Schwarz, a professor of political theory, notes that Peter Thiel and [[Marc Andreessen]] are the foremost proponents of techno-eschatology, which demonstrates the sacralizing of AI and uses spiritualism to bolster the logic of venture capitalism.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Schwarz |first1=Elke |title=Conjuring the End: Techno-eschatology and the Power of Prophecy |url=https://opiniojuris.org/2025/01/30/conjuring-the-end-techno-eschatology-and-the-power-of-prophecy/ |website=Opinio Juris |date=30 January 2025}}</ref> Thiel opines that, "Crypto is decentralizing, AI is centralizing. Or, if you want to frame it more ideologically, crypto is libertarian and AI is communist."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Primack |first1=Dan |title=Peter Thiel: AI is communist |url=https://www.axios.com/2018/02/13/peter-thiel-ai-is-communist-1518541570 |access-date=27 September 2025 |work=Axios |date=13 February 2018 |language=en}}</ref>

A topic Thiel is interested in is the [[Antichrist]], [[Armageddon]] and [[Apocalypse]], about which he has given talks in multiple events, including a September 2025 series of off-the-record private lectures organized by the Acts 17 Collective in San Francisco,<ref name="Thiel Antichrist 2025-08-27">{{Cite web|date=2025-08-27|title=Palantir co-founder Peter Thiel to lead 4-part series on the Antichrist|url=https://www.christianpost.com/news/palantir-ceo-peter-thiel-to-lead-4-part-series-on-the-antichrist.html|url-status=live|website=[[The Christian Post]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250827194017/https://www.christianpost.com/news/palantir-ceo-peter-thiel-to-lead-4-part-series-on-the-antichrist.html|archive-date=2025-08-27}}</ref><ref name="dwnar">{{cite news |last1=Borrud |first1=Gabriel |last2=Agius |first2=Matthew Ward |last3=Dillon |first3=Conor |title=Pay attention to Peter Thiel's narrative – DW – 07/04/2025 |url=https://www.dw.com/en/pay-attention-to-peter-thiels-narrative/audio-73155264 |work=dw.com |date=7 April 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref name="bloombergchafkin">{{cite news |last1=Chafkin |first1=Max |title=Peter Thiel Tries On the Antichrist for Size |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2025-09-09/peter-thiel-s-antichrist-lectures-are-a-safe-move-for-the-palantir-billionaire |work=Bloomberg.com |date=9 September 2025 |language=en}}</ref> which drew a group of protesters.<ref name="sfs-16sep2025">{{cite news |last1=Shugerman |first1=Emily |last2=Leahy |first2=Garrett |title=What the hell happened at Peter Thiel's Antichrist talk? We asked the guests |url=https://sfstandard.com/2025/09/16/peter-thiel-antichrist-san-francisco/ |access-date=September 16, 2025 |work=[[The San Francisco Standard]] |date=September 16, 2025}}</ref> Thiel opines that different people are worried about different apocalyptic threats like environment degradation, nuclear wars or bioweapons. He recognizes these as credible threats, but sees a total [[One-world government conspiracy|one-world government]] as closer to the Antichrist.<ref name="Klein">{{cite news |last1=Klein |first1=Naomi |last2=Taylor |first2=Astra |title=The rise of end times fascism |url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2025/apr/13/end-times-fascism-far-right-trump-musk |work=The Guardian |date=13 April 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Thiel |first1=Peter |title=Peter Thiel on Political Theology (Ep. 210) |url=https://conversationswithtyler.com/episodes/peter-thiel-political-theology/ |date=7 July 2018}}</ref> He sees humanity as facing the double threats of the Antichrist and the Armageddon, which is the collapse of civilization through global warfare. He sees salvation in the figure of the [[Katechon]], a mysterious force that restrains the Antichrist.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Christensen |first1=Michael |title=Antichrist or Armageddon? Peter Thiel rethinks apocalypse from Silicon Valley. |url=https://religionnews.com/2025/09/09/antichrist-or-armageddon-peter-thiel-rethinks-apocalypse-from-silicon-valley/ |work=RNS |date=9 September 2025}}</ref><ref name="Schiffer">{{cite news |last1=Schiffer |first1=Christian |title=Peter Thiels apokalyptischer Plan für Amerika |url=https://www.br.de/nachrichten/netzwelt/peter-thiels-apokalyptischer-plan-fuer-amerika,UoYDolu |work=BR24 |date=19 June 2025 |language=de}}</ref> He has referred to individuals, organizations, communism or even anti-tech regulations as precursors of the Antichrist.<ref name="Schiffer"/><ref name="Klein"/><ref name="Duran">{{cite magazine |last1=Duran |first1=Gil |title=What's Up With Peter Thiel's Obsession With the Antichrist? |url=https://newrepublic.com/article/200471/peter-thiel-obsession-antichrist-religion |magazine=The New Republic}}</ref><ref name="bloombergchafkin"/> For example, he referred to environmental activist [[Greta Thunberg]] and AI safety advocate [[Eliezer Yudkowsky]] as "legionnaires of the Antichrist".<ref name="Guardian">{{cite news|last1=Bhuiyan|first1=Johana|last2=Kerr|first2=Dara |last3=obins-Early|first3=Nick |title=Inside tech billionaire Peter Thiel's off-the-record lectures about the antichrist|url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/oct/10/peter-thiel-lectures-antichrist|magazine=The Guardian |date=10 October 2025|access-date=7 February 2026}}</ref><ref name="Fortune">{{cite magazine |last1=Lichtenberg|first1=Nick |title=Peter Thiel warns the Antichrist and apocalypse are linked to the 'end of modernity' currently happening—and cites Greta Thunberg as a driving example|url=https://fortune.com/2026/02/04/peter-thiel-antichrist-greta-thunberg-end-of-modernity-billionaires/|magazine=Fortune|date=4 February 2026|access-date=7 February 2026}}</ref> Different commentators see his Antichrist theory as a narrative to highlight the role of a hero,<ref name="dwnar"/> or a framework to attack political opponents<ref name="Duran"/> or an attempt to brand himself as tech's free thinker (who has also touched on topics such as the Kennedy assassination, Epstein's crimes or aliens).<ref name="bloombergchafkin"/> German scholar [[Adrian Daub]], Professor of German and Comparative Literature at Stanford University, describes the lectures as "amateurish talks" and a desperate effort from a man with immense power and full of contradiction to disassociate himself from his own power and even his attempts to be understood.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Daub |first1=Adrian |title=Peter Thiel's off-the-record antichrist lectures reveal more about him than Armageddon |url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/ng-interactive/2025/oct/10/peter-thiel-antichrist-lectures |work=The Guardian |date=10 October 2025}}</ref> Professor Matthew Avery Sutton, representing the [[Washington State University]], accepts that Thiel's interest in Christianity is sincere, and that he draws from serious sources, but suggests that leaders should stop dressing their political theories in apocalyptic dress, because this will "raise anxieties, delegitimize compromise and insinuate that democratic deliberation is spiritually suspect".<ref>{{cite news |last1=Sutton |first1=Matthew Avery |title=The antichrist has long haunted American politics. Now it's rearing its head again |url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2025/oct/13/antichrist-peter-thiel-michigan |work=The Guardian |date=13 October 2025}}</ref> Publishing the transcript for some of Thiel's lectures about antichrist, ''The Guardian'' contended that Thiel's arguments are self-contradictory.<ref name="Guardian"/>

Theologian and Vatican official [[Antonio Spadaro|Antonio Spatareo (Spadaro)]] writes that Thiel's theory cannot be dismissed as mere "capitalist propaganda disguised as theology", but considers it "political theology at the service of a power project". Spatareo notes that the theory is erudite and with genuine concerns for current problems, but lacks a Christian core.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Spatareo |first1=Antonio |title=Peter Thiel e la tecno-teologia {{!}} Centro Brera |url=https://www.centrobrera.com/scheda/peter-thiel-e-la-tecno-teologia-antonio-spatareo |work=www.centrobrera.com |date=11 March 2026 |language=it}}</ref> [[Paolo Benanti]] opines that Thiel's vision of time is "tragically cyclic – and therefore [[Paganism|pagan]]", while noting that Palantir plays a central role, as "the House of Solomon" in this vision, which reflects Thiel's "political heresy": "on one hand, he finances the centrifugal forces that erode the nation-state; on the other, he arms the state to establish panoptic control."<ref name="Benanti"/> Citing Spadaro, ''[[Libero (newspaper)|Libero Quotidiano]]'' notes that contrary to what some newspapers report, the Vatican does not demonize Thiel, but tries to maintain a dialogue with him, who "represents the technological and financial powers of AI and the current American administration."<ref name="libero"/> ''Der Standard'' writes that Thiel does not use the term "Antichrist" and "Katechon" in the religious sense, but in the political sense: the Antichrist represents a "boundless global order" while the Katechon delays decay but is itself an authoritarian force.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Sulzbacher |first1=Markus |title=Der "Antichrist" im Wiener Hotel: Peter Thiel kommt zu den Festwochen |url=https://www.derstandard.at/story/3000000321886/der-antichrist-im-wiener-hotel-peter-thiel-kommt-zu-den-festwochen |work=DER STANDARD |date=22 May 2026 |language=de-AT}}</ref>

=== Political activism ===
{{Conservatism US|activists}}

Thiel is a member of the Steering Committee of the [[Bilderberg Group]],<ref>{{Cite web |url-status=live |date=1 May 2021|title=Steering Committee |url=https://www.bilderbergmeetings.org/background/steering-committee/steering-committee|access-date=1 May 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210501064333/https://www.bilderbergmeetings.org/background/steering-committee/steering-committee|archive-date=1 May 2021}}</ref> a gathering of intellectual figures, political leaders, and business executives,<ref>{{cite news|last1=Cadwalladr|first1=Carole|title=Peter Thiel: 'We attribute too much to luck. Luck is an atheistic word for God'|access-date=21 September 2014|work=[[The Observer]]|url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2014/sep/21/peter-thiel-paypal-luck-atheist-god|date=21 September 2014|page=8|archive-date=21 September 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140921092107/http://www.theguardian.com/technology/2014/sep/21/peter-thiel-paypal-luck-atheist-god|url-status=live}}</ref> characterized as focused on defense and espionage,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Skelton |first1=Charlie |title=Bilderberg Group changes itself for the modern world – and return of Trump |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/dec/25/jens-stoltenberg-bilderberg-group-trump-presidency |work=The Guardian |date=25 December 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241225122149/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/dec/25/jens-stoltenberg-bilderberg-group-trump-presidency |url-status=live |archive-date=25 December 2024}}</ref> as well as Atlanticist and Europhile.<ref>{{cite book |last1=Richardson |first1=Ian |last2=Kakabadse |first2=Andrew |last3=Kakabadse |first3=Nada |title=Bilderberg People: Elite Power and Consensus in World Affairs |date=3 July 2013 |publisher=Routledge |isbn=978-1-136-66465-6 |pages=108, 109 |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=8papAgAAQBAJ&pg=PA108 |language=en}}</ref> Thiel's outsized influence at the gathering has been noted.<ref>{{cite news |last1=BORNO |first1=HANNAH |title=Wes Streeting mixes with tech billionaires at Bilderberg summit |url=https://www.declassifieduk.org/wes-streeting-mixes-with-tech-billionaires-at-bilderberg-summit/ |access-date=9 August 2025 |work=Declassified UK |date=17 June 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Thiel assume papel de Kissinger na cena política? |url=https://diario.dopovo.com.br/2025/06/12/thiel-assume-papel-de-kissinger-na-cena-politica/ |access-date=9 August 2025 |date=12 June 2025 |language=pt-BR}}</ref> Thiel, together with [[Auren Hoffman]], is also the founder of [[Dialog (organization)|Dialog]], which is often compared to Bilderberg, but focuses more on tech. It does not share the lists of participants but is known to have invited American tech and political leaders, as well as intellectual heavyweights, on both sides of the political spectrum, as well as representatives from Europe and Middle East. Past topics included "AI's energy demands, the future of health care, and political realignments" and "caring for aging parents, love, mental health and the afterlife."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Allen |first1=Mike |title=Scoop: Dialog, a secretive forum, plans D.C.-area campus |url=https://www.axios.com/2025/08/07/dialog-secret-network-thiel-hoffman |access-date=9 August 2025 |work=Axios |date=7 August 2025 |language=en}}</ref> Palantir is partner of the [[World Economic Forum]], but Thiel has not gone to the meeting since 2013, because he considers it a place without individuals – there are only representatives of companies, governments and NGOs. He opines that some types of global governance might work, but it is necessary to have dissenting views.<ref>{{cite news |title=Make Ticker Tape Parades Great Again: A Conversation with Peter Thiel |url=https://www.hoover.org/research/make-ticker-tape-parades-great-again-conversation-peter-thiel-0 |access-date=8 August 2025 |work=Hoover Institution |date=17 December 2021 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Partners Palantir Technologies |url=https://www.weforum.org/organizations/palantir-technologies/?gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=22234048793&gbraid=0AAAAAoVy5F5baKfPlm5YUl3OneZaAgTZL&gclid=Cj0KCQjwndHEBhDVARIsAGh0g3Bvq05eQOAT_rZo6S5aTOcsnYhilmXONrZnobAe2P089V3YgFUKGXAaAhJOEALw_wcB |website=weforum.org|access-date=8 August 2025}}</ref>

The Thiel Foundation is a supporter of the [[Committee to Protect Journalists]] (CPJ), which promotes the right of journalists to report the news freely without fear of reprisal.<ref>{{cite web|author=Supporters of Press Freedom|title=Supporters of Press Freedom – About CPJ – Committee to Protect Journalists|url=http://www.cpj.org/about/current-supporters.php|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100902214457/http://www.cpj.org/about/current-supporters.php|archive-date=2 September 2010|access-date=16 October 2010|publisher=Cpj.org}}</ref> Beginning in 2008, Thiel has donated over $1&nbsp;million to the CPJ.<ref>{{cite book|last=Holiday|first=Ryan|author-link=Ryan Holiday|title=Conspiracy: Peter Thiel, Hulk Hogan, Gawker, and the Anatomy of Intrigue|date=2018|publisher=Penguin Books|isbn=978-0-7352-1766-9|page=45}}</ref> He is also a supporter of the [[Human Rights Foundation]], which organizes the [[Oslo Freedom Forum]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Freedom Project page on Thiel Foundation website|url=http://thielfoundation.org/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=1&Itemid=8|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120525072242/http://thielfoundation.org/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=1&Itemid=8|archive-date=25 May 2012|access-date=8 June 2012}}</ref><ref name="thestreet">{{Cite news |date=2018-10-17 |title=Peter Thiel Urges Investing in Human Rights |newspaper=Thestreet |url=https://www.thestreet.com/personal-finance/peter-thiel-urges-investing-in-human-rights-11154811 |url-status=live |access-date=2023-05-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181017123543/https://www.thestreet.com/story/11154811/1/peter-thiel-urges-investing-in-human-rights.html |archive-date=17 October 2018 }}</ref> In 2011 he was a featured speaker at the Oslo Freedom Forum, and the Thiel Foundation was one of the event's main sponsors.<ref name="thestreet" /> He also backs the [[Alliance of Democracies Foundation]] founded by [[Anders Fogh Rasmussen]].<ref>{{cite web |title=OLFI - Kontroversielt amerikansk firma støtter Fogh-organisation |url=https://olfi.dk/2025/05/28/kontroversielt-amerikansk-firma-stoetter-fogh-organisation/ |website=olfi.dk |access-date=17 July 2025 |language=da-DK |date=28 May 2025}}</ref>

Thiel has supported mostly conservative gay rights causes such as the [[American Foundation for Equal Rights]] and [[GOProud]].<ref>{{cite web|last=Weisberg|first=Jacob|url=http://www.slate.com/articles/news_and_politics/politics/2010/10/turn_on_start_up_drop_out.html|title=Hyper-libertarian Facebook billionaire Peter Thiel's appalling plan to pay students to quit college|website=Slate|date=16 October 2010|access-date=7 October 2011|archive-date=3 October 2011|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111003143221/http://www.slate.com/articles/news_and_politics/politics/2010/10/turn_on_start_up_drop_out.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He invited conservative columnist and friend [[Ann Coulter]] to Homocon 2010 as a guest speaker.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2010/10/10/fashion/10coulter.html?pagewanted=all |title=Outflanked on Right, Coulter Seeks New Image |work=The New York Times |date=8 October 2010 |access-date=25 December 2013 |archive-date=13 April 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140413012130/http://www.nytimes.com/2010/10/10/fashion/10coulter.html?pagewanted=all |url-status=live }}</ref> Coulter later dedicated her 2011 book, ''[[Demonic: How the Liberal Mob Is Endangering America]]'', to Thiel.<ref>{{cite book |url=http://www.librarything.com/work/11297673 |title=Demonic: How the Liberal Mob Is Endangering America |publisher=Library Thing |oclc=697261630 |access-date=25 December 2013 |archive-date=27 December 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131227021814/http://www.librarything.com/work/11297673 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="coulter280">{{cite book|last1=Coulter|first1=Ann|title=¡Adios, America! : The Left's Plan to Turn Our Country into a Third World Hell Hole|date=2015|publisher=Regnery Publishing|location=Washington, DC|isbn=978-1-62157-606-8|oclc=949987257|page=280|quote=Others who have helped with this book, mostly by reading chapters and voting on titles, but in other ways, as well, are: Bill Armistead, Jon Caldara, Peter Brimelow, Rodney Conover, Mallory and Thomas Danaher, David Friedman, James Fulford, Ron Gordon, Kevin Harrington, David Limbaugh, Jay Mann, Jim Moody, Dan Travers, Jon Tukel, Marshall Sella, Peter Thiel, Kelly Victory, and Younis Zubchevich.}}</ref> In 2012, Thiel donated $10,000 to Minnesotans United for All Families, in order to fight [[Minnesota Amendment 1]]<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.minnpost.com/data/2012/11/who-funding-marriage-amendment-fight |title=Who is funding the marriage amendment fight? |work=Minn Post |date=1 November 2012 |access-date=25 December 2013 |archive-date=26 December 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131226040639/http://www.minnpost.com/data/2012/11/who-funding-marriage-amendment-fight |url-status=live }}</ref> that proposed to ban marriage between same-sex couples there.

In 2009, it was reported that Thiel helped fund [[James O'Keefe]]'s "Taxpayers Clearing House" video—a satirical look at the [[Wall Street bailout]].<ref name="Thrasher">{{cite news |url=http://www.villagevoice.com/news/conservative-facebook-investor-funded-anti-acorn-videographer-6687024 |work=[[The Village Voice]] |title=The Money Trail – Conservative Facebook Investor Funded Anti-ACORN Videographer |author=Steven Thrasher |date=22 September 2009 |author-link=Steven Thrasher |access-date=25 January 2017 |archive-date=5 February 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170205105028/http://www.villagevoice.com/news/conservative-facebook-investor-funded-anti-acorn-videographer-6687024 |url-status=dead }}</ref> O'Keefe went on to produce the [[ACORN 2009 undercover videos controversy|ACORN undercover sting videos]]; Thiel denied involvement in the ACORN sting.<ref name="Thrasher" />

In July 2012, Thiel made a $1&nbsp;million donation to the [[Club for Growth]], a fiscally conservative [[501(c)(4) organization]], becoming the group's largest contributor.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://go.bloomberg.com/political-capital/2012-08-20/thiels-1-million-tops-donors-to-club-for-growth-super-pac/|title=Thiel's $1 Million Tops Donors to Club for Growth Super-PAC|publisher=[[Bloomberg L.P.|Bloomberg]]|author=Gregory Giroux|date=20 August 2012|access-date=16 October 2012|archive-date=30 March 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130330153457/http://go.bloomberg.com/political-capital/2012-08-20/thiels-1-million-tops-donors-to-club-for-growth-super-pac/|url-status=live}}</ref>
He is a major backer of the conservative [[Rockbridge Network]], which is now an international network with Asian branches.<ref>{{cite news |title=Chung Yong-jin becomes Asia president of U.S.-founded donor group Rockbridge |url=https://prod.biz.chosun.com/en/en-industry/2025/06/25/SJZKLZAVGZATVP4UPHQE64UNII/ |access-date=17 July 2025 |work=CHOSUNBIZ |date=25 June 2025 |language=en}}</ref>

In 2023, ''[[Business Insider]]'' reported that Thiel became an [[Federal Bureau of Investigation|FBI]] [[informant]] in 2021. ''Business Insider'' also noted the fact that politicians sponsored by Thiel, including Vance and Masters, had repeatedly attacked the FBI and its leadership in public.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Schwartz |first=Mattathias |date=October 19, 2023 |title=Exclusive: Tech billionaire Peter Thiel was an FBI informant |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/peter-thiel-fbi-informant-charles-johnson-johnathan-buma-chs-genius-2023-10 |access-date=2023-12-15 |website=[[Business Insider]] |language=en-US |archive-date=16 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231216022149/https://www.businessinsider.com/peter-thiel-fbi-informant-charles-johnson-johnathan-buma-chs-genius-2023-10 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Robertson |first=Adi |date=2023-10-19 |title=Peter Thiel was reportedly an FBI informant |url=https://www.theverge.com/2023/10/19/23923759/peter-thiel-fbi-informant-foreign-influence-report |access-date=2023-12-15 |website=[[The Verge]] |language=en |archive-date=15 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231215170912/https://www.theverge.com/2023/10/19/23923759/peter-thiel-fbi-informant-foreign-influence-report |url-status=live }}</ref> According to former FBI agent [[Jonathan Buma]], Peter Thiel, Elon Musk and [[David O. Sacks|David Sacks]] have been targets of Russian intelligence. Buma notes that Thiel cooperated with the FBI to identify the foreign espionage network.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Hano |first1=Johannes |last2=Dominik |first2=Rzepka |title=Ex-FBI-Mann: Musk war Ziel russischer Agenten |website=[[ZDF]] |date=May 12, 2025 |url=https://www.zdf.de/nachrichten/politik/trump-musk-putin-100.html |access-date=May 14, 2025 |archive-date=May 12, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250512183557/https://www.zdf.de/nachrichten/politik/trump-musk-putin-100.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Hano |first1=Johannes |last2=Rzepka |first2=Dominik |title=Ex-FBI-Mann: Musk war Ziel russischer Agenten |url=https://www.zdfheute.de/politik/trump-musk-putin-100.html |access-date=20 August 2025 |work=ZDFheute |date=12 May 2025 |language=de}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Kirchgaessner |first1=Stephanie |title=FBI whistleblower claims he tried to get to Musk to warn him he was being targeted by Russia |url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2025/may/22/fbi-whistleblower-musk-russia |access-date=20 August 2025 |work=The Guardian |date=22 May 2025}}</ref>

He visited president of Argentina and fellow libertarian [[Javier Milei]] three times in 2024. The ''Noticias de América Latina y el Caribe'' (''NODAL'') remarks that the cooperation between Thiel and Milei marks the political alignment between Argentina and Washington and Silicon Valley, also through organizations like [[Endeavor (non-profit)|Endeavor]]. According to ''NODAL'', the introduction of Argentina into Thiel's network is erasing traditional politics while promoting a tech-based order which increases efficiency but also puts sovereignty at stake.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Robins-Early |first1=Nick |title=Argentinian president to meet Silicon Valley CEOs in bid to court tech titans |url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/article/2024/may/28/javier-milei-tech-ceo-apple-google-meta |work=The Guardian |date=28 May 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Jouli |first1=Luciana |title=Argentina en la red de Peter Thiel: plataformas, datos y soberanía en juego |url=https://www.nodal.am/2025/08/argentina-en-la-red-de-peter-thiel-plataformas-datos-y-soberania-en-juego/ |access-date=2 September 2025 |work=NODAL |date=29 August 2025 |language=es}}</ref>

[[Matt Stoller]], research director of [[American Economic Liberties Project]], remarks that Thiel is a "really smart nihilist", and notes that his focus is entirely on power. Thiel's biographer Max Chafkin writes that this is a likely explanation for Thiel's activities.{{sfn|Chafkin|2021|p=377}}

In 2017, Thiel reportedly refused the offer to become chairman of the president's intelligence advisory board, despite Trump's urging.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Gray |first1=Rosie |title=Peter Thiel Turns Down a Senior Intelligence Role |url=https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2017/11/peter-thiel-doesnt-want-intelligence-advisory-post/547100/ |work=The Atlantic |date=30 November 2017 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Neidig |first1=Harper |title=White House offered Peter Thiel intel adviser post: report |url=https://thehill.com/policy/technology/351574-report-white-house-offered-peter-thiel-role-as-intel-adviser/ |work=The Hill |date=20 September 2017}}</ref> In the same year, there were reports that he considered becoming U.S. Ambassador to Germany or a bid for governorship of California. At the time, he said that he was not interested in a full-time job in politics.<ref name="cnbc.com">{{cite news |last1=Amaro |first1=Silvia |title=Trump could tap tech entrepreneur Peter Thiel for Germany job: Report |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2017/01/20/trump-could-tap-tech-entrepreneur-peter-thiel-for-germany-job-report.html |work=CNBC |date=20 January 2017 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Weinberger |first1=Matt |title=Peter Thiel denies report that he might be Trump's pick for ambassador to Germany |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/peter-thiel-donald-trump-ambassador-germany-2017-1 |work=Business Insider |date=20 January 2017}}</ref> In 2024, he said that he had gotten used to tech and a full-time job as a politician would lead to depression.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Timotija |first1=Filip |title=Thiel says he won't have 'full-time' role in second Trump administration |url=https://thehill.com/policy/technology/5038883-thiel-says-he-wont-have-full-time-role-in-second-trump-administration/ |work=The Hill |date=13 December 2024}}</ref><ref name="cnbc.com"/><ref>{{cite news |last1=Nash |first1=Charlie |title='I'd Be Depressed and Crazy': Peter Thiel Says He Won't Have a Role in Second Trump Administration |url=https://www.mediaite.com/media/tv/id-be-depressed-and-crazy-peter-thiel-says-he-wont-have-a-role-in-second-trump-administration/ |work=Mediaite |date=13 December 2024 |language=en}}</ref>

In December 2025, Thiel donated $3&nbsp;million to the lobbying group California Business Roundtable to oppose a proposed 5% wealth tax on billionaires in California.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Schleifer |first=Theodore |last2=Mac |first2=Ryan |date=2026-01-11 |title=Thiel Gives $3 Million to Group Seeking to Block California Wealth Tax |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/01/11/us/politics/peter-thiel-california-wealth-tax.html |access-date=2026-03-03 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

Some authors opine that he often combines economic and political activities.<ref name="IO17"/><ref name="rbb24"/><ref name="BraunLand">{{cite news |last1=Braun |first1=Frédéric |title=Die nackten Könige der Tech-Branche |url=https://land.lu/de/wirtschaft/nationale-wirtschaft/die-nackten-konige-der-tech-branche/#:~:text=So%20sieht%20Peter,der%20Massen%20zur%C3%BCckzugreifen. |work=Land |date=6 November 2025 |language=de-DE}}</ref> ''Intelligence Online'' notes that since the 2010s, he has gradually cornered the private satellite imagery market through multiple investments by his different funds (Y Combinator, Founders Fund, Mithril), then sold this essential service to governments in the U.S. and other countries as part of a global strategy.<ref name="IO17">{{cite news |title=UNITED STATES • Peter Thiel has big GEOINT 2.0 plans - 08/02/2017 |url=https://www.intelligenceonline.com/americas/2017/02/08/peter-thiel-has-big-geoint-20-plans,108210814-art |work=Intelligence Online |date=8 February 2017 |language=en}}</ref> Professor [[Adrian Daub]] says Thiel's investments are never merely commercial, and when he invests in Europe's arms industry, he aims for the ecosystem.<ref name="rbb24">{{cite news |title=Die nächste Wette von Peter Thiel |url=https://www.rbb24.de/wirtschaft/beitrag/2026/07/berlin-peter-thiel-wette-investor-drohnen-start-up-stark-defence.html |work=rbb24.de |date=16 July 2026 |language=de}}</ref> In Israel's case, ''[[Globes (newspaper)|Globes]]'' notes that the matter lies with the lack of capital and interest from Israel's side: Founders Fund and other American funds play an important role in financing Israel's prominent defense startups, while Israeli capital only accounts for 5% (The leaders of these Israeli companies, like Kela and Covenant, also come from the Thiel ecosystem).<ref>{{cite news |title=New fund to invest in young Israeli defense-tech cos |url=https://en.globes.co.il/en/article-new-fund-to-invest-in-young-israeli-defense-tech-cos-1001547158 |work=Globes |date=25 June 2026 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Germany’s missile search draws attention to secretive startup Covenant |url=https://www.calcalistech.com/ctechnews/article/b1s912rmfg |work=ctech |date=21 June 2026 |language=en}}</ref><ref name="ShulmanCalcalis"/> ''[[Calcalist]]'' writes that "the massive American funds want the entire stake."<ref name="ShulmanCalcalis">{{cite news |last1=Shulman |first1=Sophie |title=Kela: The Israeli startup rewriting how wars are fought |url=https://www.calcalistech.com/ctechnews/article/ftop7r3p8 |work=ctech |date=30 April 2025 |language=en}}</ref> Philosopher {{ill|Norman Ajari|fr}} claims that, as Thiel sees AI as representing centralization and the possibility of global economic control, while crypto will favor an individualized and decentralized world, he is "not investing in artificial intelligence to follow its inherent logic—namely, massive centralization and unrestricted access to data—but rather to subordinate it to his libertarian and authoritarian political ambitions".<ref name="BraunLand"/>

=== Support for political candidates ===
Thiel is a member of the [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican Party]].<ref name="DW">{{cite web |last=Schwab |first=Florian |date=18 July 2018 |title=Kopf der Woche: Peter Thiel |trans-title=Interview of the Week: Peter Thiel |url=https://weltwoche.ch/story/hypnotische-massenphaenomene/ |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180724001522/https://www.weltwoche.ch/ausgaben/2018-29/artikel/en-hypnotische-massenphanomene-die-weltwoche-ausgabe-29-2018.html |archive-date=24 July 2018 |access-date=23 July 2018 |work=[[Die Weltwoche]] |language=de}}</ref> He contributes to both [[Libertarian Party (United States)|Libertarian]] and Republican candidates and causes. In December 2007, Thiel endorsed [[Ron Paul]] for [[Ron Paul presidential campaign, 2008|President]] in the [[2008 United States presidential election]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Endorsements » Blog Archive » Peter Thiel |access-date=24 January 2008 |url=http://people.ronpaul2008.com/endorsements/2007/12/22/peter-thiel/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080123224151/http://people.ronpaul2008.com/endorsements/2007/12/22/peter-thiel/ |archive-date=23 January 2008}}</ref> After Paul failed to secure the Republican nomination, Thiel contributed to the [[John McCain]] [[John McCain 2008 presidential campaign|campaign]].<ref name="Political Campaign Contributions">Peter Thiel Political Campaign Contributions (CampaignMoney.com)
<br />{{*}} {{Cite news|title=Peter Thiel Political Campaign Contributions 2000 Election Cycle|url=http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=00|access-date=25 December 2013|archive-date=12 September 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130912130213/http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=00|url-status=live}}
<br />{{*}} {{Cite news|title=Peter Thiel Political Campaign Contributions 2002 Election Cycle|url=http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=02|access-date=25 December 2013|archive-date=12 September 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130912145425/http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=02|url-status=live}}
<br />{{*}} {{Cite news|title=Peter Thiel Political Campaign Contributions 2004 Election Cycle|url=http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=04|access-date=25 December 2013|archive-date=26 December 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131226065616/http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=04|url-status=live}}
<br />{{*}} {{Cite news|title=Peter Thiel Political Campaign Contributions 2006 Election Cycle|url=http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=06|access-date=25 December 2013|archive-date=26 December 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131226071023/http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=06|url-status=live}}
<br />{{*}} {{Cite news|title=Peter Thiel Political Campaign Contributions 2008 Election Cycle|url=http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=08|access-date=25 December 2013|archive-date=12 September 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130912122042/http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=08|url-status=live}}
<br />{{*}} {{Cite news|title=Peter Thiel Political Campaign Contributions 2010 Election Cycle|url=http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=10|access-date=25 December 2013|archive-date=12 September 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130912132751/http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=10|url-status=live}}
<br />{{*}} {{Cite news|title=Peter Thiel Political Campaign Contributions 2012 Election Cycle|url=http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=12|access-date=25 December 2013|archive-date=12 September 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130912130200/http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=12|url-status=live}}
<br />{{*}} {{Cite news|title=Peter Thiel Political Campaign Contributions 2014 Election Cycle|url=http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=14|access-date=25 December 2013|archive-date=10 February 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140210231435/http://www.campaignmoney.com/political/contributions/peter-thiel.asp?cycle=14|url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2010, Thiel supported Republican [[Meg Whitman]] in her unsuccessful bid for the [[California gubernatorial election, 2010|governorship of California]]. He contributed the maximum allowable $25,900 to the Whitman campaign.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Fost |first=Dan |title=Old (Pay)Pals: Peter Thiel backs Meg Whitman |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/danfost/2010/09/17/old-paypals-peter-thiel-backs-meg-whitman/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110624023240/http://blogs.forbes.com/danfost/2010/09/17/old-paypals-peter-thiel-backs-meg-whitman/ |access-date=2023-04-30 |website=Forbes |archive-date=24 June 2011 |language=en}}</ref>

In 2012, Thiel, along with Nosek and [[Scott Banister]], put their support behind the [[Endorse Liberty]] Super PAC. Collectively they gave $3.9&nbsp;million to Endorse Liberty, whose purpose was to promote [[Ron Paul]].<ref name="Reuters">{{Cite news|last=Selyukh|first=Alina|title=PayPal co-founders fund pro-Paul Super PAC|url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-usa-campaign-spending-paul-idUSTRE80U1OF20120131|access-date=31 January 2012|newspaper=Reuters|date=31 January 2012|archive-date=1 February 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120201034004/http://www.reuters.com/article/2012/01/31/us-usa-campaign-spending-paul-idUSTRE80U1OF20120131|url-status=live}}</ref> After Paul again failed to secure the nomination in the [[2012 United States presidential election]], Thiel contributed to the [[Mitt Romney]]/[[Paul Ryan]] [[2012 Mitt Romney presidential campaign|presidential ticket of 2012]].<ref name="Political Campaign Contributions" />

Thiel initially supported [[Carly Fiorina]]'s campaign during the 2016 GOP presidential primary elections.<ref name="ABC">{{Cite news|last=Kim|first=Susanna|title=Billionaire Paypal Co-Founder Peter Thiel on List of Trump Backers|url=https://abcnews.go.com/Business/billionaire-paypal-founder-peter-thiel-list-trump-backers/story?id=39006891|access-date=10 May 2016|newspaper=ABC News|date=10 May 2016|archive-date=11 May 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160511123833/http://abcnews.go.com/Business/billionaire-paypal-founder-peter-thiel-list-trump-backers/story?id=39006891|url-status=live}}</ref> After Fiorina dropped out, Thiel supported [[Donald Trump]] and became one of the California delegates for Trump's nomination. He was a headline speaker during the [[2016 Republican National Convention]], during which he announced that he was proud to be gay, Republican, and American, for which the assembled Republicans cheered.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Selyukh|first1=Alina|title='I Am Proud To Be Gay,' Tech Investor Peter Thiel Tells GOP Convention|url=https://www.npr.org/2016/07/21/486966882/i-am-proud-to-be-gay-tech-investor-peter-thiel-tells-gop-convention|website=NPR|date=21 July 2016|access-date=22 July 2016|archive-date=22 July 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160722171038/http://www.npr.org/2016/07/21/486966882/i-am-proud-to-be-gay-tech-investor-peter-thiel-tells-gop-convention|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Margolin |first=Emma |url=https://www.nbcnews.com/feature/nbc-out/openly-gay-libertarian-tech-entrepreneur-peter-thiel-speak-rnc-n614191 |title=Peter Thiel Makes History at RNC: 'I'm Proud to be Gay' |publisher=NBC News |date=2016 |access-date=22 July 2016 |archive-date=19 January 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190119005616/https://www.nbcnews.com/feature/nbc-out/openly-gay-libertarian-tech-entrepreneur-peter-thiel-speak-rnc-n614191 |url-status=live }}</ref> On 15 October 2016, Thiel announced a $1.25&nbsp;million donation in support of [[Donald Trump presidential campaign, 2016|Donald Trump's 2016 presidential campaign]].<ref>{{cite news|last1=Streitfeld|first1=David|title=Peter Thiel to Donate $1.25 Million in Support of Donald Trump|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/16/technology/peter-thiel-donald-j-trump.html|access-date=16 October 2016|work=The New York Times|date=15 October 2016|archive-date=16 October 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161016051617/http://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/16/technology/peter-thiel-donald-j-trump.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

Thiel stated to ''[[The New York Times]]'': "I didn't give him any money for a long time because I didn't think it mattered, and then the campaign asked me to."<ref name=":5">{{cite web|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2017/01/11/fashion/peter-thiel-donald-trump-silicon-valley-technology-gawker.html|title=Peter Thiel, Trump's Tech Pal, Explains Himself|first=Maureen|last=Dowd|website=The New York Times|date=11 January 2017|access-date=22 May 2017|archive-date=22 May 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170522210658/https://www.nytimes.com/2017/01/11/fashion/peter-thiel-donald-trump-silicon-valley-technology-gawker.html|url-status=live}}</ref> After Trump's victory, Thiel was named to the executive committee of the president-elect's [[First presidential transition of Donald Trump|transition team]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://fortune.com/2016/11/11/thiel-trump-transition-team/|title=Silicon Valley Investor Peter Thiel Will Join Trump's Transition Team|first=Kia|last=Kokalitcheva|website=Fortune|date=11 November 2016|access-date=22 May 2017|archive-date=28 May 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170528154406/http://fortune.com/2016/11/11/thiel-trump-transition-team/|url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2017, [[Gavin Newsom]] (then lieutenant governor of California), whose campaign and marijuana legalization effort Thiel had supported, noted that Thiel cared deeply about criminal justice reform and had done a lot of behind-the-scene good work on marriage equality, which he was also passionate about. Newsom remarked, though, that "None of us are jumping up and down that he's aligned himself with President Donald Trump."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Marinucci |first1=Carla |title=Newsom: It will get 'intriguing' if Thiel runs for governor |url=https://www.politico.com/states/california/story/2017/01/ca-gubernatorial-candidate-gavin-newsom-peter-thiel-is-the-least-of-democrats-2018-worries-108927 |work=Politico |date=23 January 2017 |language=en}}</ref>

By February 2022, Thiel was one of the largest donors to Republican candidates in the [[2022 United States elections|2022 election campaign]]. By November 2022 he had spent $32&nbsp;million. He supported 16 senatorial and congressional candidates. Two of said senatorial candidates ([[Blake Masters]] (who lost his race) and later U.S. Vice President [[JD Vance]]) were also tech investors who had previously worked for Thiel.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Schwartz |first1=Brian |title=Peter Thiel's picks Masters, Vance split key Senate races in Arizona, Ohio after billionaire spent $32 million on 2022 midterms |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2022/11/12/midterm-results-peter-thiel-picks-masters-vance-see-mixed-results-in-arizona-ohio.html |work=CNBC |date=12 November 2022 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|last1=Mac|first1=Ryan|last2=Lerer|first2=Lisa|date=14 February 2022|title=The Right's Would-Be Kingmaker|language=en-US|work=The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/02/14/technology/republican-trump-peter-thiel.html|access-date=14 February 2022|issn=0362-4331|archive-date=12 July 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220712190214/https://www.nytimes.com/2022/02/14/technology/republican-trump-peter-thiel.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2023, [[Barton Gellman]] of ''[[The Atlantic]]'' wrote in an article interviewing Thiel that Thiel "has lost interest in democracy" and that "he wouldn't be giving money to any politician, including Donald Trump, in the next presidential campaign". According to [[Reuters]] this occurred after he disagreed with the Republican party's focus on cultural issues.<ref name="Gellman1">{{cite web |last1=Gellman |first1=Barton |title=Peter Thiel Is Taking a Break From Democracy |url=https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2023/11/peter-thiel-2024-election-politics-investing-life-views/675946/ |website=The Atlantic |access-date=1 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260303183340/https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2023/11/peter-thiel-2024-election-politics-investing-life-views/675946/ |archive-date= 2026-03-03 |url-status=live |language=en |date=9 November 2023}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title=Exclusive: Peter Thiel, Republican megadonor, won't fund candidates in 2024, sources say |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/us/peter-thiel-republican-megadonor-wont-fund-candidates-2024-sources-2023-04-26/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241208183713/https://www.reuters.com/world/us/peter-thiel-republican-megadonor-wont-fund-candidates-2024-sources-2023-04-26/ |archive-date=8 December 2024 |access-date=2025-02-03 |work=Reuters |language=en-US |url-status=live }}</ref> In the same Atlantic interview, he stated that the first Trump administration failed even his initial low expectations.{{sfn|Gellman|2023}} In 2024, he described Trump as a clown whom [[Reid Hoffman]]'s lawsuit turned into a martyr.<ref>{{cite news |title=LinkedIn Founder Clarifies Quip Wishing He'd Made Trump a 'Martyr' |url=https://www.yahoo.com/news/linkedin-founder-clarifies-quip-wishing-192253883.html |access-date=6 August 2025 |work=Yahoo News |date=14 July 2024}}</ref> In 2025, when interviewed by [[Ross Douthat]], Thiel indicated that Trump and the populists were a disruptive factor that would prepare the stage for the process of true rebuilding (in 2023, he also opined that Trump's election would "slash regulations, crush the administrative state{{snd}}before the country could rebuild"). He stressed that the support of large parts of the Silicon Valley for Trump was not pro-Trump in nature. He stated that disruption did not equal progress, and even his thought of trying to having a conversation with Trump about it (in Trump's first term) later proved "a preposterous fantasy". But he was satisfied about the fact that in the second term, deregulation was happening, for example regarding nuclear energy.<ref name="Douthat Thiel Anti NYT">{{cite news|last1=Douthat |first1=Ross |title=Peter Thiel and the Antichrist|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/26/opinion/peter-thiel-antichrist-ross-douthat.html |website=[[The New York Times]] |access-date=6 August 2025 |date=26 June 2025 |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/mYJWO |archive-date=26 October 2025}}</ref>{{sfn|Gellman|2023}}

Thiel has his own political-action committee, Free Forever, which is committed to supporting political candidates who support stricter border control, restrictive immigration policy, funds for veterans, and anti-interventionist foreign policy, among other things.<ref>{{Cite web|title=About – Free Forever PAC|url=https://freeforeverpac.com/about/|access-date=3 July 2020|language=en-US|archive-date=3 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200703210646/https://freeforeverpac.com/about/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |author1=Rob Copeland |author2=Keach Hagey |author3=Tripp Mickle |date=2 July 2020|title=Tech Tycoon Peter Thiel Shies From Trump Re-Election Campaign|language=en-US|work=The Wall Street Journal|url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/tech-tycoon-peter-thiel-shies-from-trump-reelection-campaign-11593730590|access-date=3 July 2020|issn=0099-9660|archive-date=2 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200702232041/https://www.wsj.com/articles/tech-tycoon-peter-thiel-shies-from-trump-reelection-campaign-11593730590|url-status=live}}</ref> According to [[OpenSecrets]], the PAC was active only during the [[2020 United States elections|2020 election cycle]] and then only in support of Kansas attorney general [[Kris Kobach]]'s failed [[2020 United States Senate election in Kansas|U.S. Senate bid]]. The campaign by Kobach, who lost in the Republican primary, had received almost all of its contributions from Thiel himself.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Free Forever PAC Independent Expenditures |url=https://www.opensecrets.org/political-action-committees-pacs/free-forever-pac/C00721910/independent-expenditures/2020 |access-date=2025-02-03 |website=OpenSecrets |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=PAC Profile: Free Forever PAC |url=https://www.opensecrets.org/political-action-committees-pacs/free-forever-pac/C00721910/summary/2020 |access-date=2025-02-03 |website=OpenSecrets |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Free Forever PAC PAC Donors |url=https://www.opensecrets.org/political-action-committees-pacs/free-forever-pac/C00721910/donors/2020 |access-date=2025-02-03 |website=OpenSecrets |language=en}}</ref>

In 2025, Brendan Glavin, director of insights for [[OpenSecrets]], remarked that Thiel's political donations have "an ideological agenda that's not strictly motivated by financial or business concerns [...] His views are libertarian generally, and he wants to elect people who are like minded."<ref>{{cite news |last1=Osborne |first1=James |title=Killer robots, China and Peter Thiel: Ted Cruz's campaign to keep government out of AI |url=https://www.houstonchronicle.com/politics/article/ted-cruz-ai-china-thiel-20801410.php |date=11 August 2025}}</ref>

== Philanthropy ==
{{further|Thiel Foundation}}

Thiel carries out most of his philanthropic activities through the Thiel Foundation.<ref>{{cite web|title=Thiel Foundation website|url=http://www.thielfoundation.org|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090821184531/http://www.thielfoundation.org/|archive-date=21 August 2009|access-date=28 September 2009}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|title=Peter Thiel|language=en-US|work=Inside Philanthropy|url=https://www.insidephilanthropy.com/guide-to-individual-donors/peter-thiel.html|url-status=live|access-date=26 April 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180427045023/https://www.insidephilanthropy.com/guide-to-individual-donors/peter-thiel.html|archive-date=27 April 2018}}</ref>

He has advocated for billionaires to withdraw from [[The Giving Pledge]], a commitment to donate at least 50% of one's wealth, promoting instead a form of philanthropy focused on businesses and innovation.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Schleifer |first=Theodore |date=2026-03-15 |title=The Billionaire Backlash Against a Philanthropic Dream |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/15/business/the-billionaire-backlash-against-a-philanthropic-dream.html |access-date=2026-03-29 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2026-03-23 |title=Warren Buffett Defends the Giving Pledge as 'Billionaire Backlash' Grows. What's Behind the Revolt? |url=https://www.entrepreneur.com/business-news/warren-buffett-defends-giving-pledge-against-billionaire-backlash |access-date=2026-03-29 |work=Entrepreneur}}</ref>

=== Research ===
==== Artificial intelligence ====
In 2006, Thiel provided $100,000 of matching funds to back the Singularity Challenge donation drive of the Singularity Institute for Artificial Intelligence (now known as the [[Machine Intelligence Research Institute]]), a nonprofit organization that promotes the development of [[friendly artificial intelligence]].<ref name="singular">{{Cite web |date=2013-06-17 |title=A Singular Sort of Cult |url=https://www.huffingtonpost.co.uk/nicholas-tufnell/a-singular-sort-of-cult_b_3446089.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181001031149/https://www.huffingtonpost.co.uk/nicholas-tufnell/a-singular-sort-of-cult_b_3446089.html |access-date=2023-04-30 |website=HuffPost UK |archive-date=1 October 2018 |language=en}}</ref> He provided half of the $400,000 matching funds for the 2007 donation drive, and as of 2013 the Thiel Foundation had donated over $1 million to the institute.<ref name="singular" /> Additionally, he has spoken at multiple [[Singularity Summit]]s.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Gardiner |first=Bryan |title=Peter Thiel Explains How to Invest in the Singularity |language=en-US |magazine=Wired |url=https://www.wired.com/2007/09/peter-thiel-exp/ |url-status=live |access-date=2023-04-30 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200416103202/https://www.wired.com/2007/09/peter-thiel-exp/ |issn=1059-1028|archive-date=16 April 2020 }}</ref><ref name="hplus">{{Cite web |date=2009-10-04 |title=Singularity Summit – Peter Thiel On His Single Greatest Fear |url=https://hplusmagazine.com/2009/10/04/singularity-summit-peter-thiel-his-single-greatest-fear/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140630222852/http://hplusmagazine.com/2009/10/04/singularity-summit-peter-thiel-his-single-greatest-fear/ |access-date=2023-04-30 |website=h+ Media |archive-date=30 June 2014 |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Back to the Future: Peter Thiel on Technology and Investment Strategy at the NYC Singularity Summit|website=[[Business Insider]]|url=https://www.businessinsider.com/back-to-the-future-peter-thiel-on-technology-and-investment-strategy-at-the-nyc-singularity-summit-2011-10|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181017123532/https://www.businessinsider.com/back-to-the-future-peter-thiel-on-technology-and-investment-strategy-at-the-nyc-singularity-summit-2011-10|archive-date=17 October 2018|access-date=17 October 2018}}</ref> At the 2009 Singularity Summit, he said his greatest concern is the [[technological singularity]] not arriving soon enough.<ref name=hplus/>

In December 2015, [[OpenAI]], a nonprofit company aimed at the safe development of [[artificial general intelligence]], announced that Thiel was one of its financial backers.<ref>{{cite magazine|last1=Priestly|first1=Theo|date=11 December 2015|title=Elon Musk And Peter Thiel Launch OpenAI, A Non-Profit Artificial Intelligence Research Company|url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/theopriestley/2015/12/11/elon-musk-and-peter-thiel-launch-openai-a-non-profit-artificial-intelligence-research-company/|url-status=live|magazine=[[Forbes]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151214024722/http://www.forbes.com/sites/theopriestley/2015/12/11/elon-musk-and-peter-thiel-launch-openai-a-non-profit-artificial-intelligence-research-company/|archive-date=14 December 2015|access-date=11 December 2015}}</ref>

==== Life extension ====
In September 2006, Thiel announced that he would donate $3.5 million to foster [[anti-aging]] research through the non-profit [[Methuselah Mouse Prize]] foundation.<ref>{{cite web|title=The Mprize-PayPal Founder pledges $3.5 Million to antiaging research|url=http://www.mprize.org/index.php?pagename=newsdetaildisplay&ID=0107|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080521050850/http://www.mprize.org/index.php?pagename=newsdetaildisplay&ID=0107|archive-date=21 May 2008|access-date=24 January 2008}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last=Davidson|first=Keay|date=18 September 2006|title=Entrepreneur backs research on anti-aging|url=https://www.sfgate.com/health/article/BAY-AREA-Entrepreneur-backs-research-on-2469507.php|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181231215640/https://www.sfgate.com/health/article/BAY-AREA-Entrepreneur-backs-research-on-2469507.php|archive-date=31 December 2018|access-date=6 October 2018|website=SFGate}}</ref> He gave the following reasons for his pledge: "Rapid advances in biological science foretell of a treasure trove of discoveries this century, including dramatically improved health and longevity for all. I'm backing [[Aubrey de Grey|Dr. [Aubrey] de Grey]], because I believe that his revolutionary approach to aging research will accelerate this process, allowing many people alive today to enjoy radically longer and healthier lives for themselves and their loved ones." As of February 2017, he had donated over $7 million to the foundation.<ref>{{Cite magazine |date=2017-02-16 |title=How Silicon Valley Is Trying to Hack Its Way Into a Longer Life |url=https://time.com/4672962/silicon-valley-longer-life/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180129224516/http://time.com/4672962/silicon-valley-longer-life/ |access-date=2023-04-30 |magazine=Time |archive-date=29 January 2018 |language=en}}</ref>

When asked "What is the biggest achievement that you haven't achieved yet?" by the moderator of a discussion panel at the Venture Alpha West 2014 conference, Thiel said he wants to make progress in anti-aging research.<ref name="Reilly2014">{{cite news|last1=Reilly|first1=Richard Byrne|date=8 October 2014|title=Billionaire Peter Thiel embarks on anti-aging crusade|work=Venture Beat|url=https://venturebeat.com/2014/10/08/billionaire-peter-thiel-may-want-to-live-forever/|url-status=live|access-date=22 October 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141020234402/http://venturebeat.com/2014/10/08/billionaire-peter-thiel-may-want-to-live-forever/|archive-date=20 October 2014}}</ref> Thiel also said that he is registered to be [[cryopreservation|cryonically preserved]], meaning that he would be subject to low-temperature preservation in case of his legal death in hopes that he might be successfully revived by future medical technology, and is signed up with the [[Alcor Life Extension Foundation]].<ref name=Brown2014/>

Thiel has expressed interest in the science of [[parabiosis]], including [[young blood transfusion]] for potential health benefits.{{sfn|Gellman|2023}}<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Kosoff |first1=Maya |title=Peter Thiel Wants to Inject Himself With Young People's Blood |url=https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2016/08/peter-thiel-wants-to-inject-himself-with-young-peoples-blood |access-date=28 June 2025 |magazine=Vanity Fair |date=1 August 2016}}</ref> He said in a 2016 ''Inc.'' interview that the technology had been found to work on mice before being strangely dropped after the 1950s.<ref name="inc2016">{{cite magazine |last=Bercovici |first=Jeff |url=https://www.inc.com/jeff-bercovici/peter-thiel-young-blood.html |title=Peter Thiel Is Very, Very Interested in Young People's Blood |magazine=[[Inc. (magazine)|Inc.]] |date=August 1, 2016 |access-date=July 2, 2025}}</ref> The same ''Inc.'' article reported that the Thiel Capital medical director Jason Camm had contacted the transfusion startup Ambrosia,<ref name="inc2016"/> but its founder Jesse Karmazin told ''TechCrunch'' in a 2017 article that they had never been contacted by Thiel or Thiel Capital.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Buhr |first1=Sarah |title=No, Peter Thiel is not harvesting the blood of the young |url=https://techcrunch.com/2017/06/14/no-peter-thiel-is-not-harvesting-the-blood-of-the-young/ |access-date=28 June 2025 |work=TechCrunch |date=14 June 2017}}</ref> In a 2022 ''[[Jacobin (magazine)|Jacobin]]'' article, Ben Burgis characterizes the blood transfusion story as part of a deliberate attempt by Thiel to portray himself as an "evil genius".<ref>{{cite news |title=Peter Thiel Wants You to Think He's an Evil Genius. He's Just a Rich Guy. |url=https://jacobin.com/2022/07/peter-thiel-superrich-wealth-inequality-political-influence |access-date=28 June 2025 |work=jacobin.com}}</ref>

==== Seasteading ====
On 15 April 2008, Thiel pledged $500,000 to the newly created non-profit [[Seasteading Institute]],<ref>{{Cite news |last=Gelles |first=David |date=2017-11-13 |title=Floating Cities, No Longer Science Fiction, Begin to Take Shape |language=en-US |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2017/11/13/business/dealbook/seasteading-floating-cities.html |url-status=live |access-date=2023-04-30 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180301225508/https://www.nytimes.com/2017/11/13/business/dealbook/seasteading-floating-cities.html |issn=0362-4331|archive-date=1 March 2018 }}</ref> directed by [[Patri Friedman]], whose mission is "to establish permanent, autonomous ocean communities to enable experimentation and innovation with diverse social, political, and legal systems."<ref name="tsi20080415">{{cite web|title=Introducing The Seasteading Institute|url=http://seasteading.org/stay-in-touch/press-releases/introducing-the-seasteading-institute|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080807032117/http://www.seasteading.org/stay-in-touch/press-releases/introducing-the-seasteading-institute|archive-date=7 August 2008|access-date=16 April 2008}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last=Hodgkinson|first=Tom|date=6 October 2016|title=How Utopia shaped the world|work=BBC News|url=http://www.bbc.com/culture/story/20160920-how-utopia-shaped-the-world|url-status=live|access-date=6 October 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181007080712/http://www.bbc.com/culture/story/20160920-how-utopia-shaped-the-world|archive-date=7 October 2018}}</ref> At one of the institute's conferences, he described [[seasteading]] as "one of the few technological frontiers that has the promise to create a new space for human freedom."<ref>[https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2018-07-30/floating-island-project-pushes-on-without-peter-thiel-s-support Floating Island Project Pushes On, Without Peter Thiel's Support] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181017123633/https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2018-07-30/floating-island-project-pushes-on-without-peter-thiel-s-support|date=17 October 2018}} Bloomberg</ref> In 2011, Thiel gave $1.25 million to the Seasteading Institute,<ref>[http://www.chicagomag.com/Chicago-Magazine/The-312/August-2011/Milton-Friedmans-Grandson-to-Built-Floating-Libertarian-Nation/ Milton Friedman's Grandson to Build Floating Libertarian Nation] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181001031133/http://www.chicagomag.com/Chicago-Magazine/The-312/August-2011/Milton-Friedmans-Grandson-to-Built-Floating-Libertarian-Nation/|date=1 October 2018}} ''Chicago''</ref><ref>[https://www.inverse.com/article/25166-peter-thiel-strangest-projects Peter Thiel's Strangest Projects] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181001031358/https://www.inverse.com/article/25166-peter-thiel-strangest-projects|date=1 October 2018}} ''Inverse''</ref> but resigned from its board the same year.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Robinson |first=Melia |title=A Silicon Valley billionaire's dream of a floating libertarian utopia may have finally been killed |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/libertarian-peter-thiel-utopia-seasteading-institute-2018-3 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181017082216/https://www.businessinsider.com/libertarian-peter-thiel-utopia-seasteading-institute-2018-3 |access-date=2023-04-30 |website=Business Insider |archive-date=17 October 2018 |language=en-US}}</ref> In a 2017 interview with ''The New York Times'', Thiel said seasteads are "not quite feasible from an engineering perspective" and "still very far in the future".<ref name=":5" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Robinson |first=Melia |title=Tech billionaire Peter Thiel no longer thinks his dream of a floating libertarian utopia is realistic |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/peter-thiel-seastead-dream-floating-city-2017-1 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181001031352/https://www.businessinsider.com/peter-thiel-seastead-dream-floating-city-2017-1 |access-date=2023-04-30 |website=Business Insider |archive-date=1 October 2018 |language=en-US}}</ref>

=== Thiel Fellowship ===
{{Main|Thiel Fellowship}}

On 29 September 2010, Thiel created the controversial Thiel Fellowship, which annually offers a total of $100,000 (raised to $200,000 since 2025<ref>{{cite news |title=Thiel Foundation Announces 2025 Class of Thiel Fellows |url=https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250522267532/en/Thiel-Foundation-Announces-2025-Class-of-Thiel-Fellows |access-date=5 August 2025 |date=22 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250702033948/https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20250522267532/en/Thiel-Foundation-Announces-2025-Class-of-Thiel-Fellows |archive-date=2 July 2025 |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref>) over two years to 20 people under the age of 23 in order to spur them to drop out of college and create their own ventures.<ref>{{cite web|date=29 September 2010|title=The Thiel Fellowship|url=http://20under20.org|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180116004456/http://20under20.org/|archive-date=16 January 2018|access-date=16 October 2010|publisher=20 Under 20}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=30 September 2010|title=Peter Thiel Launches Fellowship Program|url=http://www.silicontap.com/peter_thiel_launches_fellowship_program/s-0031372.html|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20101029212423/http://www.silicontap.com/peter_thiel_launches_fellowship_program/s-0031372.html|archive-date=29 October 2010|access-date=30 September 2010|website=silicontap.com}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last=Kolodny|first=Lora|date=18 December 2013|title=Why a Nonprofit Backs Dropping Out of School|url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/no-headline-available-1387303362|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181007073731/https://www.wsj.com/articles/no-headline-available-1387303362|archive-date=7 October 2018|access-date=6 October 2018|website=The Wall Street Journal}}</ref> According to Thiel, many young people choose college simply because they're unsure of what else to do with their lives.<ref name=Brown2014/> He envisions a future system that offers different paths for different people, and believes that change in the university system will require external pressure ("Reformation") before any internal willingness to adapt can arise.<ref>{{cite web |title=Transcript of Peter Thiel on Conversations with Bill Kristol |url=https://conversationswithbillkristol.org/transcript/peter-thiel-transcript/ |website=Conversations with Bill Kristol |access-date=17 October 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Hurley |first1=Bevan |title=Peter Thiel gave these dropouts $100k each. What happened next? |url=https://www.thetimes.com/world/article/peter-thiel-dropouts-100k-each-us-university-paypal-vxfvqvpzq |work=www.thetimes.com |date=12 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240609185642/https://www.thetimes.com/world/article/peter-thiel-dropouts-100k-each-us-university-paypal-vxfvqvpzq |archive-date=2024-06-09 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Young |first1=Jeffrey R. |title=How a Billionaire's Fellowship Spread Skepticism About College's Value - EdSurge News |url=https://www.edsurge.com/news/2023-12-12-how-a-billionaire-s-fellowship-spread-skepticism-about-college-s-value |work=EdSurge |date=12 December 2023 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite episode |credits=Farley Center for Entrepreneurship and Innovation|date= 8 December 2014 |title= e@nu Speaker Series with Peter Thiel: Developing The Developed World|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XJgwIgOLoyM |location=Farley Center for Entrepreneurship and Innovation |series =e@nu speaker series|publisher= Northwestern University's McCormick School of Engineering|minutes= |time=30:00}}</ref>

=== Breakout Labs ===
In November 2011, the Thiel Foundation announced the creation of [[Breakout Labs]], a grant-making program intended "to fill the funding gap that exists for innovative research outside the confines of an academic institution, large corporation, or government."<ref>{{cite web|title=About Us|url=https://www.breakoutlabs.org/about-us.html|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131114103546/http://www.breakoutlabs.org/about-us.html|archive-date=14 November 2013|access-date=5 December 2013|website=Breakout Labs}}</ref><ref name="naturebl">{{Cite web |date=2012-04-26 |title=Nature News Blog: PayPal co-founder's Breakout Labs issues first grants : Nature News Blog |url=http://blogs.nature.com/news/2012/04/paypal-co-founders-breakout-labs-issues-first-grants.html |access-date=2023-05-01 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120426072643/http://blogs.nature.com/news/2012/04/paypal-co-founders-breakout-labs-issues-first-grants.html |archive-date=26 April 2012 }}</ref> It offers grants of up to $350,000 to science-focused start-ups, "with no strings attached".<ref name="forbesbl">{{Cite web |last=Mac |first=Ryan |title=Peter Thiel's Breakout Labs Turns More Science Projects Into Businesses |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/ryanmac/2013/04/17/peter-thiels-breakout-labs-turns-more-science-projects-into-businesses/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181017082923/https://www.forbes.com/sites/ryanmac/2013/04/17/peter-thiels-breakout-labs-turns-more-science-projects-into-businesses/#44b6c1f21d2f |access-date=2023-05-01 |website=Forbes |archive-date=17 October 2018 |language=en}}</ref><ref name="techcrunchbl">{{Cite web |last=Loizos |first=Connie |date=2017-09-14 |title=Breakout Ventures, spun out of Peter Thiel's Breakout Labs, has closed its debut fund with $60M |url=https://techcrunch.com/2017/09/14/breakout-ventures-spun-out-of-peter-thiels-breakout-labs-has-closed-its-debut-fund-with-60m/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181017082214/https://techcrunch.com/2017/09/14/breakout-ventures-spun-out-of-peter-thiels-breakout-labs-has-closed-its-debut-fund-with-60m/ |access-date=2023-05-01 |website=TechCrunch |archive-date=17 October 2018 |language=en-US}}</ref> In April 2012, Breakout Labs announced its first set of grantees.<ref name=naturebl/><ref>{{cite web|date=17 April 2012|title=Breakout Labs press release on first batch of grantees|url=https://www.breakoutlabs.org/news-events/news-event-item/article/breakout-labs-announces-first-grantees.html|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120616114659/https://www.breakoutlabs.org/news-events/news-event-item/article/breakout-labs-announces-first-grantees.html|archive-date=16 June 2012|access-date=8 June 2012}}</ref> In total, 12 startups received funding, for a total of $4.5 million in grants.<ref name=forbesbl/> One of the first ventures to receive funding from Breakout Labs was [[3Scan]], a [[Automated tissue image analysis|tissue imaging]] platform.<ref name=techcrunchbl/>

Breakout Ventures is a privately held venture capital firm founded in 2016 out of [[Breakout Labs]] to invest in science.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Levy |first1=Ari |title=Peter Thiel's foundation spawned a science-based venture fund that just raised $46.5 million |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2017/05/17/breakout-ventures-spun-out-of-thiel-foundation-raises-46-point-5-million.html |work=CNBC |date=17 May 2017 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Loizos |first=Connie |date=2017-09-14 |title=Breakout Ventures, spun out of Peter Thiel's Breakout Labs, has closed its debut fund with $60M |url=https://techcrunch.com/2017/09/14/breakout-ventures-spun-out-of-peter-thiels-breakout-labs-has-closed-its-debut-fund-with-60m/
 |access-date=2024-11-23 |website=TechCrunch |language=en-US}}</ref> Based in [[San Francisco, California]], it invests in early-stage companies in technology, biology, and chemistry focused on human health and sustainability.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Homepage |url=https://www.breakout.vc/
 |access-date=2025-10-30 |website=www.breakout.vc
}}</ref> The program focuses on biotech with a mix of hardware. Its partners include Founders Fund, Formation 8, OATV, Lux Capital, Khosla Ventures among others.<ref>{{cite news |title=Breakout Labs looking for robots that can change the world |url=https://robohub.org/breakout-labs-looking-for-robots/ |access-date=27 July 2025 |work=Robohub}}</ref> Some of its recent investments include Noetik (cancer treatment),<ref>{{cite news |last1=Dorbian |first1=Iris |title=Biotech firm Noetik fetches $40m Series A |url=https://www.venturecapitaljournal.com/biotech-firm-noetik-fetches-40m-series-a/ |access-date=27 July 2025 |work=Venture Capital Journal |date=29 August 2024}}</ref> Phantom Neuro (neurotechnology).<ref>{{cite news |last1=Lunden |first1=Ingrid |title=Phantom Neuro grabs $19M to help amputees put their phantom limbs to use |url=https://techcrunch.com/2025/04/15/phantom-neuro-grabs-19m-to-help-amputees-gain-control-of-their-phantom-limbs/ |work=TechCrunch |date=15 April 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Bluemner |first1=Paul |title=EnPlusOne Biosciences Raises $10M Financing |url=https://www.citybiz.co/article/663821/enplusone-biosciences-raises-10m-financing/ |access-date=27 July 2025 |work=citybiz |date=21 February 2025}}</ref> Corpernic Catalysts (catalysts for ammonia production),<ref>{{cite news |title=Copernic Catalysts raises $8m to scale sustainable ammonia catalyst |url=https://www.qcintel.com/ammonia/article/copernic-catalysts-raises-8m-to-scale-sustainable-ammonia-catalyst-32115.html |work=www.qcintel.com |date=15 November 2024 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Neuhauser |first1=Alan |title=Breakout Ventures leads Copernic Catalysts' $8M raise |url=https://www.axios.com/pro/climate-deals/2024/11/12/copernic-catalysts-jacob-ammonia-breakout-ventures |work=Axios |date=12 November 2024 |language=en}}</ref> EnPlusOne Biosciences (RNA therapeutics),<ref>{{cite news |last1=Chavez |first1=Eli |title=George Church spinout adds $10M for RNA synthesis platform |url=https://www.bizjournals.com/boston/inno/stories/news/2025/02/24/george-church-spinout-10-million-rna-synthesis.html |work=Boston Business Journal |date=24 February 2025}}</ref> Passkey Therapeutics (synergistic multifunctional therapeutics),<ref>{{cite news |last1=Garfinkle |first1=Allie |title=Exclusive: Ramp, valued at $7.65 billion, launches its own app store |url=https://fortune.com/2024/10/24/ramp-valued-at-7-65-billion-launches-app-store/ |work=Fortune |date=24 October 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260221091523/https://fortune.com/2024/10/24/ramp-valued-at-7-65-billion-launches-app-store/ |archive-date= 2026-02-21|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=PhD |first1=Jonathan D. Grinstein |title=Passkey Therapeutics Launches with Platform to Design Multifunctional Drugs |url=https://www.insideprecisionmedicine.com/topics/informatics/passkey-therapeutics-launches-with-platform-to-design-multifunctional-drugs/ |work=Inside Precision Medicine |date=22 October 2024}}</ref> Cytovale (medical diagnostics).<ref>{{cite news |last1=Hale |first1=Conor |title=Cytovale gains momentum with $100M for its sepsis screening test |url=https://www.fiercebiotech.com/medtech/cytovale-gains-momentum-100m-its-sepsis-screening-test |work=www.fiercebiotech.com |date=10 October 2024 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Loizos |first1=Connie |title=Breakout Ventures has a new, $112.5 million fund, backed by Tony Fadell, Chris Sacca and others |url=https://techcrunch.com/2021/12/09/breakout-ventures-has-a-new-112-5-million-fund-backed-by-tony-fadell-chris-sacca-and-others/ |work=TechCrunch |date=10 December 2021}}</ref>

=== Other causes ===

In 2011, Thiel made a [[New Zealand dollar|NZ$]]1 million donation to an appeal fund for the casualties of the [[2011 Christchurch earthquake|Christchurch earthquake]].<ref>{{cite web|last1=van Beynen|first1=Martin|last2=Kuprienko|first2=Dasha|date=25 January 2017|title=Billionaire Donald Trump supporter Peter Thiel sending more of his mates our way|url=http://www.stuff.co.nz/business/88746174/billionaire-donald-trump-supporter-peter-thiel-sending-more-of-his-mates-our-way|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170908234201/http://www.stuff.co.nz/business/88746174/billionaire-donald-trump-supporter-peter-thiel-sending-more-of-his-mates-our-way|archive-date=8 September 2017|access-date=30 June 2017|website=Stuff.co.nz}}</ref>

In Girard's honour, he has established the ''Imitatio'' project (part of the philanthropic Thiel Foundation), which aims to "supports research, education, and publications building on Rene Girard's mimetic theory."<ref>{{cite web |title=The Thiel Foundation |url=https://www.influencewatch.org/non-profit/the-thiel-foundation/ |website=InfluenceWatch}}</ref>

== Personal life ==
Thiel resided in [[San Francisco]], California, until 2018, when he moved to Los Angeles. He had criticized San Francisco for being "intolerant of conservatives, insular and overpriced".<ref>{{cite news |last1=Chapman |first1=Lizette |title=Peter Thiel is ditching San Francisco for Los Angeles |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2018-02-15/peter-thiel-is-said-to-be-ditching-san-francisco-for-los-angeles |date=15 February 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260102054351/https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2018-02-15/peter-thiel-is-said-to-be-ditching-san-francisco-for-los-angeles |archive-date= 2026-01-02}}</ref> Both Thiel Capital and Thiel Foundation followed him to Los Angeles, but the Founders Fund remains in San Francisco. Mithril's headquarters moved to Austin.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Calvey |first1=Mark |title=Peter Thiel's VC firm moves from S.F. to Austin for its food trucks, tolerance and lower costs |url=https://www.bizjournals.com/sanfrancisco/news/2018/09/26/peter-thiel-venture-capital-austin-yelp-taxes.html |access-date=13 August 2025 |work=San Francisco Business Journal |date=26 September 2018}}</ref><ref name=insider-2023 /> Thiel owns homes all over the world, with his main residence in [[Miami]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Bubola |first1=Emma |last2=Mac |first2=Ryan |author2-link=Ryan Mac |title=In Argentina, U.S. Tech Billionaire Peter Thiel Finds An Escape |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/28/world/americas/peter-thiel-argentina.html |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=May 28, 2026 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Shead |first1=Sam |title=Peter Thiel's luxury New Zealand lodge should be rejected, council planner says |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2022/05/03/peter-thiels-new-zealand-lodge-should-be-rejected-council-planner-says.html |work=CNBC |date=3 May 2022 |language=en}}</ref>

Thiel married his long-time partner, [[Matt Danzeisen]], in [[Vienna]], Austria, on Thiel's 50th birthday (October 2017), when he was reported to have proposed to Danzeisen.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Karnak |first1=Chris |title=PayPal-Gründer Peter Thiel: Hochzeitsantrag in Wien? {{!}} GGG.at |url=https://www.ggg.at/2017/10/30/paypal-gruender-peter-thiel-hochzeitsantrag-in-wien/ |date=30 October 2017 |language=de}}</ref>{{sfn|Gellman|2023}}<ref>{{cite web|url =https://www.axios.com/peter-thiel-got-married-over-the-weekend-1513306233-29abae6d-fa70-4939-b15e-0d0042986700.html|title =Peter Thiel got married over the weekend|website =Axios|first1 =Dan|last1 =Primack|first2 =Mike|last2 =Allen|date =16 October 2017|access-date =1 September 2018|archive-date =2 September 2018|archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20180902012028/https://www.axios.com/peter-thiel-got-married-over-the-weekend-1513306233-29abae6d-fa70-4939-b15e-0d0042986700.html|url-status =live}}</ref> Danzeisen started his career as an investment banker at [[BofA Securities|Bank of America Securities]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Matt Danzeisen {{!}} Career, Personal Life, and Public Profile |url=https://markmagazine.co.uk/personality/matt-danzeisen-career-personal-life-and-public-profile/ |website=markmagazine.co.uk |access-date=5 June 2025 |date=30 April 2025}}</ref> By 2007, when the couple were dating, Danzeisen was vice president of [[BlackRock]]. By 2021, he was chairman of Bridgetown 1 and Bridgetown 2, sponsored by Thiel Capital and [[Richard Li]]'s [[Pacific Century Group]]. [[Sam Altman]] also sat on the board.<ref>{{cite book |last1=Chafkin |first1=Max |title=The Contrarian: Peter Thiel and Silicon Valley's Pursuit of Power |date=21 September 2021 |publisher=Bloomsbury Publishing |isbn=978-1-5266-4554-8 |page=127 |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=5bc_EAAAQBAJ&pg=PA127 |access-date=5 June 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Bridgetown 3 Holdings Limited |url=https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1844028/000121390021012944/filename1.htm |website=www.sec.gov |access-date=5 June 2025}}</ref> Danzeisen also participates in other Thiel enterprises related to the family of [[Li Ka-shing]] (father of Richard Li), such as the Malta-based EUM.<ref>{{cite news |title=Peter Thiel, Major U.S. Political Donor, Is Said to Pursue Maltese Citizenship (Published 2022) |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/15/technology/peter-thiel-malta-citizenship.html |access-date=5 June 2025 |date=15 October 2022 |language=en |last1=Mac |first1=Ryan |last2=Scheck |first2=Justin }}</ref> In 2017 Danzeisen was working as head of private investments at Thiel Capital, with a primary focus on North America and Asia.<ref name=express>{{cite news |url=http://expressdigest.com/billionaire-peter-thiel-gets-married-to-matt-danzeisen/|title=Billionaire Peter Thiel gets married to Matt Danzeisen|publisher=Express Digest|date=18 October 2017|access-date=12 September 2018|archive-date=13 September 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180913032826/http://expressdigest.com/billionaire-peter-thiel-gets-married-to-matt-danzeisen/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Peter Thiel-backed Bridgetown Spac seals $550m US IPO |url=https://www.globalcapital.com/article/28msrwf3i64sdcdc9f8eg/asia/peter-thiel-backed-bridgetown-spac-seals-550m-us-ipo |access-date=5 June 2025 |work=GlobalCapital |date=16 October 2020 |language=en}}</ref> Thiel and Danzeisen have two young daughters, aged five and three as of June 2024, born through a surrogate.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Adeaga |first1=Favour |title=Meet Matt Danzeisen: The husband of PayPal co-founder Peter Thiel - Briefly.co.za |url=https://briefly.co.za/96153-meet-matt-danzeisen-husband-paypal-founder-peter-thiel.html |access-date=6 June 2025 |work=briefly.co.za |date=14 June 2022 |language=en}}</ref>{{unreliable source?|date=April 2026|reason=See current RSN discusssion}}<ref>{{cite news |title=Tech billionaire Peter Thiel says he only allows his children 1.5 hours of screen time a week |url=https://www.yahoo.com/news/tech-billionaire-peter-thiel-says-110403774.html |access-date=6 June 2025 |work=Yahoo News |date=30 June 2024}}</ref> [[Adrian Wooldridge]] from ''Bloomberg'' reported in August 2025 that Thiel had four children.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Wooldridge |first1=Adrian |title=Today's Eugenics Is Much More Dangerous |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2025-08-22/eugenics-is-more-dangerous-with-musk-and-noor-siddiqui |date=22 August 2025}}</ref> In 2023, in an interview with the ''Atlantic'', Thiel noted that Danzeisen had tried to dissuade him from donating money to Republicans.{{sfn|Gellman|2023}}

Thiel was in a long-term relationship with model [[Jeff Thomas (model)|Jeff Thomas]] until Thomas's suicide in March 2023. Media coverage of Thomas's death drew widespread attention, partly because of Thomas's involvement with Democratic researchers led by [[David Brock]] and Jack Bury.<ref name="intercept1">{{Cite web |last=Grim |first=Ryan |date=2023-03-23 |title=The Death of Peter Thiel's "Kept" Romantic Partner Is Being Investigated as a Suicide |url=https://theintercept.com/2023/03/23/peter-thiel-jeff-thomas/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260227091252/https://theintercept.com/2023/03/23/peter-thiel-jeff-thomas/ |archive-date= 2026-02-27|access-date=2023-03-24 |website=The Intercept |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Newsham |first1=Jack |title=Peter Thiel's reported romantic partner was found dead in Miami. Police are investigating as possible suicide. |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/male-model-kept-peter-thiel-relationship-dead-possible-suicide-2023-3 |access-date=4 August 2025 |work=Business Insider |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260217000627/https://www.businessinsider.com/male-model-kept-peter-thiel-relationship-dead-possible-suicide-2023-3 |archive-date= 2026-02-17}}</ref> Puck.news wrote that the anti-Thiel campaign exposed an undercurrent in modern politics in which there is an increasing tendency towards using people's private problems to achieve political goals.<ref name="puck">{{cite news |title=Thiel, Brock & a Gutter Oppo Campaign for Our Times |url=https://puck.news/newsletter_content/thiel-brock-a-gutter-oppo-campaign-for-our-times-2/ |access-date=4 August 2025 |work=Puck |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230711235022/https://puck.news/newsletter_content/thiel-brock-a-gutter-oppo-campaign-for-our-times-2/ |archive-date=11 July 2023}}</ref>

In 2026, Thiel visited South America, combining "a family vacation" with other activities. He met with leaders like [[Javier Milei]], [[Santiago Peña]], [[José Antonio Kast]].<ref name="Telematica">{{cite news |last1=Telemática |first1=Convergencia |title=Peter Thiel visitó tres países de América Latina para ofrecer su software y predicar su filosofía |url=https://www.convergencia.com/convergencia-telematica/peter-thiel-visito-tres-paises-de-america-latina-para-ofrecer-su-software-y-predicar-su-filosofia-8208/ |work=www.convergencia.com |date=5 May 2026 |language=es}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=President Santiago Peña and Peter Thiel Explore Investment and Innovation Opportunities in Paraguay |url=https://latingulf.ae/2026/05/14/president-santiago-pena-and-peter-thiel-explore-investment-and-innovation-opportunities-in-paraguay/ |work=Latin&gulf |date=14 May 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Citizen |first1=The |title=Milei Locks Down Casa Rosada as He Hosts Palantir's Peter Thiel Amid Media Blackout |url=https://www.elciudadano.com/en/milei-locks-down-casa-rosada-as-he-hosts-palantirs-peter-thiel-amid-media-blackout/04/24/ |work=El Ciudadano |date=24 April 2026 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Donoso |first1=Nicole |title=Supuesta reunión secreta entre Kast y Peter Thiel lleva a Winter a oficiar a Presidencia por seguridad digital |url=https://eldesconcierto.cl/actualidad/supuesta-reunion-secreta-kast-y-peter-thiel-lleva-winter-oficiar-presidencia-seguridad-digital-n5458732 |work=eldesconcierto.cl |date=12 May 2026 |language=es-CL}}</ref> He also visited Venezuela and Ecuador.<ref name="Telematica"/><ref>{{cite news |last1=Vaz |first1=Ricardo |title=[UPDATED] Venezuela's Rodríguez Hosts World Bank Delegation as Trump Allies Eye Investment Opportunities |url=https://venezuelanalysis.com/news/venezuelas-rodriguez-hosts-world-bank-delegation-as-trump-allies-eye-investment-opportunities/ |work=Venezuelanalysis |date=19 May 2026}}</ref> He intended to stay in Argentina for two months, buying properties in Argentina and Uruguay.<ref>{{cite news |title=Millonaria inversión en Maldonado: empresario tecnológico desembolsó US$ 10 millones |url=https://www.montevideo.com.uy/Noticias/Millonaria-inversion-en-Maldonado-empresario-tecnologico-desembolso-US-10-millones-uc962613 |work=Montevideo Portal |date=19 May 2026 |language=es-UY}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Löhning |first1=Ute |title=Peter Thiel en expedición de saqueo por Chile y Argentina |url=https://interferencia.cl/articulos/peter-thiel-en-expedicion-de-saqueo-por-chile-y-argentina |work=Interferencia |date=29 May 2026 |language=es}}</ref>

=== Chess ===
Thiel began playing [[chess]] at the age of six<ref name=fortune>{{cite web|url=http://fortune.com/2014/09/04/peter-thiels-contrarian-strategy/|first=Roger|last=Parloff|title=Peter Thiel disagrees with you|website=[[Fortune (magazine)|Fortune]]|date=4 September 2014|access-date=18 November 2016|archive-date=5 December 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161205192725/http://fortune.com/2014/09/04/peter-thiels-contrarian-strategy/|url-status=live}}</ref> and was at one time one of the top junior players in the United States.<ref name=":6" /><ref name=NYTchess>{{cite web|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/nyregion/magnus-carlsen-defends-title-in-world-chess-championship.html|title=Magnus Carlsen Overwhelms Challenger in Tiebreakers to Win World Chess Championship|first=John|last=Leland|website=The New York Times|date=30 November 2016|access-date=30 June 2017|archive-date=7 August 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170807162316/https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/30/nyregion/magnus-carlsen-defends-title-in-world-chess-championship.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://en.chessbase.com/post/busine-insider-24-executives-who-are-exceptional-at-che|title=24 executives who are exceptional at chess|publisher=ChessBase|date=7 February 2012|access-date=30 June 2017|archive-date=21 July 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170721034655/http://en.chessbase.com/post/busine-insider-24-executives-who-are-exceptional-at-che|url-status=live}}</ref> He holds the title of [[Chess title#Life Master|Life Master]],<ref name=USCF>{{cite web |url=http://www.uschess.org/datapage/ratings_graph.php?memid=12056150 |title=USCF Ratings History Graph for 12056150: Peter Thiel |publisher=[[United States Chess Federation]] |author=<!--Not stated--> |access-date=24 November 2016 |archive-date=5 March 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170305042533/http://www.uschess.org/datapage/ratings_graph.php?memid=12056150 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url =https://www.businessinsider.com/steigman-challenges-thiel-to-million-dollar-chess-game-2012-7|title =Entrepreneur Challenges Peter Thiel To Million Dollar Chess Game|website =Business Insider|first =Vivian|last =Giang|date =16 July 2012|access-date =21 September 2018|archive-date =22 September 2018|archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20180922024802/https://www.businessinsider.com/steigman-challenges-thiel-to-million-dollar-chess-game-2012-7|url-status =live}}</ref> but he has not competed since 2003.<ref name=DW/> On 30 November 2016, Thiel made the ceremonial first move in the first tiebreak game of the [[World Chess Championship 2016]] between [[Sergey Karjakin]] and [[Magnus Carlsen]].<ref name=NYTchess/><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.businessinsider.com/photos-peter-thiel-made-first-move-at-fide-world-chess-championship-2016-12|title=Peter Thiel made a rare public appearance at a chess tournament|first=Kif|last=Leswing|website=Business Insider|date=1 December 2016|access-date=30 June 2017|archive-date=18 August 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170818185917/http://uk.businessinsider.com/photos-peter-thiel-made-first-move-at-fide-world-chess-championship-2016-12|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url =https://www.fide.com/component/content/article/1-fide-news/9901-fwccm2016.html|title =Magnus Carlsen retained the title|author =Staff writer(s)|publisher =FIDE|date =30 November 2016|access-date =21 September 2018|archive-date =5 January 2019|archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20190105151204/http://www.fide.com/component/content/article/1-fide-news/9901-fwccm2016.html|url-status =live}}</ref> He said that he stopped trying to become better at chess once he reached a certain level, because he believed excessive chess could become an "alternate reality" requiring "massive tradeoffs with success in other domains of life".<ref>{{cite news |last1=Pariser |first1=Eli |title=The Filter Bubble: How the New Personalized Web Is Changing What We Read and How We Think |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=wcalrOI1YbQC&pg=PT112 |publisher=Penguin |date=12 May 2011 |isbn=978-1-101-51512-9 |language=en}}</ref>

=== Media appearances ===
Thiel is an occasional commentator on [[CNBC]], having appeared on both ''[[Closing Bell]]'' with [[Kelly Evans]], and ''[[Squawk Box]]'' with [[Becky Quick]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cnbc.com/id/15840232?video=955505429&play=1|title=News Headlines|publisher=[[CNBC]]|date=26 February 2009|access-date=16 October 2010|archive-date=27 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201027160943/https://www.cnbc.com/video/2008/12/08/hedge-funds-losing-streak.html?play=1|url-status=dead}}</ref> He has been interviewed twice by [[Charlie Rose]] on [[PBS]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.charlierose.com/guest/view/926|title=Peter Thiel|publisher=Charlie Rose|access-date=16 October 2010|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20101012044655/http://www.charlierose.com/guest/view/926|archive-date=12 October 2010}}</ref> He has also contributed articles to ''[[The Wall Street Journal]]'', ''[[First Things]]'', ''[[Forbes]]'', and ''[[Policy Review]]'', a journal formerly published by the [[Hoover Institution]], on whose board he sits.

In ''[[The Social Network]]'', Thiel was portrayed by [[Wallace Langham]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.nationalreview.com/article/257531/back-future-peter-thiel-interview|title=Back to the Future with Peter Thiel|first=Matthew|last=Shaffer|website=National Review|date=20 January 2011|access-date=22 May 2017|archive-date=2 March 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150302165534/http://www.nationalreview.com/article/257531/back-future-peter-thiel-interview|url-status=live}}</ref> He described the film as "wrong on many levels".<ref>{{cite news|url=https://techcrunch.com/2010/11/19/peter-thiel-saverin/|title=Peter Thiel: Facebook Co-Founder Eduardo Saverin Did A Poor Job, Got Rich Anyway|first=Robin|last=Wauters|work=TechCrunch|date=19 November 2010|access-date=22 May 2017|archive-date=8 July 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170708001324/https://techcrunch.com/2010/11/19/peter-thiel-saverin/|url-status=live}}</ref> His distaste for the portrayal led to the establishment of the [[Thiel Fellowship]] on a whim.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Cucci |first1=Dorothy |title=Inside the disastrous early days of the Thiel Fellowship and the depression, mental health issues, and drug abuse that followed |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/peter-thiel-fellowship-inside-disastrous-early-days-contrarian-max-chafkin-2021-9 |access-date=4 August 2025 |work=Business Insider |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260213081509/https://www.businessinsider.com/peter-thiel-fellowship-inside-disastrous-early-days-contrarian-max-chafkin-2021-9 |archive-date= 2026-02-13}}</ref>

Thiel was the inspiration for the [[List of Silicon Valley characters|Peter Gregory]] character on HBO's ''[[Silicon Valley (TV series)|Silicon Valley]]''.<ref>{{cite web |author=Bort |first=Julie |date=28 April 2014 |title=A Guide To The Best Inside Jokes On HBO's Hit Comedy 'Silicon Valley' |url=http://www.businessinsider.com/a-guide-to-hbos-silicon-valley-jokes-2014-4#ixzz30OLeYqJ8 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140430111947/http://www.businessinsider.com/a-guide-to-hbos-silicon-valley-jokes-2014-4#ixzz30OLeYqJ8 |archive-date=30 April 2014 |access-date=30 April 2014 |website=[[Business Insider]]}}</ref> Thiel said of Gregory, "I liked him [...] I think eccentric is always better than evil".<ref name="dowd20170111">{{Cite news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2017/01/11/fashion/peter-thiel-confirm-or-deny.html |title=Confirm or Deny: Peter Thiel |last=Dowd |first=Maureen |date=11 January 2017 |newspaper=The New York Times |author-link=Maureen Dowd |access-date=12 January 2017 |archive-date=12 January 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170112112127/https://www.nytimes.com/2017/01/11/fashion/peter-thiel-confirm-or-deny.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

[[Jonas Lüscher]] stated in an interview with ''[[Basellandschaftliche Zeitung]]'' that he based the character Tobias Erkner in his novel ''Kraft'' ("Force") on Thiel.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.basellandschaftlichezeitung.ch/leben/leben/trend-autor-jonas-luescher-die-reichen-werden-unsterblich-und-der-grosse-rest-ueberfluessig-131231659|title=Trend-Autor Jonas Lüscher: 'Die Reichen werden unsterblich und der grosse Rest überflüssig'|first=Raffael|last=Schuppisser|website=Basellandschaftliche Zeitung|language=de|date=16 April 2017|access-date=22 May 2017|archive-date=24 May 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170524065447/https://www.basellandschaftlichezeitung.ch/leben/leben/trend-autor-jonas-luescher-die-reichen-werden-unsterblich-und-der-grosse-rest-ueberfluessig-131231659|url-status=live}}</ref>

After he hired former Austrian chancellor [[Sebastian Kurz]] (following scandals that led to Kurz's resignation) for Thiel Capital in 2022, [[Jan Böhmermann]] of the [[ZDF]] wrote and performed the satirical song ''Right time to Thiel'' that portrayed Thiel as a [[James Bond]] villain.<ref>{{cite news |title="Germany's Next Topmodel": Hat Böhmermann eine Kandidatin eingeschleust? |url=https://www.leadersnet.de/news/56152,germanys-next-topmodel-hat-boehmermann-eine-kandidatin.html |access-date=4 August 2025 |work=www.leadersnet.de |language=de-DE}}</ref>

=== New Zealand citizenship ===
Thiel was a [[German citizen]] by birth and became an [[American citizen]] by naturalization.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Drange |first=Matt |title=Peter Thiel Obtained New Zealand Citizenship Possibly Because Of 'Exceptional Circumstances' |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/ryanmac/2017/01/25/peter-thiel-obtained-new-zealand-citizenship-possibly-because-of-exceptional-circumstances/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180308043604/https://www.forbes.com/sites/ryanmac/2017/01/25/peter-thiel-obtained-new-zealand-citizenship-possibly-because-of-exceptional-circumstances/#637cda313bd9 |access-date=2023-05-01 |website=Forbes |archive-date=8 March 2018 |language=en}}</ref> He received [[New Zealand citizenship]] in a private ceremony at the New Zealand consulate in [[Santa Monica, California]], in August 2011; his citizenship status was not made public until 2017.<ref name="nz2011">{{cite news |last1=Nippert |first1=Matt |date=1 February 2017 |title=Revealed: How Peter Thiel got New Zealand citizenship |url=https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/news/article.cfm?c_id=3&objectid=11790034 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200416095744/https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/news/article.cfm?c_id=3&objectid=11790034 |archive-date=16 April 2020 |access-date=10 May 2020 |work=New Zealand Herald}}</ref><ref name="cnbc">{{Cite web |last=Novet |first=Jordan |title=Peter Thiel got New Zealand citizenship after spending 12 days there in five years |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2017/06/29/new-zealand-releases-peter-thiel-citizenship-details.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180308042849/https://www.cnbc.com/2017/06/29/new-zealand-releases-peter-thiel-citizenship-details.html |access-date=2023-05-01 |website=CNBC |date=29 June 2017 |archive-date=8 March 2018 |language=en}}</ref><ref name="NYT">{{cite news|last1=Streitfeld|first1=David|last2=Williams|first2=Jacqueline|date=1 February 2017|title=New Zealand Is 'the Future,' Peter Thiel Said in His Push for Citizenship|work=The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/01/business/peter-thiel-new-zealand-citizenship.html|url-status=live|access-date=10 May 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200518005202/https://www.nytimes.com/2017/02/01/business/peter-thiel-new-zealand-citizenship.html|archive-date=18 May 2020}}</ref> Thiel had visited the country on four occasions prior to his application for citizenship,<ref name="econ">{{cite news|date=4 February 2017|title=How Peter Thiel Became a New Zealander|url=https://www.economist.com/news/asia/21716086-and-why-it-has-caused-fuss-how-peter-thiel-became-new-zealander|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171203223334/https://www.economist.com/news/asia/21716086-and-why-it-has-caused-fuss-how-peter-thiel-became-new-zealander|archive-date=3 December 2017|access-date=8 September 2017|newspaper=[[The Economist]]}}</ref> staying a total of 12 days; the typical residency requirement is 1,350 days in five years.<ref name="nzherald2017">{{cite news|last1=Nippert|first1=Matt|date=28 June 2017|title=Controversial billionaire Peter Thiel made a Kiwi after two-week holiday|work=New Zealand Herald|url=https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/news/article.cfm?c_id=3&objectid=11883554|url-status=live|access-date=10 May 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200615233021/https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/news/article.cfm?c_id=3&objectid=11883554|archive-date=15 June 2020 }}</ref> When he applied, Thiel stated he had no intention of living in New Zealand, which is a criterion for citizenship.<ref name="intercept">{{Cite web|last=Biddle|first=Sam|date=2 February 2017|title=Billionaire Trump Adviser Peter Thiel Bought His New Zealand Citizenship, Documents Show|url=https://theintercept.com/2017/02/01/billionaire-trump-adviser-peter-thiel-bought-his-new-zealand-citizenship-documents-show/|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200416103255/https://theintercept.com/2017/02/01/billionaire-trump-adviser-peter-thiel-bought-his-new-zealand-citizenship-documents-show/|archive-date=16 April 2020|access-date=3 February 2017|work=[[The Intercept]]}}</ref> Then-Minister of Internal Affairs [[Nathan Guy]] waived those normal requirements, under an "exceptional circumstances" clause of the [[New Zealand nationality law|Citizenship Act]].<ref name="nz2011" /><ref name="econ" /><ref name="intercept" />

Thiel's application cited his contribution to the economy—he had founded a venture capital fund in Auckland before applying, and had invested $7 million in two local companies—as well as a $1 million donation to the [[2011 Christchurch earthquake]] appeal fund.<ref name="econ" /> [[Rod Drury]], founder of [[Xero (software)|Xero]], also provided a formal reference for Thiel's application.<ref name="nz2011" /> Thiel's case was cited by critics as an example of how New Zealand passports can be bought,<ref name="econ" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mac |first=Ryan |date=February 1, 2017 |title=The Many Contradictions Of Peter Thiel's New Zealand Citizenship |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/ryanmac/2017/02/01/the-many-contradictions-of-peter-thiels-new-zealand-citizenship/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180307214716/https://www.forbes.com/sites/ryanmac/2017/02/01/the-many-contradictions-of-peter-thiels-new-zealand-citizenship/#7f0b3d531317 |archive-date=7 March 2018 |access-date=2023-05-01 |website=Forbes |language=en}}</ref> something the New Zealand government denied.<ref name="econ" /> At the time that his citizenship was revealed, ''[[The New Zealand Herald]]'' came out with the report that the [[New Zealand Defence Force]], the [[New Zealand Security Intelligence Service|Security Intelligence Service]], and the [[Government Communications and Security Bureau]] have long-standing links with Thiel's Palantir.<ref name="nzherald2017"/>

In 2015, Thiel purchased a {{convert|193|hectare|0|adj=on}} estate near [[Wānaka]], which fit the classification of "sensitive land" and required foreign buyers to obtain permission from New Zealand's [[Overseas Investment Office]]. Thiel did not require permission, as he was a citizen.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Nippert|first1=Matt|date=25 January 2017|title=Facebook billionaire Peter Thiel a Kiwi citizen, owns Wanaka estate|work=New Zealand Herald|url=http://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/news/article.cfm?c_id=3&objectid=11787741|url-status=live|access-date=10 May 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200514120438/https://www.nzherald.co.nz/business/news/article.cfm?c_id=3&objectid=11787741|archive-date=14 May 2020}}</ref>

=== Awards and honors ===
* In 2006, Thiel won the Herman Lay Award for Entrepreneurship.<ref>{{cite web|title=The Association of Private Enterprise Education|access-date=24 January 2008|url=http://www.apee.org/award-lay.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20081006060543/http://www.apee.org/award-lay.html|archive-date=6 October 2008|url-status=dead}}</ref>
* In 2007, he was honored as a Young Global leader by the [[World Economic Forum]] as one of the 250 most distinguished leaders age 40 and under.<ref>{{cite web|title=List of Active Young Global Leaders|work=The Forum of Active Young Global Leaders|publisher=[[World Economic Forum]]|date=26 January 2010|url=http://www.weforum.org/docs/YGL/YGL2010_Community.pdf|access-date=28 June 2010}}</ref>
* On 7 November 2009, Thiel was awarded an honorary degree from [[Guatemala]]n [[Universidad Francisco Marroquin]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.ufm.edu/cms/es/honorary-doctoral-degrees |title=Honorary Doctoral Degrees at Universidad Francisco Marroquín |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110501185429/https://www.ufm.edu/cms/es/honorary-doctoral-degrees |archive-date=1 May 2011 }}</ref>
* In 2012, [[Students For Liberty]], an organization dedicated to spreading [[Libertarianism|libertarian]] ideals on college campuses, awarded Thiel its "Alumnus of the Year" award.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://studentsforliberty.org/upcoming-events/peter-thiel-at-isflc12-you-are-the-entrepreneur-of-your-life/|title=Peter Thiel at No. ISFLC12: 'You are the Entrepreneur of Your Life'|date=27 February 2012|access-date=11 June 2012|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120603161754/http://studentsforliberty.org/upcoming-events/peter-thiel-at-isflc12-you-are-the-entrepreneur-of-your-life/|archive-date=3 June 2012}}</ref>
* In 2018, [[German-American Heritage Foundation of the USA|German-American Heritage Foundation and Museum (GAHMUSA)]] honoured Thiel as Distinguished German-American of the Year.<ref name="GAHF"/>
* In 2021, the ''[[Frankfurter Allgemeine Zeitung]]'' (''FAZ'') gave him the Frank Schirrmacher prize, which typically honors intellectuals and artists for "outstanding achievements in understanding our current events." The awarding caused some controversies. The Frank Schirrmacher Foundation stated that, "By awarding Thiel the prize, his comprehensive work in analyzing the opportunities and risks of technological progress will be honored [...] disregarding prohibitions on thinking, he provides intellectual impulses and thus enriches the current socio-political discussions in a wide variety of fields."<ref>{{cite news |title=A cultural prize for billionaire Peter Thiel – DW – 10/07/2021 |url=https://www.dw.com/en/a-cultural-prize-for-tech-billionaire-peter-thiel/a-58875559 |access-date=6 August 2025 |work=dw.com |language=en}}</ref>
*In July 2026, German media conglomerate [[Axel Springer SE|Axel Springer]] announced that the [[Axel Springer Award]] 2026 will be given to Thiel, claiming that Thiel has brought about the emergence of entirely new markets and industries, and that he has helped defend democracies and has been "attacked and vilified".<ref>{{cite web |title=Peter Thiel to Receive the 2026 Axel Springer Award |url=https://www.axelspringer.com/en/ax-press-release/peter-thiel-to-receive-the-2026-axel-springer-award |website=www.axelspringer.com |access-date=25 July 2026}}</ref> The decision generates controversy, with ''[[Der Spiegel]]'' writing that Axel Springer presents just one half of the story.<ref>{{cite news |title=Peter Thiel mit Axel-Springer-Award 2026 geehrt |url=https://www.spiegel.de/wirtschaft/springer-konzern-ehrt-peter-thiel-mit-axel-springer-award-2026-a-4074675d-9a14-42fa-841d-1a53ee351b86 |work=Der Spiegel |date=17 July 2026 |language=de}}</ref> ''[[Süddeutsche Zeitung]]'' opines that Thiel's companies provide states what they need to function, but the German right's embracing of Thiel as a figure of hope has implications for democracy, noting that CSU politician [[Peter Gauweiler]] has called on the government to make Thiel federal minister for artificial intelligence and technological sovereignty.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Bovermann |first1=Philipp |title=Konservative Hoffnungsfigur: Peter Thiel erhält Axel Springer Award |url=https://www.sueddeutsche.de/medien/axel-springer-award-peter-thiel-preistraeger-konservativ-li.3517563 |work=Süddeutsche.de |date=17 July 2026 |language=de}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=WELT |first1=Peter Gauweiler |title=Herr Bundeskanzler, holen Sie sich Peter Thiel! - WELT |url=https://www.welt.de/debatte/plus6a1d4e7aae59523b137e3cb5/herr-bundeskanzler-holen-sie-sich-peter-thiel.html |work=DIE WELT |date=4 June 2026 |language=de}}</ref>

== Works ==
=== ''The Diversity Myth'' ===
In 1995, the [[Independent Institute]] published ''The Diversity Myth: Multiculturalism and the Politics of Intolerance at Stanford'', which Thiel co-authored along with fellow tech entrepreneur [[David O. Sacks]], and with a foreword by the late [[Emory University]] historian [[Elizabeth Fox-Genovese]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.independent.org/store/book.asp?id=38|title=The Diversity Myth: Multiculturalism and Political Intolerance on Campus|work=The Independent Institute|access-date=7 June 2015|archive-date=15 April 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150415063331/http://www.independent.org/store/book.asp?id=38|url-status=live}}</ref> The book is critical of [[political correctness]] and [[multiculturalism]] in higher education and alleges that it has diluted academic rigor. The authors also argue that, "You don't have diversity when you gather people who look different but talk and think alike."<ref>{{cite web |last1=Thiel |first1=Peter |last2=Sacks |first2=David |title=The diversity myth {{!}} The New Criterion |url=https://newcriterion.com/article/the-diversity-myth/ |date=24 May 2023 |access-date=22 September 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260124140500/https://newcriterion.com/article/the-diversity-myth/ |archive-date= 2026-01-24}}</ref>{{refn|group=N|''The Diversity Myth'': "If you stress "diversity", it means that diversity is not real, a fiction. There's no real multiculturalism; it's monocultural. The agenda is not non-Western; it's anti-Western. At Stanford, for instance, multicultural initiatives were funded by slashing the budgets of the university's foreign-language departments. You don't have diversity when you gather people who look different but talk and think alike."{{sfn|Thiel|Sacks|2023}}}}

Thiel and Sacks's writings drew criticism from then-Stanford Provost [[Condoleezza Rice]] and then-Stanford President [[Gerhard Casper]] in describing Thiel and Sacks's view of Stanford as "a cartoon, not a description of our freshman curriculum",<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.sfgate.com/news/article/Stanford-President-Condemns-Opinion-Piece-3022703.php|title=Stanford President Condemns Opinion Piece / Former students ridiculed school in Wall Street Journal|author1=Bill Workman|author2=Chronicle Peninsula Bureau|date=11 October 1995|work=SFGate|access-date=29 May 2016|archive-date=31 May 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160531145859/http://www.sfgate.com/news/article/Stanford-President-Condemns-Opinion-Piece-3022703.php|url-status=live}}</ref> and their commentary as "demagoguery, pure and simple".<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.paloaltoonline.com/weekly/morgue/cover/1995_Nov_29.4COVER29.html|title=Taking aim at Stanford|access-date=29 May 2016|archive-date=4 March 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160304061106/http://www.paloaltoonline.com/weekly/morgue/cover/1995_Nov_29.4COVER29.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2016, Thiel apologized for two statements involving the rape crisis movement and date rape that he made in the book.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bort |first=Julie |title=VC Peter Thiel and Zenefits CEO David Sacks apologize for writing a book that downplayed rape |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/peter-thiel-and-david-sacks-apologize-rape-comments-book-2016-10 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161026000319/http://www.businessinsider.com/peter-thiel-and-david-sacks-apologize-rape-comments-book-2016-10?r=UK&IR=T |date=October 25, 2016 |access-date=May 1, 2023 |website=[[Business Insider]] |archive-date=October 26, 2016 |language=en-US}}</ref>

=== ''Zero to One'' ===
In spring 2012, Thiel taught the class CS 183: Startup at Stanford University.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/ryanmac/2012/06/07/ten-lessons-from-peter-thiels-class-on-startups/ |title=Ten Lessons from Peter Thiel's Class On Startups |work=Forbes |first=Ryan |last=Mac |date=7 June 2012 |access-date=8 September 2017 |archive-date=14 January 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170114050110/http://www.forbes.com/sites/ryanmac/2012/06/07/ten-lessons-from-peter-thiels-class-on-startups/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Notes for the course, taken by student [[Blake Masters]], led to a book titled ''[[Zero to One]]: Notes on Startups, or How to Build the Future'' by Thiel and Masters, which was released in September 2014.<ref>{{cite web|url = http://www.zerotoonebook.com|title = Zero to One|access-date = 13 September 2014|archive-date = 3 June 2019|archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20190603095457/http://zerotoonebook.com/|url-status = live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url = http://blakemasters.com/peter-thiels-cs183-startup|title = Notes Essays – Peter Thiel's CS183: Startup – Stanford, Spring 2012|last = Masters|first = Blake|access-date = 13 September 2014|archive-date = 20 December 2013|archive-url = https://wayback.archive-it.org/all/20131220173612/http://blakemasters.com/peter-thiels-cs183-startup|url-status = live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://techcrunch.com/2014/09/08/peter-thiel-tweets/|title=Peter Thiel Tweets|first=Sarah|last=Buhr|work=TechCrunch|date=8 September 2014|access-date=22 May 2017|archive-date=26 February 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190226072202/https://techcrunch.com/2014/09/08/peter-thiel-tweets/|url-status=live}}</ref>

[[Derek Thompson (journalist)|Derek Thompson]], writing for ''[[The Atlantic]]'', stated ''Zero to One'' "might be the best business book I've read". He described it as a "self-help book for entrepreneurs, bursting with bromides" but also as a "lucid and profound articulation of capitalism and success in the 21st century economy."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/business/archive/2014/09/peter-thiel-zero-to-one-review/380738|title=Peter Thiel's Zero to One Might Be the Best Business Book I've Read|first=Derek|last=Thompson|website=The Atlantic|date=24 September 2014|access-date=22 May 2017|archive-date=21 May 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170521110054/https://www.theatlantic.com/business/archive/2014/09/peter-thiel-zero-to-one-review/380738/|url-status=live}}</ref>

==="The Straussian Moment"===
"The Straussian Moment" is an essay written by Thiel in 2004, sometimes considered to be a fundamental text in his political thinking and was the subject of a 2019 interview at the [[Hoover Institution]]. The essay draws on several thinkers and political theorists and argues that the [[September 11 attacks]] upset "the entire political and military framework of the nineteenth and twentieth centuries", and therefore "a reexamination of the foundations of modern politics" was needed.<ref name=":4" />

=== Others ===
One of Thiel's favorite books is ''[[The Sovereign Individual]]'', which was a little-known work before he helped to popularize it.{{sfn|Chafkin|2021|p=175}} He wrote the preface for the reprinted edition.<ref>{{cite book |last1=Gatehouse |first1=Gabriel |title=The Coming Storm: Shortlisted for the Orwell Prize for Political Writing - A Journey into the Heart of the Conspiracy Machine |date=5 September 2024 |publisher=Random House |isbn=978-1-4735-3343-1 |page=217 |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=o8TnEAAAQBAJ&pg=PT217 |language=en}}</ref>

Thiel also has a chapter giving advice in [[Tim Ferriss]] [[self-help]] book ''[[Tools of Titans|Tools of Titans: The Tactics, Routines, and Habits of Billionaires, Icons, and World-Class Performers]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bugbee |first=Stella |date=2017-06-30 |title=I Hate This Book About Lifehacks, But I Can't Stop Reading It |url=https://www.thecut.com/2017/06/review-tools-of-titans-by-tim-ferriss.html |access-date=2026-01-23 |website=The Cut |language=en}}</ref>

